const GRAM2 = [{"lv":4,"k":"b1_le12","form":"V + 了 + 數量 + O（了1：selesai）／ 句子 + 了（了2：keadaan baru）","icon":"check","name":["了1 vs 了2: selesai vs keadaan berubah","了1 vs 了2: completion vs change of state","了1 vs 了2: natapos vs nagbagong sitwasyon"],"gloss":["了 setelah verba (了1) menandai aksi yang sudah selesai, biasanya dengan objek berjumlah: 吃了兩個便當. 了 di akhir kalimat (了2) menandai situasi baru atau perubahan: 下雨了 (sekarang jadi hujan), 不喝咖啡了 (sekarang sudah tidak minum lagi). 了 bukan penanda 'masa lalu'.","了 after the verb (了1) marks a completed action, usually with a quantified object: 吃了兩個便當. 了 at the end of the sentence (了2) marks a new situation or change: 下雨了 (it's raining now), 不喝咖啡了 (I don't drink coffee anymore). 了 is not a past-tense marker.","Ang 了 pagkatapos ng pandiwa (了1) ay nagsasabing tapos na ang kilos, kadalasan may bilang ang object. Ang 了 sa dulo ng pangungusap (了2) ay nagsasabing may bagong sitwasyon o pagbabago. Hindi ito simpleng past tense."],"tip":["了1 = 'selesai satu paket' (V了 + angka + benda). 了2 = 'sekarang sudah beda dari sebelumnya'. Tanya diri: ini laporan aksi selesai, atau kabar 'ada yang berubah'?","了1 = 'one finished package' (V了 + number + thing). 了2 = 'now it's different from before'. Ask yourself: am I reporting a finished action, or announcing a change?","了1 = 'isang natapos na kilos'. 了2 = 'iba na ngayon kaysa dati'. Tanungin: tapos na kilos ba, o balita ng pagbabago?"],"warn":["✗ 我昨天很忙了。→ ✓ 我昨天很忙。（keadaan di masa lalu tidak perlu 了; 了 bukan 'past tense'）","✗ 我昨天很忙了。→ ✓ 我昨天很忙。(a past state needs no 了; 了 is not a past tense)","✗ 我昨天很忙了。→ ✓ 我昨天很忙。(walang 了 sa nakaraang kalagayan)"],"logic":{"id":"Bahasa Indonesia memakai 'sudah' untuk dua hal sekaligus: 'sudah makan' (selesai) dan 'sudah tidak minum kopi' (berubah). Penutur Taiwan memisahkannya: 了 di belakang verba melaporkan satu kejadian yang tuntas, 了 di akhir kalimat mengumumkan 'keadaan sekarang baru'. Kalau kalimat hanya menceritakan masa lalu biasa (dulu tinggal di Jakarta), orang Taiwan tidak memakai 了 sama sekali. Jadi berpikirlah tentang 'tuntas/berubah', bukan 'kemarin/dulu'.","en":"Indonesian 'sudah' covers both 'already ate' (completion) and 'no longer drink coffee' (change). Taiwanese speakers split them: 了 after the verb reports one finished event, 了 at the end announces 'the situation is new now'. For plain past background (I used to live in Jakarta) they use no 了 at all. So think 'finished / changed', not 'yesterday / before'."},"ex":[["我吃了兩個便當。","wǒ chī le liǎng ge biàn dāng","Aku makan dua kotak bento.","I ate two bento boxes.","Kumain ako ng dalawang bento.","daily"],["下雨了，帶傘吧。","xià yǔ le dài sǎn ba","Hujan nih, bawa payung ya.","It's raining now, take an umbrella.","Umuulan na, magdala ka ng payong.","daily"],["我現在不喝咖啡了。","wǒ xiàn zài bù hē kā fēi le","Sekarang aku sudah tidak minum kopi lagi.","I don't drink coffee anymore.","Hindi na ako umiinom ng kape ngayon.","daily"],["我會用示波器了。","wǒ huì yòng shì bō qì le","Aku sekarang sudah bisa pakai osiloskop.","I can use the oscilloscope now.","Marunong na akong gumamit ng oscilloscope.","campus"],["老師講完了，我們可以開始做實驗了。","lǎo shī jiǎng wán le wǒ men kě yǐ kāi shǐ zuò shí yàn le","Dosen sudah selesai menjelaskan, sekarang kita boleh mulai praktikum.","The teacher has finished explaining; we can start the experiment now.","Tapos na ang guro, puwede na tayong magsimula ng eksperimento.","campus"],["他昨天檢查了三台機台。","tā zuó tiān jiǎn chá le sān tái jī tái","Kemarin dia memeriksa tiga mesin.","Yesterday he inspected three tools.","Kahapon, tatlong makina ang sinuri niya.","fab"],["機台修好了，可以跑貨了。","jī tái xiū hǎo le kě yǐ pǎo huò le","Mesinnya sudah beres, sudah bisa jalan produksi lagi.","The tool is fixed; we can run lots again.","Naayos na ang makina, puwede nang magpatakbo ng produkto.","fab"]],"drill":[{"q":"我昨天買＿一支新手機。","opts":["了","著","得"],"a":0,"why":"Aksi selesai dengan objek berjumlah (一支) → V了."},{"q":"我以前很喜歡吃辣，現在不喜歡＿。","opts":["的","了","過"],"a":1,"why":"Perubahan keadaan (dulu suka, sekarang tidak) → 了 di akhir."},{"q":"機台已經修好＿，可以用了。","opts":["著","過","了"],"a":2,"why":"Hasil sudah tercapai dan situasinya baru → 修好了."},{"q":"他已經二十歲＿。","opts":["了","著","過"],"a":0,"why":"Keadaan baru (sekarang sudah 20) → 了2."}]},{"lv":4,"k":"b1_dur","form":"V + 了 + 時間 + O（了）／ V + O + V + 了 + 時間（了）／ 時間 + 沒 + V + 了","icon":"clock","name":["Durasi: V了三年 vs V了三年了","Duration: V了三年 vs V了三年了","Tagal: V了三年 vs V了三年了"],"gloss":["Lama waktu diletakkan SETELAH verba: 睡了十個小時. Kalau ada objek, ulangi verbanya (學中文學了兩年) atau taruh waktu sebelum objek (學了兩年中文). Tambahan 了 di akhir (了…了) berarti aksinya masih berlangsung sampai sekarang. Untuk 'sudah lama tidak…', waktu diletakkan sebelum 沒.","Duration goes AFTER the verb: 睡了十個小時. With an object, repeat the verb (學中文學了兩年) or put the time before the object (學了兩年中文). An extra final 了 (了…了) means the action is still going on now. For 'haven't … for (time)', the time goes before 沒.","Ang tagal ay inilalagay PAGKATAPOS ng pandiwa. Kapag may object, ulitin ang pandiwa o ilagay ang oras bago ang object. Kapag may isa pang 了 sa dulo, tuloy pa rin ang kilos hanggang ngayon."],"tip":["Satu 了 = cerita yang sudah tutup buku. Dua 了 = 'sampai sekarang dan masih jalan'. Ingat: 我住了三年 (dulu), 我住了三年了 (dan masih tinggal).","One 了 = a closed story. Two 了 = 'up to now and still going'. 我住了三年 (in the past), 我住了三年了 (and I still live here).","Isang 了 = tapos na kuwento. Dalawang 了 = 'hanggang ngayon at tuloy pa'."],"warn":["✗ 我兩年學中文。→ ✓ 我學中文學了兩年。/ 我學了兩年中文。","✗ 我兩年學中文。→ ✓ 我學中文學了兩年。/ 我學了兩年中文。","✗ 我兩年學中文。→ ✓ 我學中文學了兩年。/ 我學了兩年中文。"],"logic":{"id":"Orang Indonesia bilang 'aku belajar Mandarin dua tahun' dan menaruh durasi bebas. Dalam bahasa Mandarin, durasi adalah 'ukuran' dari verba, jadi harus menempel tepat di belakang verba, seperti label panjang. Kalau objek ikut, verbanya diulang supaya durasi tetap menempel. Lalu penutur Taiwan menambah 了 di akhir untuk berkata 'dan ini masih berlanjut' — informasi yang dalam bahasa Indonesia biasanya disampaikan dengan 'sudah … dan masih'. Tapi untuk 'sudah lama tidak', durasinya menjadi jangka waktu kosong, jadi diletakkan sebelum 沒.","en":"Indonesians say 'aku belajar Mandarin dua tahun' and place the duration freely. In Mandarin the duration is a measurement of the verb, so it must stick right after the verb like a length label. If there's an object, the verb is repeated so the duration can still attach. Taiwanese speakers then add a final 了 to mean 'and it's still continuing'. For 'haven't done X for a while', the duration is an empty stretch of time, so it goes before 沒."},"ex":[["我學中文學了兩年。","wǒ xué zhōng wén xué le liǎng nián","Aku belajar bahasa Mandarin selama dua tahun.","I studied Chinese for two years.","Nag-aral ako ng Chinese nang dalawang taon.","campus"],["我學了兩年中文了。","wǒ xué le liǎng nián zhōng wén le","Aku sudah belajar Mandarin dua tahun (dan masih belajar).","I've been studying Chinese for two years (and still am).","Dalawang taon na akong nag-aaral ng Chinese.","campus"],["我在高雄住了三年了。","wǒ zài gāo xióng zhù le sān nián le","Aku sudah tinggal di Kaohsiung tiga tahun.","I've lived in Kaohsiung for three years now.","Tatlong taon na akong nakatira sa Kaohsiung.","daily"],["昨天我睡了十個小時。","zuó tiān wǒ shuì le shí ge xiǎo shí","Kemarin aku tidur sepuluh jam.","Yesterday I slept for ten hours.","Kahapon, sampung oras akong natulog.","daily"],["這個實驗我們做了三個小時。","zhè ge shí yàn wǒ men zuò le sān ge xiǎo shí","Praktikum ini kami kerjakan selama tiga jam.","We spent three hours on this experiment.","Tatlong oras naming ginawa ang eksperimentong ito.","campus"],["我們等工程師等了四十分鐘了。","wǒ men děng gōng chéng shī děng le sì shí fēn zhōng le","Kami sudah menunggu insinyurnya empat puluh menit.","We've been waiting for the engineer for forty minutes.","Apatnapung minuto na naming hinihintay ang engineer.","fab"],["他在晶圓廠工作了五年了。","tā zài jīng yuán chǎng gōng zuò le wǔ nián le","Dia sudah lima tahun kerja di fab wafer.","He's been working at the wafer fab for five years.","Limang taon na siyang nagtatrabaho sa wafer fab.","fab"],["我已經兩個星期沒運動了。","wǒ yǐ jīng liǎng ge xīng qí méi yùn dòng le","Aku sudah dua minggu tidak olahraga.","I haven't exercised for two weeks.","Dalawang linggo na akong hindi nag-eehersisyo.","daily"]],"drill":[{"q":"我在台灣住＿三年＿，還想再住兩年。","opts":["了…了","過…過","了…的"],"a":0,"why":"Masih tinggal sampai sekarang → 了…了."},{"q":"我們等公車等＿二十分鐘。","opts":["著","了","過"],"a":1,"why":"Durasi setelah verba yang diulang: 等了二十分鐘."},{"q":"我已經一個星期＿去實驗室了。","opts":["不","沒","別"],"a":1,"why":"'Sudah seminggu tidak' → 時間 + 沒 + V + 了."},{"q":"老師講＿一個小時的課。","opts":["了","在","得"],"a":0,"why":"V + 了 + durasi + 的 + objek."}]},{"lv":3,"k":"b1_zhengzai","form":"(正)在 + V + (O)（呢）；否定：沒在 + V","icon":"wave","name":["正在/在: sedang","正在/在: in the middle of doing","正在/在: kasalukuyang ginagawa"],"gloss":["在 atau 正在 sebelum verba berarti aksi sedang berlangsung pada saat itu (sekarang, atau pada waktu tertentu di masa lalu). 呢 di akhir membuat lebih santai. Negasinya 沒在, bukan 不在.","在 or 正在 before the verb means the action is in progress at that moment (now, or at a given past time). A final 呢 sounds more casual. The negative is 沒在, not 不在.","Ang 在 o 正在 bago ang pandiwa ay nangangahulugang ginagawa ito sa sandaling iyon. Ang negatibo ay 沒在, hindi 不在."],"tip":["正在 = 'sedang persis sekarang', lebih tegas daripada 在. Gampang: 在 + tempat = di; 在 + verba = sedang.","正在 = 'right in the middle of it', stronger than 在. Easy rule: 在 + place = at; 在 + verb = -ing.","正在 = 'mismong ngayon'. 在 + lugar = sa; 在 + pandiwa = ginagawa."],"warn":["✗ 我不在看電視。→ ✓ 我沒在看電視。","✗ 我不在看電視。→ ✓ 我沒在看電視。","✗ 我不在看電視。→ ✓ 我沒在看電視。"],"logic":{"id":"Bahasa Indonesia punya 'sedang' yang mirip sekali, jadi pola ini mudah. Bedanya ada dua. Pertama, orang Taiwan biasanya tidak menggabungkan 'sedang' dengan 了, karena 了 berarti selesai dan 在 berarti belum selesai. Kedua, negasinya 沒在 karena kita menyangkal sebuah kejadian nyata ('tidak sedang terjadi'), bukan kemauan. Di masa lalu, cukup sebut waktunya: 他打來的時候我在洗澡.","en":"Indonesian 'sedang' maps almost perfectly, so this pattern is easy. Two differences: Taiwanese speakers normally don't combine 在 with 了, since 了 means finished and 在 means not finished. And the negative is 沒在, because you're denying an actual event ('it isn't happening'), not a wish. For the past, just name the time: 他打來的時候我在洗澡."},"ex":[["我正在吃飯，等一下打給你。","wǒ zhèng zài chī fàn děng yí xià dǎ gěi nǐ","Aku lagi makan, nanti aku telepon balik.","I'm eating right now, I'll call you back.","Kumakain ako ngayon, tatawagan kita mamaya.","daily"],["你在做什麼？我在找機車鑰匙。","nǐ zài zuò shén me wǒ zài zhǎo jī chē yào shi","Lagi ngapain? Aku lagi cari kunci motor.","What are you doing? I'm looking for my scooter key.","Ano ang ginagawa mo? Hinahanap ko ang susi ng motor.","daily"],["學長正在幫我們檢查電路。","xué zhǎng zhèng zài bāng wǒ men jiǎn chá diàn lù","Senior lagi bantu memeriksa rangkaian kami.","Our senior is checking our circuit for us.","Tinitingnan ng senior ang circuit namin.","campus"],["老師打電話來的時候，我在寫實驗報告。","lǎo shī dǎ diàn huà lái de shí hòu wǒ zài xiě shí yàn bào gào","Waktu dosen menelepon, aku sedang menulis laporan praktikum.","When the teacher called, I was writing my lab report.","Nang tumawag ang guro, nagsusulat ako ng lab report.","campus"],["機台正在跑貨，先不要開門。","jī tái zhèng zài pǎo huò xiān bú yào kāi mén","Mesin lagi jalan produksi, jangan buka pintunya dulu.","The tool is running a lot, don't open the door yet.","Tumatakbo ang makina, huwag munang buksan ang pinto.","fab"],["工程師正在處理異常，請等一下。","gōng chéng shī zhèng zài chǔ lǐ yì cháng qǐng děng yí xià","Insinyurnya sedang menangani abnormal, tunggu sebentar.","The engineer is handling the abnormality, please wait.","Inaayos ng engineer ang abnormalidad, sandali lang.","fab"]],"drill":[{"q":"A：你在做什麼？B：我＿寫作業。","opts":["在","了","過"],"a":0,"why":"Aksi sedang berlangsung → 在 + V."},{"q":"他現在＿上課，不能接電話。","opts":["已經","正在","剛才"],"a":1,"why":"'Sekarang sedang' → 正在."},{"q":"我＿在玩手機，我在查資料！","opts":["不","沒","別"],"a":1,"why":"Negasi progresif → 沒在."},{"q":"你打給我的時候，我正在＿澡。","opts":["洗","洗了","洗過"],"a":0,"why":"正在 tidak dipakai dengan 了/過."}]},{"lv":4,"k":"b1_zhe","form":"V + 著（keadaan tetap）／ V1 + 著 + V2（sambil）／ 地點 + V + 著 + O","icon":"pin","name":["著: keadaan yang bertahan","著: lasting state","著: patuloy na kalagayan"],"gloss":["著 setelah verba menunjukkan keadaan hasil yang bertahan: 門開著 (pintunya terbuka). V1著V2 berarti melakukan V2 dalam posisi/cara V1: 聽著音樂寫作業. Pola 'tempat + V著 + benda' menggambarkan apa yang ada di suatu tempat: 桌上放著一本書.","著 after a verb shows a resulting state that lasts: 門開著 (the door is open). V1著V2 means doing V2 in the manner of V1: 聽著音樂寫作業. 'Place + V著 + thing' describes what is located somewhere: 桌上放著一本書.","Ang 著 ay nagpapakita ng kalagayang nananatili. Ang V1著V2 ay paggawa ng V2 habang nasa V1. 'Lugar + V著 + bagay' ay naglalarawan kung ano ang nasa lugar."],"tip":["在 = aksi sedang bergerak (video). 著 = keadaan diam (foto). 他在穿外套 = sedang memakai; 他穿著外套 = dalam keadaan memakai.","在 = action in motion (a video). 著 = still state (a photo). 他在穿外套 = putting it on; 他穿著外套 = wearing it.","在 = gumagalaw na kilos (video). 著 = tahimik na kalagayan (larawan)."],"warn":["✗ 他在穿一件紅色的外套。(maksud: dia memakai jaket merah) → ✓ 他穿著一件紅色的外套。（在穿 = sedang mengenakan/memasang）","✗ 他在穿一件紅色的外套。(meaning: he is wearing a red jacket) → ✓ 他穿著一件紅色的外套。(在穿 = in the act of putting it on)","✗ 他在穿一件紅色的外套。(ibig sabihin: suot niya) → ✓ 他穿著一件紅色的外套。"],"logic":{"id":"Bahasa Indonesia memakai awalan ter- atau kata 'dalam keadaan': 'pintunya terbuka', 'lampunya menyala'. Penutur Taiwan melihat hasil sebuah aksi yang masih bertahan, lalu menempelkan 著 ke verba aksinya: 開著, 亮著, 穿著. Jadi pikirkan aksi apa yang menghasilkan keadaan itu. Untuk 'sambil', 著 menandai aksi latar (posisi/cara) dan verba kedua adalah aksi utama.","en":"Indonesian uses ter- or 'dalam keadaan': 'pintunya terbuka', 'lampunya menyala'. Taiwanese speakers see the result of an action that is still holding, and attach 著 to that action verb: 開著, 亮著, 穿著. So think about which action produced the state. In V1著V2, 著 marks the background manner and the second verb is the main action."},"ex":[["門開著，冷氣都跑出去了。","mén kāi zhe lěng qì dōu pǎo chū qù le","Pintunya terbuka, dinginnya AC keluar semua.","The door's open, all the AC is escaping.","Bukas ang pinto, lumalabas ang lamig ng aircon.","daily"],["別站著，坐下來吧。","bié zhàn zhe zuò xià lái ba","Jangan berdiri terus, duduk saja.","Don't stand there, sit down.","Huwag kang tumayo, umupo ka.","daily"],["桌上放著一本說明書。","zhuō shàng fàng zhe yì běn shuō míng shū","Di atas meja ada sebuah buku manual.","There's a manual lying on the table.","May isang manual sa ibabaw ng mesa.","campus"],["他喜歡聽著音樂寫作業。","tā xǐ huān tīng zhe yīn yuè xiě zuò yè","Dia suka mengerjakan PR sambil mendengarkan musik.","He likes doing homework while listening to music.","Gusto niyang gumawa ng homework habang nakikinig ng musika.","campus"],["無塵室裡要一直穿著無塵衣。","wú chén shì lǐ yào yì zhí chuān zhe wú chén yī","Di dalam cleanroom harus selalu memakai baju cleanroom.","In the cleanroom you must keep the bunny suit on the whole time.","Sa cleanroom, dapat laging suot ang cleanroom suit.","fab"],["機台上亮著紅燈，可能有異常。","jī tái shàng liàng zhe hóng dēng kě néng yǒu yì cháng","Di mesin lampu merah menyala, mungkin ada abnormal.","A red light is on at the tool, there may be an abnormality.","Nakabukas ang pulang ilaw sa makina, baka may problema.","fab"]],"drill":[{"q":"牆上掛＿一張製程流程圖。","opts":["得","著","在"],"a":1,"why":"Tempat + V著 + benda → keadaan."},{"q":"他笑＿說：「沒問題！」","opts":["著","了","的"],"a":0,"why":"V1著V2: berbicara sambil tersenyum."},{"q":"教室的燈還亮＿，誰在裡面？","opts":["過","的","著"],"a":2,"why":"Lampu dalam keadaan menyala → 亮著."},{"q":"不要躺＿看手機，對眼睛不好。","opts":["著","了","得"],"a":0,"why":"Posisi saat melakukan aksi lain → 躺著看."}]},{"lv":4,"k":"b1_guole","form":"V + 過（pengalaman）vs V + 了（kejadian selesai）；沒 + V + 過","icon":"scale","name":["過 vs 了: pernah vs sudah","過 vs 了: experience vs completion","過 vs 了: karanasan vs natapos"],"gloss":["過 berbicara tentang pengalaman: pernah atau tidak pernah, tanpa peduli kapan tepatnya. 了 melaporkan satu kejadian tertentu yang selesai, sering dengan waktu jelas (昨天). 他去了日本 berarti dia pergi (mungkin masih di sana); 他去過日本 berarti dia pernah ke sana (sudah kembali). Negasi pengalaman: 沒V過.","過 talks about experience: ever or never, regardless of exactly when. 了 reports one specific finished event, often with a clear time (昨天). 他去了日本 = he went (maybe still there); 他去過日本 = he has been there (and came back). Negative experience: 沒V過.","Ang 過 ay tungkol sa karanasan. Ang 了 ay isang tiyak na pangyayaring natapos. 他去了日本 = umalis siya (baka nandoon pa); 他去過日本 = nakapunta na siya."],"tip":["過 = isi CV hidupmu. 了 = isi buku harian kemarin.","過 = your life CV. 了 = yesterday's diary entry.","過 = CV ng buhay mo. 了 = talaarawan kahapon."],"warn":["✗ 我沒去了花蓮。→ ✓ 我沒去花蓮。/ 我沒去過花蓮。","✗ 我沒去了花蓮。→ ✓ 我沒去花蓮。/ 我沒去過花蓮。","✗ 我沒去了花蓮。→ ✓ 我沒去花蓮。/ 我沒去過花蓮。"],"logic":{"id":"Dalam bahasa Indonesia 'pernah' dan 'sudah' memang berbeda, tapi sering dicampur dalam percakapan. Orang Taiwan memilih berdasarkan pertanyaan di kepala: 'apakah ini bagian dari pengalaman hidupnya?' → 過; 'apakah kejadian itu sudah terjadi?' → 了. Kalimat dengan waktu spesifik (昨天, 上星期) hampir selalu memakai 了. Di pabrik, 保養過了 berarti 'sudah pernah dirawat, jadi itu bukan penyebabnya' — 過 membawa nuansa 'sudah dicoba/dialami'.","en":"Indonesian distinguishes 'pernah' and 'sudah', but speakers blur them. Taiwanese speakers choose by the question in mind: 'is this part of someone's life experience?' → 過; 'did that event happen?' → 了. A sentence with a specific time (昨天, 上星期) almost always uses 了. In the fab, 保養過了 means 'it has already had PM, so that's not the cause' — 過 carries the sense of 'already been tried/experienced'."},"ex":[["我去過墾丁，可是還沒去過花蓮。","wǒ qù guò kěn dīng kě shì hái méi qù guò huā lián","Aku pernah ke Kenting, tapi belum pernah ke Hualien.","I've been to Kenting, but never to Hualien.","Nakapunta na ako sa Kenting, pero hindi pa sa Hualien.","daily"],["我昨天去了墾丁，玩得很開心。","wǒ zuó tiān qù le kěn dīng wán de hěn kāi xīn","Kemarin aku ke Kenting, seru banget.","I went to Kenting yesterday and had a great time.","Pumunta ako sa Kenting kahapon at nag-enjoy ako.","daily"],["他去了日本，下個月才回來。","tā qù le rì běn xià ge yuè cái huí lái","Dia pergi ke Jepang, baru pulang bulan depan.","He's gone to Japan and won't be back until next month.","Pumunta siya sa Japan, sa susunod na buwan pa babalik.","daily"],["你用過示波器嗎？","nǐ yòng guò shì bō qì ma","Kamu pernah pakai osiloskop?","Have you ever used an oscilloscope?","Nakagamit ka na ba ng oscilloscope?","campus"],["這個題目老師上星期講過了。","zhè ge tí mù lǎo shī shàng xīng qí jiǎng guò le","Soal ini sudah pernah dibahas dosen minggu lalu.","The teacher already went over this problem last week.","Naipaliwanag na ng guro ang tanong na ito noong isang linggo.","campus"],["我進過無塵室，可是沒操作過機台。","wǒ jìn guò wú chén shì kě shì méi cāo zuò guò jī tái","Aku pernah masuk cleanroom, tapi belum pernah mengoperasikan mesin.","I've been inside a cleanroom, but I've never operated a tool.","Nakapasok na ako sa cleanroom, pero hindi pa ako nakapag-operate ng makina.","fab"],["這台機台上個月保養過了，這次是別的問題。","zhè tái jī tái shàng ge yuè bǎo yǎng guò le zhè cì shì bié de wèn tí","Mesin ini sudah di-PM bulan lalu, kali ini masalahnya lain.","This tool already had PM last month; this time it's a different problem.","Na-PM na ang makinang ito noong nakaraang buwan, iba ang problema ngayon.","fab"]],"drill":[{"q":"你吃＿臭豆腐嗎？","opts":["過","了","著"],"a":0,"why":"Menanyakan pengalaman → 過."},{"q":"他去＿日本，下個月才回來。","opts":["過","了","著"],"a":1,"why":"Dia masih di Jepang (belum kembali) → 去了, bukan 去過 (pengalaman yang sudah selesai)."},{"q":"我從來沒看＿這種機台。","opts":["了","著","過"],"a":2,"why":"從來沒…過 = belum pernah sama sekali."},{"q":"A：報告寫好了嗎？B：寫好了，我也檢查＿了。","opts":["過","著","得"],"a":0,"why":"Sudah dicek (pengalaman/sudah dilakukan) → 檢查過了."}]},{"lv":4,"k":"b1_jiucai","form":"時間/條件 + 就 + V + 了（lebih awal, mudah）／ 時間/條件 + 才 + V（lebih lambat, susah）","icon":"clock","name":["就 vs 才: cepat vs telat","就 vs 才: early vs late","就 vs 才: maaga vs huli"],"gloss":["就 setelah keterangan waktu berarti lebih awal/cepat/mudah dari perkiraan, dan biasanya diikuti 了. 才 berarti lebih lambat/susah dari perkiraan, dan biasanya TIDAK memakai 了. 才 juga bisa berarti 'baru boleh … kalau …' (syarat).","就 after a time expression means earlier/faster/easier than expected, usually with 了. 才 means later/harder than expected and normally does NOT take 了. 才 can also mean 'only then' (a condition).","Ang 就 ay mas maaga o mas madali kaysa inaasahan, karaniwang may 了. Ang 才 ay mas huli o mas mahirap, at karaniwang walang 了."],"tip":["就 = 'udah!' (cepat, puas). 才 = 'baru…' (lama, kesal). Indonesian 'baru' hampir selalu = 才.","就 = 'already!' (quick, satisfied). 才 = 'not until…' (slow, annoyed). Indonesian 'baru' almost always = 才.","就 = 'agad!' 才 = 'saka lang…'"],"warn":["✗ 我十點才起床了。→ ✓ 我十點才起床。","✗ 我十點才起床了。→ ✓ 我十點才起床。","✗ 我十點才起床了。→ ✓ 我十點才起床。"],"logic":{"id":"Kalimat '他七點到' hanya fakta. Penutur Taiwan hampir selalu menambahkan penilaian: 就 kalau menurutnya itu cepat, 才 kalau menurutnya itu lambat. Bahasa Indonesia punya 'baru' (= 才) dan 'sudah … saja' (≈ 就). Karena 才 menekankan sesuatu yang baru saja terjadi setelah lama, ia tidak memakai 了. Di pabrik, 'diperbaiki sampai jam dua pagi baru bisa' = 修到兩點才好 — kata 才 sudah membawa rasa lelahnya.","en":"'他七點到' is a bare fact. Taiwanese speakers almost always add a judgment: 就 if they think it's early, 才 if they think it's late. Indonesian has 'baru' (= 才) and 'sudah … saja' (≈ 就). Because 才 stresses something that only just happened after a long wait, it doesn't take 了. In the fab, 修到兩點才好 already carries the tiredness in 才."},"ex":[["他七點就到學校了。","tā qī diǎn jiù dào xué xiào le","Jam tujuh dia sudah sampai di kampus.","He was already at school by seven.","Alas siyete pa lang, nasa paaralan na siya.","campus"],["我十點才起床。","wǒ shí diǎn cái qǐ chuáng","Aku baru bangun jam sepuluh.","I didn't get up until ten.","Alas diyes na ako bumangon.","daily"],["公車二十分鐘才來一班。","gōng chē èr shí fēn zhōng cái lái yì bān","Busnya baru datang satu tiap dua puluh menit.","A bus only comes every twenty minutes.","Isang bus lang kada dalawampung minuto.","daily"],["這個電路我接了三次才接對。","zhè ge diàn lù wǒ jiē le sān cì cái jiē duì","Rangkaian ini baru benar setelah kusambung tiga kali.","It took me three tries to wire this circuit correctly.","Tatlong beses ko itong kinabit bago tumama.","campus"],["實驗做完了才可以回家。","shí yàn zuò wán le cái kě yǐ huí jiā","Praktikum harus selesai dulu, baru boleh pulang.","You can only go home after the experiment is done.","Saka lang puwedeng umuwi kapag tapos na ang eksperimento.","campus"],["新人三個月就學會操作機台了。","xīn rén sān ge yuè jiù xué huì cāo zuò jī tái le","Karyawan baru itu dalam tiga bulan sudah bisa mengoperasikan mesin.","The new hire learned to run the tool in just three months.","Sa tatlong buwan lang, natuto na ang bago na mag-operate ng makina.","fab"],["機台修到半夜兩點才好。","jī tái xiū dào bàn yè liǎng diǎn cái hǎo","Mesinnya baru beres diperbaiki jam dua pagi.","The tool wasn't fixed until 2 a.m.","Alas dos na ng madaling-araw bago naayos ang makina.","fab"]],"drill":[{"q":"電影七點開始，他七點半＿來。","opts":["就","才","也"],"a":1,"why":"Terlambat → 才, tanpa 了."},{"q":"我五分鐘＿吃完了，因為太餓了。","opts":["才","再","就"],"a":2,"why":"Cepat sekali → 就…了."},{"q":"他已經等了一個小時，你怎麼現在＿到？","opts":["才","就","也"],"a":0,"why":"Lambat, bikin kesal → 才."},{"q":"這個問題很簡單，學長看一下＿懂了。","opts":["才","就","還"],"a":1,"why":"Mudah dan cepat → 就…了."}]},{"lv":4,"k":"b1_zaiyou","form":"再 + V（lagi, belum terjadi）／ 又 + V + 了（lagi, sudah terjadi）／ 還 + 想/要 + V（masih mau lagi）","icon":"arrows","name":["再, 又, 還: 'lagi'","再, 又, 還: three kinds of 'again'","再, 又, 還: tatlong klase ng 'ulit'"],"gloss":["再 dipakai untuk pengulangan yang BELUM terjadi (permintaan, rencana): 請再說一次. 又 untuk pengulangan yang SUDAH terjadi, sering dengan nada kesal: 又當機了! 還 berarti 'masih' — 還想再… = masih ingin … lagi. 再 juga berarti 'baru kemudian': 等一下再做.","再 is for repetition that has NOT happened yet (requests, plans): 請再說一次. 又 is for repetition that HAS happened, often with annoyance: 又當機了! 還 means 'still' — 還想再… = still want to … again. 再 also means 'then, later': 等一下再做.","Ang 再 ay para sa pag-uulit na hindi pa nangyayari. Ang 又 ay para sa nangyari na ulit, madalas may inis. Ang 還 ay 'pa rin'."],"tip":["再 = tombol 'replay' yang belum ditekan. 又 = 'aduh, lagi-lagi!'","再 = a replay button not yet pressed. 又 = 'ugh, not again!'","再 = replay na hindi pa pinipindot. 又 = 'hay, na naman!'"],"warn":["✗ 他明天又來。(rencana) → ✓ 他明天再來。","✗ 他明天又來。(a plan) → ✓ 他明天再來。","✗ 他明天又來。→ ✓ 他明天再來。"],"logic":{"id":"Bahasa Indonesia hanya punya satu kata 'lagi' untuk semua arah waktu. Penutur Taiwan langsung memilih berdasarkan garis waktu: kalau pengulangannya ada di depan (belum terjadi) → 再; kalau sudah di belakang (sudah terjadi) → 又, biasanya ditutup 了. 還 bukan soal pengulangan tapi soal 'masih berlanjut', jadi sering dipasangkan: 還想再吃 = masih ingin makan lagi. Pengecualian kecil: 又 boleh untuk masa depan yang pasti terulang, misalnya 明天又是星期一了.","en":"Indonesian has one word 'lagi' for every direction of time. Taiwanese speakers pick by timeline: repetition ahead (not yet happened) → 再; repetition behind (already happened) → 又, usually closed with 了. 還 isn't about repeating but about 'still continuing', so it often pairs up: 還想再吃 = still want to eat more. Small exception: 又 can describe a certain recurring future, e.g. 明天又是星期一了."},"ex":[["請你再說一次。","qǐng nǐ zài shuō yí cì","Tolong ulangi sekali lagi.","Please say it once more.","Pakiulit mo nga.","daily"],["我還想再來這家店。","wǒ hái xiǎng zài lái zhè jiā diàn","Aku masih ingin datang lagi ke toko ini.","I'd like to come to this place again.","Gusto ko pang bumalik sa tindahang ito.","daily"],["他昨天遲到，今天又遲到了。","tā zuó tiān chí dào jīn tiān yòu chí dào le","Kemarin dia telat, hari ini telat lagi.","He was late yesterday, and late again today.","Na-late siya kahapon, na-late na naman ngayon.","campus"],["電阻燒掉了，我們再換一個吧。","diàn zǔ shāo diào le wǒ men zài huàn yí ge ba","Resistornya terbakar, kita ganti satu lagi yuk.","The resistor burned out, let's swap in another one.","Nasunog ang resistor, palitan natin ulit.","campus"],["這台機台又當機了！","zhè tái jī tái yòu dàng jī le","Mesin ini hang lagi!","This tool crashed again!","Nag-hang na naman ang makinang ito!","fab"],["良率又下降了，主管很不高興。","liáng lǜ yòu xià jiàng le zhǔ guǎn hěn bù gāo xìng","Yield turun lagi, atasan nggak senang.","Yield dropped again and the manager isn't happy.","Bumaba na naman ang yield, hindi masaya ang supervisor.","fab"],["等一下再跑一次測試。","děng yí xià zài pǎo yí cì cè shì","Nanti kita jalankan tes sekali lagi.","We'll run the test again in a bit.","Mamaya, patakbuhin ulit ang test.","fab"]],"drill":[{"q":"老師，我聽不清楚，可以＿說一次嗎？","opts":["又","再","還"],"a":1,"why":"Permintaan, belum terjadi → 再."},{"q":"你怎麼＿忘了帶識別證？","opts":["又","再","才"],"a":0,"why":"Sudah terjadi lagi, nada kesal → 又."},{"q":"這個便當很好吃，我＿想再吃一個。","opts":["已經","還","才"],"a":1,"why":"'Masih ingin' → 還想再."},{"q":"機台修好了，我們＿試一次看看。","opts":["又","才","再"],"a":2,"why":"Rencana mencoba ulang → 再."}]},{"lv":4,"k":"b1_rc","form":"V + 完／好／到／懂／錯／見／掉 (+ 了)；否定：沒 + V + 補語","icon":"target","name":["Komplemen hasil: V完/好/到/懂/錯/見/掉","Result complements: V完/好/到/懂/錯/見/掉","Result complement: V完/好/到/懂/錯/見/掉"],"gloss":["Mandarin memisahkan aksi dan hasilnya: verba pertama = aksinya, kata kedua = hasilnya. 完 = selesai, 好 = beres/siap, 到 = berhasil mencapai, 懂 = paham, 錯 = salah, 見 = tertangkap indra, 掉 = hilang/lepas. Negasinya 沒 + V + hasil.","Mandarin separates an action from its result: first verb = the action, second word = the result. 完 = finished, 好 = done properly/ready, 到 = reached/managed, 懂 = understood, 錯 = wrong, 見 = perceived, 掉 = gone/off. Negate with 沒 + V + result.","Hinihiwalay ng Mandarin ang kilos at ang resulta. 完 = tapos, 好 = handa, 到 = naabot, 懂 = naintindihan, 錯 = mali, 見 = napansin, 掉 = nawala. Negatibo: 沒 + V + resulta."],"tip":["Tanya dua hal: 'ngapain?' + 'hasilnya apa?'. 看 (melihat) + 到 (ketemu) = 看到. 聽 (mendengar) + 懂 (paham) = 聽懂.","Ask two things: 'what action?' + 'what result?'. 看 + 到 = saw it. 聽 + 懂 = understood by listening.","Dalawang tanong: 'anong kilos?' + 'anong resulta?'."],"warn":["✗ 我不聽懂。→ ✓ 我沒聽懂。/ 我聽不懂。","✗ 我不聽懂。→ ✓ 我沒聽懂。/ 我聽不懂。","✗ 我不聽懂。→ ✓ 我沒聽懂。/ 我聽不懂。"],"logic":{"id":"Dalam bahasa Indonesia, satu kata sering sudah mengandung hasil: 'menemukan', 'memahami', 'menghabiskan'. Penutur Taiwan berpikir dua langkah: aksinya dulu, lalu hasilnya. 找 hanya 'mencari'; kalau berhasil, baru 找到. 聽 hanya 'mendengarkan'; kalau paham, 聽懂. Karena itu 'aku sudah mencari tapi tidak menemukan' sangat alami: 我找了，可是沒找到. Di lab dan fab, hasil ini penting: 設好 (sudah diset dengan benar) berbeda dengan 設錯 (salah set).","en":"In Indonesian, one word often already contains the result: 'menemukan' (find), 'memahami'. Taiwanese speakers think in two steps: the action, then the result. 找 is only 'look for'; if you succeed, it's 找到. 聽 is only 'listen'; if you understand, 聽懂. So 'I looked but didn't find it' is very natural: 我找了，可是沒找到. In the lab and fab the result matters: 設好 (set correctly) vs 設錯 (set wrong)."},"ex":[["我寫完作業了。","wǒ xiě wán zuò yè le","PR-ku sudah selesai kutulis.","I've finished my homework.","Natapos ko na ang homework.","campus"],["晚餐準備好了，快來吃！","wǎn cān zhǔn bèi hǎo le kuài lái chī","Makan malam sudah siap, ayo makan!","Dinner's ready, come eat!","Handa na ang hapunan, kain na!","daily"],["我找到我的學生證了。","wǒ zhǎo dào wǒ de xué shēng zhèng le","Kartu mahasiswaku sudah ketemu.","I found my student ID.","Nahanap ko na ang student ID ko.","campus"],["你聽懂老師的說明了嗎？","nǐ tīng dǒng lǎo shī de shuō míng le ma","Kamu paham penjelasan dosen tadi?","Did you understand the teacher's explanation?","Naintindihan mo ba ang paliwanag ng guro?","campus"],["我看錯時間了，差一點遲到。","wǒ kàn cuò shí jiān le chà yì diǎn chí dào","Aku salah lihat jam, hampir telat.","I misread the time and was nearly late.","Mali ang tingin ko sa oras, muntik na akong ma-late.","daily"],["你聽見警報聲了嗎？","nǐ tīng jiàn jǐng bào shēng le ma","Kamu dengar bunyi alarm?","Did you hear the alarm?","Narinig mo ba ang alarma?","fab"],["機台的參數我設好了。","jī tái de cān shù wǒ shè hǎo le","Parameter mesin sudah kuset.","I've set the tool parameters.","Na-set ko na ang parameters ng makina.","fab"],["這片晶圓破掉了，要重新跑。","zhè piàn jīng yuán pò diào le yào chóng xīn pǎo","Wafer ini pecah, harus dijalankan ulang.","This wafer broke; we have to rerun it.","Nabasag ang wafer na ito, kailangang patakbuhin ulit.","fab"]],"drill":[{"q":"這本書我還沒看＿，下星期還你。","opts":["完","見","錯"],"a":0,"why":"Belum selesai membaca → 看完."},{"q":"對不起，我打＿電話了。","opts":["好","錯","掉"],"a":1,"why":"Salah sambung → 打錯."},{"q":"你看＿我的手機了嗎？","opts":["懂","完","到"],"a":2,"why":"Melihat dan menemukan → 看到."},{"q":"把壞掉的零件丟＿吧。","opts":["掉","懂","錯"],"a":0,"why":"Dibuang sampai hilang → 丟掉."}]},{"lv":4,"k":"b1_dc","form":"V + 上/下/進/出/回/過/起 + 來/去；V + 進/回 + 地點 + 來/去","icon":"arrows","name":["Komplemen arah: V進來/出去/回來","Directional complements: V進來/出去/回來","Directional complement: V進來/出去/回來"],"gloss":["Komplemen arah memberi tahu ke mana gerakan pergi. 來 = mendekat ke pembicara, 去 = menjauh. 上/下/進/出/回/過 = arah. Tempat diletakkan sebelum 來/去: 進教室來. Benda bisa diletakkan sebelum seluruh komplemen (買了一杯珍奶回來) atau di antara arah dan 來/去 (拿出一本書來).","Directional complements show where movement goes. 來 = toward the speaker, 去 = away. 上/下/進/出/回/過 = the direction. A place goes before 來/去: 進教室來. An object can come before the whole complement (買了一杯珍奶回來) or between the direction word and 來/去 (拿出一本書來).","Ipinapakita kung saan pupunta ang galaw. 來 = palapit sa nagsasalita, 去 = palayo. Ang lugar ay bago ang 來/去."],"tip":["Bayangkan kamera ada di tempat pembicara. Masuk ke kamera = 來, keluar dari kamera = 去.","Picture the camera at the speaker. Toward the camera = 來, away = 去.","Isipin ang kamera nasa nagsasalita: palapit = 來, palayo = 去."],"warn":["✗ 他進來教室。→ ✓ 他進教室來。/ 他走進教室。","✗ 他進來教室。→ ✓ 他進教室來。/ 他走進教室。","✗ 他進來教室。→ ✓ 他進教室來。/ 他走進教室。"],"logic":{"id":"Bahasa Indonesia biasanya cukup bilang 'masuk', 'keluar', 'naik'. Penutur Taiwan selalu menambahkan sudut pandang: apakah gerakan itu mendekat ke saya (來) atau menjauh (去)? 'Masuk!' dari dalam kelas = 進來; menyuruh orang masuk ke ruangan lain = 進去. Selain itu, verbanya menunjukkan cara bergerak (走, 跑, 拿, 帶) dan komplemennya menunjukkan arah. Jadi 'ambil keluar' = 拿出來, 'bawa pulang' = 帶回去.","en":"Indonesian usually just says 'masuk', 'keluar', 'naik'. Taiwanese speakers always add a viewpoint: is the movement coming toward me (來) or going away (去)? 'Come in!' from inside the room = 進來; telling someone to enter another room = 進去. The verb shows how you move (走, 跑, 拿, 帶) and the complement shows direction, so 'take out' = 拿出來, 'take back home' = 帶回去."},"ex":[["外面很熱，快進來吧！","wài miàn hěn rè kuài jìn lái ba","Di luar panas, ayo cepat masuk!","It's hot outside, come on in!","Mainit sa labas, pumasok ka na!","daily"],["他買了一杯珍奶回來。","tā mǎi le yì bēi zhēn nǎi huí lái","Dia pulang bawa segelas bubble tea.","He came back with a bubble tea.","Bumalik siya na may dalang milk tea.","daily"],["他跑上樓去了。","tā pǎo shàng lóu qù le","Dia lari naik ke lantai atas.","He ran upstairs.","Tumakbo siya paakyat.","daily"],["請把手機拿出來。","qǐng bǎ shǒu jī ná chū lái","Tolong keluarkan HP-nya.","Please take out your phone.","Pakilabas ang cellphone mo.","campus"],["用完的工具要放回去。","yòng wán de gōng jù yào fàng huí qù","Alat yang sudah dipakai harus dikembalikan.","Put tools back after you use them.","Ibalik ang mga gamit pagkatapos gamitin.","campus"],["工程師把晶圓從機台裡拿出來。","gōng chéng shī bǎ jīng yuán cóng jī tái lǐ ná chū lái","Insinyur mengeluarkan wafer dari dalam mesin.","The engineer took the wafer out of the tool.","Inilabas ng engineer ang wafer mula sa makina.","fab"],["主管走過來問我們怎麼了。","zhǔ guǎn zǒu guò lái wèn wǒ men zěn me le","Atasan menghampiri dan tanya ada apa.","The supervisor came over and asked what was wrong.","Lumapit ang supervisor at nagtanong kung ano ang nangyari.","fab"]],"drill":[{"q":"（你在樓上）媽媽在樓下叫你：「快下＿吃飯！」","opts":["來","去","過"],"a":0,"why":"Mendekat ke ibu (pembicara) → 下來."},{"q":"我在宿舍，室友在外面。我問他：「你什麼時候回＿？」","opts":["去","來","起"],"a":1,"why":"Kembali ke tempat pembicara → 回來."},{"q":"（你在教室裡）他走＿教室來。","opts":["上","出","進"],"a":2,"why":"Masuk ke kelas → 走進教室來."},{"q":"工具用完要放＿原來的地方。","opts":["回","起","過"],"a":0,"why":"Dikembalikan ke tempat asal → V + 回 + tempat: 放回原來的地方."}]},{"lv":4,"k":"b1_dcfig","form":"想起來／看出來／找出來／說下去／停下來／V/Vs + 起來（mulai）","icon":"sparkle","name":["Arah kiasan: 想起來, 看出來, 說下去","Figurative directions: 想起來, 看出來, 說下去","Matalinghagang direksyon: 想起來, 看出來, 說下去"],"gloss":["Komplemen arah juga punya makna abstrak. 起來 = muncul/mulai (想起來 teringat, 冷起來 mulai dingin, 好起來 membaik). 出來 = keluar dari 'tersembunyi' (看出來 bisa menangkap, 找出來 menemukan). 下去 = berlanjut (說下去). 下來 = berhenti/menetap (停下來, 安靜下來).","Directional complements also have abstract meanings. 起來 = come up/begin (想起來 recall, 冷起來 get cold, 好起來 improve). 出來 = come out of hiding (看出來 tell/notice, 找出來 find out). 下去 = keep going (說下去). 下來 = come to rest (停下來, 安靜下來).","May abstraktong kahulugan din: 起來 = lumitaw/magsimula, 出來 = lumabas sa tago, 下去 = magpatuloy, 下來 = huminto."],"tip":["起來 = naik ke permukaan pikiran/keadaan. 出來 = ditarik keluar dari tersembunyi. 下去 = jalan terus ke depan. 下來 = mendarat dan diam.","起來 = rises to the surface. 出來 = pulled out of hiding. 下去 = keeps rolling forward. 下來 = lands and settles.","起來 = umaakyat, 出來 = hinihila palabas, 下去 = tuloy, 下來 = lumalapag."],"warn":["✗ 我想出來他的名字了。→ ✓ 我想起來他的名字了。（想起來 = teringat; 想出來 = menemukan ide baru）","✗ 我想出來他的名字了。→ ✓ 我想起來他的名字了。(想起來 = recall; 想出來 = come up with something new)","✗ 我想出來他的名字了。→ ✓ 我想起來他的名字了。"],"logic":{"id":"Bahasa Indonesia memakai kata yang berbeda: 'teringat', 'ketahuan', 'lanjut', 'mulai'. Orang Taiwan memakai gambar gerakan yang sama seperti arah fisik. Ingatan yang tadinya tenggelam lalu 'naik' → 想起來. Penyebab masalah yang tersembunyi lalu 'keluar' → 找出來. Cerita yang 'menurun terus' ke depan → 說下去. Mesin yang bergerak lalu 'turun dan diam' → 停下來. Kalau kamu membayangkan gerakannya, kamu bisa menebak artinya.","en":"Indonesian uses different words: 'teringat', 'ketahuan', 'lanjut', 'mulai'. Taiwanese speakers reuse the same movement images as physical directions. A sunken memory 'rises up' → 想起來. A hidden cause 'comes out' → 找出來. A story 'rolls on down' → 說下去. A moving machine 'comes down and stops' → 停下來. Picture the movement and you can guess the meaning."},"ex":[["我想起來了！他叫阿明。","wǒ xiǎng qǐ lái le tā jiào ā míng","Aku ingat! Namanya A-Ming.","I remember now! His name is A-Ming.","Naalala ko na! A-Ming ang pangalan niya.","daily"],["天氣冷起來了。","tiān qì lěng qǐ lái le","Cuacanya mulai dingin.","It's getting cold.","Lumalamig na ang panahon.","daily"],["你再這樣熬夜下去，身體會受不了。","nǐ zài zhè yàng áo yè xià qù shēn tǐ huì shòu bù liǎo","Kalau kamu terus begadang begini, badanmu nggak akan kuat.","If you keep staying up like this, your body won't take it.","Kung magpupuyat ka pa nang ganyan, hindi kakayanin ng katawan mo.","daily"],["我看出來了，是電容裝反了。","wǒ kàn chū lái le shì diàn róng zhuāng fǎn le","Aku sudah lihat masalahnya, kapasitornya terpasang terbalik.","I can see it now: the capacitor is in backwards.","Nakita ko na, baligtad ang pagkakabit ng capacitor.","campus"],["請繼續說下去。","qǐng jì xù shuō xià qù","Silakan lanjutkan bicaranya.","Please go on.","Pakituloy mo ang sinasabi mo.","campus"],["異常的原因，我們終於找出來了。","yì cháng de yuán yīn wǒ men zhōng yú zhǎo chū lái le","Penyebab abnormalnya akhirnya kami temukan.","We finally found the cause of the abnormality.","Sa wakas, nahanap namin ang sanhi ng problema.","fab"],["良率慢慢好起來了。","liáng lǜ màn màn hǎo qǐ lái le","Yield pelan-pelan mulai membaik.","Yield is slowly getting better.","Unti-unting gumaganda ang yield.","fab"],["機台突然停下來了。","jī tái tú rán tíng xià lái le","Mesinnya tiba-tiba berhenti.","The tool suddenly stopped.","Biglang huminto ang makina.","fab"]],"drill":[{"q":"我忘了他的電話，現在想＿了！","opts":["起來","出來","下去"],"a":0,"why":"Teringat kembali → 想起來."},{"q":"你說得很好，請繼續說＿。","opts":["起來","下去","出來"],"a":1,"why":"Melanjutkan → 說下去."},{"q":"天氣熱＿了，可以穿短袖了。","opts":["下去","出來","起來"],"a":2,"why":"Keadaan mulai → Vs + 起來."},{"q":"你看得＿他今天心情不好嗎？","opts":["出來","起來","下來"],"a":0,"why":"Menangkap sesuatu yang tersembunyi → 看出來."}]},{"lv":4,"k":"b1_pc","form":"V + 得/不 + 補語（完/到/懂/了/見/動/清楚）","icon":"no","name":["Komplemen potensial: V得懂 / V不完","Potential complements: V得懂 / V不完","Potential complement: V得懂 / V不完"],"gloss":["Sisipkan 得 (bisa) atau 不 (tidak bisa) di antara verba dan komplemen hasil/arah: 聽得懂 = bisa paham, 做不完 = tidak bisa selesai, 去不了 = tidak bisa pergi (了 dibaca liǎo). Ini menyatakan apakah hasil BISA tercapai karena kondisi, bukan izin.","Insert 得 (can) or 不 (can't) between a verb and its result/direction complement: 聽得懂 = can understand, 做不完 = can't finish, 去不了 = can't go (了 read liǎo). It says whether the result CAN be reached given the conditions, not permission.","Isingit ang 得 (kaya) o 不 (hindi kaya) sa pagitan ng pandiwa at complement: 聽得懂, 做不完, 去不了. Tungkol ito sa kakayahan dahil sa kondisyon, hindi pahintulot."],"tip":["Ambil komplemen hasil (聽懂), sisipkan 得/不 di tengah (聽得懂/聽不懂). 了 liǎo = 'sanggup/bisa terjadi' secara umum.","Take a result compound (聽懂) and slip 得/不 into the middle (聽得懂/聽不懂). 了 liǎo = generic 'manage to'.","Kunin ang 聽懂, isingit ang 得/不: 聽得懂/聽不懂."],"warn":["✗ 我不能聽懂。→ ✓ 我聽不懂。","✗ 我不能聽懂。→ ✓ 我聽不懂。","✗ 我不能聽懂。→ ✓ 我聽不懂。"],"logic":{"id":"Orang Indonesia berpikir 'tidak bisa' + verba, lalu menerjemahkannya jadi 不能 + verba. Penutur Taiwan berpikir: aksinya dicoba, tapi hasilnya tidak tercapai. Jadi 'bisa/tidak bisa' disisipkan tepat di antara aksi dan hasil: 聽不懂 (sudah mendengar, tapi tidak sampai paham), 買不到 (mencari beli, tapi tidak dapat). 不能 lebih terasa 'tidak boleh' atau 'tidak memungkinkan karena aturan'. Di pabrik, 'stok part ini tidak ada' sangat alami diucapkan 這個零件買不到.","en":"Indonesians think 'tidak bisa' + verb and translate it as 不能 + verb. Taiwanese speakers think: the action is attempted, but the result isn't reached. So 'can / can't' slips right between the action and the result: 聽不懂 (heard it but didn't get to understanding), 買不到 (tried to buy, couldn't get it). 不能 feels more like 'not allowed' or ruled out. In a fab, 'we can't get this part' is naturally 這個零件買不到."},"ex":[["這麼多菜，我們吃得完嗎？","zhè me duō cài wǒ men chī de wán ma","Lauknya banyak banget, kita bisa habiskan nggak?","So many dishes — can we finish them?","Ang dami nito, mauubos ba natin?","daily"],["字太小了，我看不清楚。","zì tài xiǎo le wǒ kàn bù qīng chǔ","Tulisannya terlalu kecil, aku nggak bisa lihat jelas.","The text is too small, I can't see it clearly.","Masyadong maliit ang sulat, hindi ko makita nang malinaw.","daily"],["老師講得太快，我聽不懂。","lǎo shī jiǎng de tài kuài wǒ tīng bù dǒng","Dosennya bicara terlalu cepat, aku nggak paham.","The teacher talks too fast; I can't understand.","Masyadong mabilis magsalita ang guro, hindi ko maintindihan.","campus"],["這份報告我一個人做不完。","zhè fèn bào gào wǒ yí ge rén zuò bù wán","Laporan ini nggak bisa kuselesaikan sendirian.","I can't finish this report by myself.","Hindi ko kayang tapusin mag-isa ang report na ito.","campus"],["這個零件現在買不到。","zhè ge líng jiàn xiàn zài mǎi bú dào","Komponen ini sekarang nggak bisa dibeli (kosong).","This part can't be bought right now.","Hindi mabili ang pyesang ito ngayon.","fab"],["明天早班我去不了，可以換班嗎？","míng tiān zǎo bān wǒ qù bù liǎo kě yǐ huàn bān ma","Besok shift pagi aku nggak bisa datang, boleh tukar shift?","I can't make tomorrow's morning shift — can I swap?","Hindi ako makakapasok sa morning shift bukas, puwede bang magpalit?","fab"],["這台機台我們自己修得好嗎？","zhè tái jī tái wǒ men zì jǐ xiū de hǎo ma","Mesin ini bisa kita perbaiki sendiri nggak?","Can we fix this tool ourselves?","Kaya ba nating ayusin mag-isa ang makinang ito?","fab"]],"drill":[{"q":"他說台語，我聽＿懂。","opts":["沒","不","很"],"a":1,"why":"Tidak bisa paham → 聽不懂."},{"q":"東西太重了，我一個人拿＿動。","opts":["不","了","過"],"a":0,"why":"Tidak sanggup mengangkat → 拿不動."},{"q":"這麼多工作，今天做得＿嗎？","opts":["過","完","著"],"a":1,"why":"Bisa selesai? → 做得完."},{"q":"我明天有考試，去＿了你的生日派對。","opts":["得","沒","不"],"a":2,"why":"Tidak bisa pergi → 去不了 (liǎo)."}]},{"lv":4,"k":"b1_deobj","form":"(V) + O + V + 得 + (很) Vs ／ O + V + 得 + Vs","icon":"star","name":["Komplemen derajat dengan objek: 說中文說得…","Degree complement with an object: 說中文說得…","Degree complement na may object: 說中文說得…"],"gloss":["Untuk menilai BAGAIMANA sebuah aksi dilakukan, pakai V + 得 + Vs: 跑得很快. Kalau ada objek, verbanya diulang (說中文說得很好) atau objeknya ditaruh di depan (中文說得很好). 得 tidak boleh langsung setelah objek. Pertanyaannya: V得怎麼樣？","To judge HOW an action is done, use V + 得 + Vs: 跑得很快. With an object, repeat the verb (說中文說得很好) or move the object to the front (中文說得很好). 得 can't come straight after the object. Question form: V得怎麼樣？","Para husgahan KUNG PAANO ginawa ang kilos: V + 得 + Vs. Kapag may object, ulitin ang pandiwa o ilagay ang object sa unahan."],"tip":["得 harus menempel pada VERBA, bukan pada objek. Kalau objek menghalangi, panggil verbanya sekali lagi.","得 must hug the VERB, never the object. If the object is in the way, call the verb again.","Ang 得 ay laging kasunod ng PANDIWA."],"warn":["✗ 他說中文得很好。→ ✓ 他說中文說得很好。/ 他中文說得很好。","✗ 他說中文得很好。→ ✓ 他說中文說得很好。/ 他中文說得很好。","✗ 他說中文得很好。→ ✓ 他說中文說得很好。/ 他中文說得很好。"],"logic":{"id":"Bahasa Indonesia cukup menambah kata keterangan: 'dia bicara Mandarin dengan lancar'. Penutur Taiwan memandang penilaian sebagai komentar tentang verba, jadi komentar itu harus datang langsung setelah verba dengan 得. Objek tidak boleh menyela, maka verbanya diulang atau objek diangkat ke depan sebagai topik ('Mandarinnya, ngomongnya bagus'). Penilaian ini juga untuk kebiasaan atau hasil, bukan rencana: 你明天說得很好 tidak alami.","en":"Indonesian just adds an adverb: 'dia bicara Mandarin dengan lancar'. Taiwanese speakers treat the evaluation as a comment on the verb, so it must come right after the verb with 得. The object can't interrupt, so the verb is repeated or the object is raised to the front as a topic ('His Chinese — he speaks it well'). It evaluates habits or outcomes, not plans: 你明天說得很好 is unnatural."},"ex":[["你說中文說得很流利。","nǐ shuō zhōng wén shuō de hěn liú lì","Mandarinmu lancar banget.","You speak Chinese very fluently.","Matatas kang magsalita ng Chinese.","daily"],["他打籃球打得很好。","tā dǎ lán qiú dǎ de hěn hǎo","Dia jago main basket.","He plays basketball really well.","Magaling siyang maglaro ng basketball.","daily"],["我今天起得太晚了。","wǒ jīn tiān qǐ de tài wǎn le","Hari ini aku bangun terlalu siang.","I got up too late today.","Masyadong late akong nagising ngayon.","daily"],["他焊電路焊得很漂亮。","tā hàn diàn lù hàn de hěn piào liàng","Solderan rangkaiannya rapi banget.","His circuit soldering is really neat.","Napakaganda ng pag-solder niya ng circuit.","campus"],["老師講得很清楚，大家都懂了。","lǎo shī jiǎng de hěn qīng chǔ dà jiā dōu dǒng le","Dosen menjelaskan dengan jelas, semua paham.","The teacher explained clearly and everyone got it.","Malinaw ang paliwanag ng guro, naintindihan ng lahat.","campus"],["你報告寫得怎麼樣？","nǐ bào gào xiě de zěn me yàng","Laporanmu gimana, lancar nulisnya?","How's your report going?","Kumusta ang pagsulat mo ng report?","campus"],["她操作機台操作得很熟練。","tā cāo zuò jī tái cāo zuò de hěn shú liàn","Dia sangat mahir mengoperasikan mesin.","She operates the tool very skillfully.","Bihasa siyang mag-operate ng makina.","fab"],["這台機台跑得不太穩。","zhè tái jī tái pǎo de bú tài wěn","Mesin ini jalannya kurang stabil.","This tool isn't running very stably.","Hindi masyadong stable ang takbo ng makinang ito.","fab"]],"drill":[{"q":"他寫字寫＿很漂亮。","opts":["的","得","地"],"a":1,"why":"Objek ada → verba diulang, lalu V + 得 + Vs: 寫字寫得很漂亮."},{"q":"她唱歌唱＿很好聽。","opts":["得","了","著"],"a":0,"why":"Objek + verba diulang + 得."},{"q":"你打字打＿真快！","opts":["了","的","得"],"a":2,"why":"Verba diulang lalu 得 + Vs."},{"q":"我昨天睡得不＿，今天很累。","opts":["好","得","了"],"a":0,"why":"Negasi: V得 + 不 + Vs."}]},{"lv":3,"k":"b1_yidian","form":"一點（兒）也/都 + 不/沒 + V/Vs；一點 + N + 也/都 + 不/沒 + V","icon":"no","name":["一點也不 / 一點都不: sama sekali tidak","一點也不 / 一點都不: not at all","一點也不: hindi talaga"],"gloss":["一點也不 + Vs/V atau 一點都不 + Vs/V berarti 'sama sekali tidak'. Untuk aksi yang tidak terjadi, pakai 沒: 一點也沒吃. Benda bisa disisipkan: 一點灰塵都不能有. Pola ini hanya untuk kalimat negatif.","一點也不 / 一點都不 + Vs/V means 'not at all'. For actions that didn't happen, use 沒: 一點也沒吃. A noun can be inserted: 一點灰塵都不能有. The pattern is only for negative sentences.","Ang 一點也不 / 一點都不 ay 'hindi talaga'. Para sa kilos na hindi nangyari, gamitin ang 沒. Pang-negatibo lamang."],"tip":["Urutan tetap: 一點 → 也/都 → 不/沒 → kata sifat/verba. Seperti 'sedikit pun … tidak …'.","Fixed order: 一點 → 也/都 → 不/沒 → adjective/verb. Like 'not even a little'.","Ayos: 一點 → 也/都 → 不/沒 → salita."],"warn":["✗ 我不一點累。→ ✓ 我一點也不累。","✗ 我不一點累。→ ✓ 我一點也不累。","✗ 我不一點累。→ ✓ 我一點也不累。"],"logic":{"id":"Bahasa Indonesia bilang 'sama sekali tidak' atau 'sedikit pun tidak', dan urutan kata Mandarin justru mirip dengan 'sedikit pun tidak': ukurannya dulu, lalu 也/都 sebagai 'pun', lalu negasi. Jangan bingung dengan 有一點 (agak, negatif) dan V一點 (sedikit lebih). Penutur Taiwan memakai pola ini untuk menekankan dengan kuat, sering untuk membantah: 'Ini sama sekali nggak susah!' Di fab, 一點都不能錯 adalah cara tegas untuk bilang toleransi nol.","en":"Indonesian says 'sama sekali tidak' or 'sedikit pun tidak', and Mandarin word order matches 'sedikit pun tidak': the amount first, then 也/都 as 'even', then the negation. Don't confuse it with 有一點 (a bit, negative feeling) or V一點 (a little more). Taiwanese speakers use it for strong emphasis, often to push back: 'It's not hard at all!' In the fab, 一點都不能錯 is a firm way to say zero tolerance."},"ex":[["我一點都不累。","wǒ yì diǎn dōu bú lèi","Aku sama sekali nggak capek.","I'm not tired at all.","Hindi ako pagod kahit kaunti.","daily"],["今天的晚餐我一點都沒吃。","jīn tiān de wǎn cān wǒ yì diǎn dōu méi chī","Makan malam hari ini sama sekali nggak kusentuh.","I didn't eat any of tonight's dinner.","Hindi ko ginalaw ang hapunan ngayon.","daily"],["這個考試一點也不難。","zhè ge kǎo shì yì diǎn yě bù nán","Ujian ini sama sekali nggak susah.","This exam isn't hard at all.","Hindi mahirap ang exam na ito.","campus"],["他上台報告的時候一點也不緊張。","tā shàng tái bào gào de shí hòu yì diǎn yě bù jǐn zhāng","Waktu presentasi di depan dia sama sekali nggak gugup.","He wasn't nervous at all when presenting.","Hindi siya kinabahan nang mag-present siya.","campus"],["無塵室裡一點灰塵都不能有。","wú chén shì lǐ yì diǎn huī chén dōu bù néng yǒu","Di cleanroom nggak boleh ada debu sedikit pun.","There can't be even a speck of dust in the cleanroom.","Bawal kahit kaunting alikabok sa cleanroom.","fab"],["這個步驟一點都不能錯。","zhè ge bù zòu yì diǎn dōu bù néng cuò","Langkah ini sama sekali nggak boleh salah.","This step can't have even the slightest mistake.","Bawal magkamali kahit kaunti sa hakbang na ito.","fab"]],"drill":[{"q":"這家店的牛肉麵＿不好吃，別去。","opts":["一點也","也一點","一下"],"a":0,"why":"Sama sekali tidak → 一點也不."},{"q":"我一點＿不想去。","opts":["很","都","還"],"a":1,"why":"一點 + 都/也 + 不."},{"q":"他昨天一點也＿休息。","opts":["不","別","沒"],"a":2,"why":"Aksi yang tidak terjadi → 沒."},{"q":"這次的製程＿都不能出錯。","opts":["一點","一下","一次"],"a":0,"why":"一點都不能 = sama sekali tidak boleh."}]},{"lv":4,"k":"b1_huineng","form":"會 + V（keahlian dipelajari / kemungkinan）／ 能 + V（kemampuan / kondisi）／ 可以 + V（izin）","icon":"scale","name":["會 vs 能 vs 可以: tiga 'bisa'","會 vs 能 vs 可以: three kinds of 'can'","會 vs 能 vs 可以: tatlong 'kaya'"],"gloss":["會 = bisa karena sudah belajar (會騎機車) ATAU 'akan/mungkin' (明天會下雨). 能 = mampu karena kondisi fisik/situasi (手受傷了，不能寫字) atau kapasitas (一天能跑幾批). 可以 = boleh/diizinkan (可以用嗎？). Larangan biasanya 不可以 atau 不能.","會 = can because you've learned it (會騎機車) OR 'will/likely' (明天會下雨). 能 = able given physical condition/situation (手受傷了，不能寫字) or capacity (一天能跑幾批). 可以 = may/allowed (可以用嗎？). Prohibitions use 不可以 or 不能.","會 = marunong / malamang mangyari. 能 = kaya dahil sa kondisyon o kapasidad. 可以 = puwede / pinapayagan."],"tip":["會 = otak (sudah belajar) + ramalan. 能 = badan/kondisi. 可以 = satpam (izin).","會 = brain (learned) + forecast. 能 = body/conditions. 可以 = security guard (permission).","會 = utak + hula. 能 = katawan. 可以 = guwardiya."],"warn":["✗ 我的腳受傷了，不會走路。→ ✓ 我的腳受傷了，不能走路。","✗ 我的腳受傷了，不會走路。→ ✓ 我的腳受傷了，不能走路。","✗ 我的腳受傷了，不會走路。→ ✓ 我的腳受傷了，不能走路。"],"logic":{"id":"Bahasa Indonesia memakai 'bisa' untuk semua: bisa berenang, bisa datang, bisa pakai. Penutur Taiwan bertanya kenapa bisa. Karena sudah belajar → 會. Karena kondisi memungkinkan → 能. Karena diizinkan → 可以. Selain itu 會 juga untuk prediksi ('akan'), jadi 他不會來 berarti 'dia (kemungkinan) tidak akan datang', bukan 'dia tidak bisa datang'. Dalam percakapan Taiwan, 能 dan 可以 sering bertukar untuk permintaan, tapi 會 tidak pernah dipakai untuk izin.","en":"Indonesian uses 'bisa' for everything: can swim, can come, may use. Taiwanese speakers ask why it's possible. Learned skill → 會. Conditions allow it → 能. Permission → 可以. 會 is also for predictions, so 他不會來 means 'he (probably) won't come', not 'he can't come'. In everyday Taiwanese speech 能 and 可以 often swap in requests, but 會 is never used for permission."},"ex":[["明天會下雨，記得帶傘。","míng tiān huì xià yǔ jì de dài sǎn","Besok bakal hujan, jangan lupa bawa payung.","It's going to rain tomorrow, remember your umbrella.","Uulan bukas, magdala ka ng payong.","daily"],["我會騎機車，可是今天喝酒了，不能騎。","wǒ huì qí jī chē kě shì jīn tiān hē jiǔ le bù néng qí","Aku bisa naik motor, tapi hari ini minum alkohol, jadi nggak bisa nyetir.","I can ride a scooter, but I've been drinking today so I can't.","Marunong akong mag-motor, pero uminom ako ngayon kaya hindi puwede.","daily"],["老師，我可以用一下這台示波器嗎？","lǎo shī wǒ kě yǐ yòng yí xià zhè tái shì bō qì ma","Pak, boleh saya pakai osiloskop ini sebentar?","Teacher, may I use this oscilloscope for a moment?","Sir, puwede ko bang gamitin sandali ang oscilloscope?","campus"],["我的手受傷了，這星期不能做實驗。","wǒ de shǒu shòu shāng le zhè xīng qí bù néng zuò shí yàn","Tanganku terluka, minggu ini nggak bisa praktikum.","I hurt my hand, so I can't do labs this week.","Nasugatan ang kamay ko, hindi ako makakapag-eksperimento ngayong linggo.","campus"],["溫度太高，晶圓會壞掉。","wēn dù tài gāo jīng yuán huì huài diào","Kalau suhunya terlalu tinggi, wafernya bisa rusak.","If the temperature is too high, the wafer will be ruined.","Kapag masyadong mataas ang temperatura, masisira ang wafer.","fab"],["無塵室裡不可以吃東西。","wú chén shì lǐ bù kě yǐ chī dōng xī","Di dalam cleanroom tidak boleh makan.","You're not allowed to eat in the cleanroom.","Bawal kumain sa loob ng cleanroom.","fab"],["這台機台一天能跑幾批貨？","zhè tái jī tái yì tiān néng pǎo jǐ pī huò","Mesin ini sehari bisa jalan berapa lot?","How many lots can this tool run in a day?","Ilang lot ang kayang patakbuhin ng makinang ito sa isang araw?","fab"]],"drill":[{"q":"A：你＿說台語嗎？B：會一點。","opts":["會","可以","得"],"a":0,"why":"Jawabannya 會一點 → menanyakan keahlian hasil belajar → 會."},{"q":"老師，我＿用一下您的筆電嗎？","opts":["會","還","可以"],"a":2,"why":"Minta izin → 可以."},{"q":"天氣預報說晚上＿很冷。","opts":["能","會","可以"],"a":1,"why":"Prediksi → 會."},{"q":"我的腳受傷了，現在不＿走路。","opts":["會","能","得"],"a":1,"why":"Tidak mampu karena kondisi → 不能."}]},{"lv":3,"k":"b1_dei","form":"得／必須 + V（harus）vs 不用／不必 + V（tidak perlu）","icon":"bolt","name":["得 děi, 必須, 不用, 不必: harus vs tidak perlu","得 děi, 必須, 不用, 不必: must vs needn't","得 děi, 必須, 不用, 不必: kailangan vs hindi na kailangan"],"gloss":["得 (dibaca děi) = harus, sangat umum dalam percakapan. 必須 = harus, lebih formal/tegas (aturan, SOP). Lawannya bukan 不得 atau 不必須, tapi 不用 (santai) atau 不必 (sedikit formal) = tidak perlu.","得 (read děi) = have to, very common in speech. 必須 = must, more formal/strict (rules, procedures). The opposite is not 不得 or 不必須 but 不用 (casual) or 不必 (slightly formal) = don't need to.","Ang 得 (děi) = kailangan, karaniwan sa usapan. 必須 = dapat, mas pormal. Ang kabaligtaran ay 不用 o 不必 = hindi na kailangan."],"tip":["Harus: 得 (ngobrol) / 必須 (peraturan). Tidak perlu: 不用 (ngobrol) / 不必 (agak formal). 'Terima kasih' → 不用謝!","Must: 得 (chat) / 必須 (rules). Needn't: 不用 (chat) / 不必 (a bit formal). 'Thanks' → 不用謝!","Dapat: 得 / 必須. Hindi kailangan: 不用 / 不必."],"warn":["✗ 你不得來。(maksud: tidak perlu datang) → ✓ 你不用來。（不得 = dilarang, sangat formal）","✗ 你不得來。(meaning: needn't come) → ✓ 你不用來。(不得 = forbidden, very formal)","✗ 你不得來。→ ✓ 你不用來。"],"logic":{"id":"Dalam bahasa Indonesia, 'harus' dinegasikan menjadi 'tidak harus' atau 'tidak perlu'. Kalau langsung diterjemahkan, hasilnya 不得 — tapi di Taiwan 不得 adalah bahasa peraturan yang berarti 'dilarang'. Penutur Taiwan berpikir dengan pasangan: kewajiban (得/必須) vs kebutuhan yang hilang (不用/不必). Sering juga 得 dipakai untuk pamit: 我得走了 = aku harus pergi sekarang. Di pabrik, papan aturan memakai 必須, tapi teman kerja bilang 你得先…","en":"In Indonesian, 'harus' is negated as 'tidak harus' or 'tidak perlu'. A direct translation gives 不得 — but in Taiwan 不得 is rulebook language meaning 'forbidden'. Taiwanese speakers think in pairs: obligation (得/必須) vs no need (不用/不必). 得 is also how you excuse yourself: 我得走了 = I've got to go. In the fab, signs say 必須, but coworkers say 你得先…"},"ex":[["我得走了，九點要上班。","wǒ děi zǒu le jiǔ diǎn yào shàng bān","Aku harus pergi, jam sembilan masuk kerja.","I've got to go, I start work at nine.","Kailangan ko nang umalis, alas nuwebe ang pasok ko.","daily"],["不用謝！","bú yòng xiè","Sama-sama! (Nggak usah terima kasih.)","No need to thank me!","Walang anuman!","daily"],["明天要考試，今天晚上得好好準備。","míng tiān yào kǎo shì jīn tiān wǎn shàng děi hǎo hǎo zhǔn bèi","Besok ujian, malam ini harus belajar baik-baik.","There's an exam tomorrow, so I need to prepare properly tonight.","May exam bukas, kailangan kong mag-review nang mabuti ngayong gabi.","campus"],["這份作業不必寫太長，兩頁就夠了。","zhè fèn zuò yè bú bì xiě tài cháng liǎng yè jiù gòu le","Tugas ini nggak perlu panjang-panjang, dua halaman cukup.","This assignment needn't be long; two pages is enough.","Hindi kailangang mahaba ang assignment na ito, sapat na ang dalawang pahina.","campus"],["進無塵室以前，必須穿好無塵衣。","jìn wú chén shì yǐ qián bì xū chuān hǎo wú chén yī","Sebelum masuk cleanroom, wajib memakai baju cleanroom dengan benar.","Before entering the cleanroom, you must put on the bunny suit properly.","Bago pumasok sa cleanroom, dapat maayos ang suot na cleanroom suit.","fab"],["操作機台必須按照步驟來。","cāo zuò jī tái bì xū àn zhào bù zòu lái","Mengoperasikan mesin wajib sesuai langkah-langkahnya.","Operating the tool must follow the steps.","Dapat sundin ang mga hakbang sa pag-operate ng makina.","fab"],["你不用來了，我已經修好了。","nǐ bú yòng lái le wǒ yǐ jīng xiū hǎo le","Kamu nggak perlu datang, sudah kuperbaiki.","You don't need to come, I've already fixed it.","Hindi mo na kailangang pumunta, naayos ko na.","fab"]],"drill":[{"q":"很晚了，明天還要上課，我＿回家了。","opts":["得","不用","不必"],"a":0,"why":"Keharusan dalam percakapan → 得 děi."},{"q":"明天放假，你＿早起，可以睡晚一點。","opts":["得","必須","不用"],"a":2,"why":"Tidak perlu → 不用."},{"q":"在工廠裡，安全規定＿遵守。","opts":["不必","必須","不用"],"a":1,"why":"Aturan resmi → 必須."},{"q":"這個實驗很簡單，＿找學長幫忙。","opts":["不必","必須","得"],"a":0,"why":"Tidak perlu → 不必."}]},{"lv":3,"k":"b1_haoxiang","form":"好像 + 句子／看起來 + Vs/像…／聽起來 + Vs","icon":"wave","name":["好像, 看起來, 聽起來: sepertinya","好像, 看起來, 聽起來: seems / looks / sounds","好像, 看起來, 聽起來: parang / mukhang"],"gloss":["好像 = sepertinya (dugaan umum, dari info apa saja), diletakkan sebelum predikat. 看起來 = kelihatannya (berdasarkan penglihatan). 聽起來 = kedengarannya (berdasarkan suara atau cerita orang). Setelah 看起來/聽起來 langsung pakai kata sifat atau 像 + benda.","好像 = it seems (a general guess from any information), placed before the predicate. 看起來 = it looks (based on sight). 聽起來 = it sounds (based on sound or what someone said). After 看起來/聽起來 use an adjective directly, or 像 + noun.","Ang 好像 = parang (pangkalahatang hula). 看起來 = mukhang (batay sa nakikita). 聽起來 = parang (batay sa naririnig)."],"tip":["Mata → 看起來. Telinga/cerita → 聽起來. Firasat/umum → 好像.","Eyes → 看起來. Ears/story → 聽起來. Hunch/general → 好像.","Mata → 看起來. Tenga → 聽起來. Kutob → 好像."],"warn":["✗ 他看起來像很累。→ ✓ 他看起來很累。/ 他好像很累。","✗ 他看起來像很累。→ ✓ 他看起來很累。/ 他好像很累。","✗ 他看起來像很累。→ ✓ 他看起來很累。/ 他好像很累。"],"logic":{"id":"Bahasa Indonesia memakai 'kayaknya' untuk semua jenis dugaan. Penutur Taiwan sering menyebut sumber dugaannya: dari mata (看起來), dari telinga atau cerita orang (聽起來), atau sekadar perasaan (好像). Ini juga cara sopan untuk tidak terlalu tegas, misalnya saat melapor ke atasan: 良率好像比上個月低 terdengar lebih halus daripada langsung 良率比上個月低. 像 dipakai sebelum kata benda atau kalimat (看起來像學生, 聽起來像是馬達壞了), tidak langsung sebelum kata sifat.","en":"Indonesian uses 'kayaknya' for every kind of guess. Taiwanese speakers often name the source: eyes (看起來), ears or someone's account (聽起來), or just a feeling (好像). It's also a polite softener, e.g. reporting to a manager: 良率好像比上個月低 sounds gentler than a flat 良率比上個月低. 像 goes before a noun or a clause (看起來像學生, 聽起來像是馬達壞了), not directly before an adjective."},"ex":[["外面好像下雨了。","wài miàn hǎo xiàng xià yǔ le","Kayaknya di luar hujan.","It seems to be raining outside.","Parang umuulan sa labas.","daily"],["你看起來很累，昨天沒睡好嗎？","nǐ kàn qǐ lái hěn lèi zuó tiān méi shuì hǎo ma","Kamu kelihatan capek, semalam kurang tidur?","You look tired, didn't you sleep well?","Mukha kang pagod, hindi ka ba nakatulog nang maayos?","daily"],["這個計畫聽起來不錯。","zhè ge jì huà tīng qǐ lái bú cuò","Rencana ini kedengarannya bagus.","This plan sounds good.","Mukhang maganda ang planong ito.","campus"],["這個電路看起來很簡單，其實很難。","zhè ge diàn lù kàn qǐ lái hěn jiǎn dān qí shí hěn nán","Rangkaian ini kelihatannya simpel, padahal susah.","This circuit looks simple, but it's actually hard.","Mukhang simple ang circuit na ito, pero mahirap talaga.","campus"],["這台機台的聲音聽起來怪怪的。","zhè tái jī tái de shēng yīn tīng qǐ lái guài guài de","Suara mesin ini kedengarannya aneh.","This tool sounds a bit off.","Parang kakaiba ang tunog ng makinang ito.","fab"],["良率好像比上個月低。","liáng lǜ hǎo xiàng bǐ shàng ge yuè dī","Yield-nya sepertinya lebih rendah dari bulan lalu.","Yield seems lower than last month.","Parang mas mababa ang yield kaysa noong nakaraang buwan.","fab"],["他好像是新來的工程師。","tā hǎo xiàng shì xīn lái de gōng chéng shī","Kayaknya dia insinyur yang baru masuk.","He seems to be the new engineer.","Parang siya ang bagong engineer.","fab"]],"drill":[{"q":"這碗麵＿很好吃，我也想點一碗。","opts":["看起來","聽起來","想起來"],"a":0,"why":"Berdasarkan penglihatan → 看起來."},{"q":"你說的方法＿不錯，試試看吧。","opts":["看出來","聽起來","想起來"],"a":1,"why":"Berdasarkan cerita orang → 聽起來."},{"q":"他＿生病了，今天沒來上課。","opts":["好像","想起來","看出來"],"a":0,"why":"Dugaan umum → 好像."},{"q":"這個聲音＿像是馬達壞了。","opts":["看起來","好像","聽起來"],"a":2,"why":"Dari suara → 聽起來 (像 + benda/kalimat)."}]},{"lv":3,"k":"b1_kuaiyao","form":"快(要) + V/Vs + 了 ／ 時間 + 就要 + V + 了","icon":"clock","name":["快要…了 / 就要…了: sebentar lagi","快要…了 / 就要…了: about to","快要…了 / 就要…了: malapit na"],"gloss":["快…了 atau 快要…了 = sebentar lagi akan terjadi. 就要…了 juga 'segera', dan bisa dipakai bersama keterangan waktu spesifik (下星期就要考試了). 快要 TIDAK dipakai dengan waktu spesifik. 了 di akhir wajib.","快…了 / 快要…了 = something is about to happen. 就要…了 also means 'soon' and can take a specific time (下星期就要考試了). 快要 is NOT used with a specific time. The final 了 is required.","Ang 快要…了 = malapit nang mangyari. Ang 就要…了 ay puwedeng may tiyak na oras. Kailangan ang 了 sa dulo."],"tip":["Ada jam/tanggal? → 就要. Tidak ada? → 快要. Dan selalu tutup dengan 了.","Specific time? → 就要. None? → 快要. Always close with 了.","May oras? → 就要. Wala? → 快要. Laging may 了."],"warn":["✗ 明天快要考試了。→ ✓ 明天就要考試了。","✗ 明天快要考試了。→ ✓ 明天就要考試了。","✗ 明天快要考試了。→ ✓ 明天就要考試了。"],"logic":{"id":"Bahasa Indonesia cukup bilang 'sebentar lagi' atau 'hampir'. Penutur Taiwan membingkai kejadian yang akan datang sebagai 'keadaan baru yang hampir tiba', jadi kalimatnya ditutup dengan 了 — mirip 了2. Kalau mereka sudah menyebut waktunya (besok, jam delapan), mereka memakai 就要 karena 就 menghubungkan waktu dengan kejadian. 快 sendiri juga bisa dipakai dengan kata sifat: 手機快沒電了.","en":"Indonesian just says 'sebentar lagi' or 'hampir'. Taiwanese speakers frame an upcoming event as 'a new situation about to arrive', so the sentence closes with 了 — like 了2. Once they've named the time (tomorrow, at eight), they use 就要, because 就 links the time to the event. 快 also works with states: 手機快沒電了."},"ex":[["快下雨了，我們走吧。","kuài xià yǔ le wǒ men zǒu ba","Sebentar lagi hujan, ayo kita pergi.","It's about to rain, let's go.","Uulan na, tara na.","daily"],["電影快要開始了！","diàn yǐng kuài yào kāi shǐ le","Filmnya sebentar lagi mulai!","The movie's about to start!","Magsisimula na ang pelikula!","daily"],["手機快沒電了，我要充電。","shǒu jī kuài méi diàn le wǒ yào chōng diàn","HP-ku hampir habis baterai, aku mau ngecas.","My phone's almost dead, I need to charge it.","Malapit nang ma-lowbat ang cellphone ko, magcha-charge ako.","daily"],["下星期就要期中考了。","xià xīng qí jiù yào qí zhōng kǎo le","Minggu depan sudah UTS.","Midterms are next week.","Midterm exam na sa susunod na linggo.","campus"],["我們快要畢業了，要開始找工作了。","wǒ men kuài yào bì yè le yào kāi shǐ zhǎo gōng zuò le","Kita sebentar lagi lulus, harus mulai cari kerja.","We're about to graduate; time to start job hunting.","Malapit na kaming magtapos, kailangan nang maghanap ng trabaho.","campus"],["光阻快用完了，要趕快補。","guāng zǔ kuài yòng wán le yào gǎn kuài bǔ","Photoresist-nya hampir habis, harus cepat diisi ulang.","The photoresist is almost used up; we need to refill it fast.","Malapit nang maubos ang photoresist, kailangang dagdagan agad.","fab"],["晚上八點就要交接班了。","wǎn shàng bā diǎn jiù yào jiāo jiē bān le","Jam delapan malam sudah serah terima shift.","Shift handover is at 8 p.m.","Alas otso ng gabi ang handover ng shift.","fab"]],"drill":[{"q":"明天＿放假了，好開心！","opts":["快","就要","正在"],"a":1,"why":"Ada waktu spesifik (明天) → 就要."},{"q":"飛機快要起飛＿，請關手機。","opts":["了","過","著"],"a":0,"why":"快要…了 wajib 了."},{"q":"電池＿沒電了，先別用。","opts":["才","再","快"],"a":2,"why":"Hampir habis → 快…了."},{"q":"再五分鐘就要下班＿。","opts":["著","了","過"],"a":1,"why":"就要…了."}]},{"lv":3,"k":"b1_yijing","form":"已經 + V/Vs + 了 vs 還沒（有）+ V（呢）","icon":"check","name":["已經…了 / 還沒…呢: sudah vs belum","已經…了 / 還沒…呢: already vs not yet","已經…了 / 還沒…呢: na vs hindi pa"],"gloss":["已經…了 = sudah (terjadi atau tercapai). Lawannya 還沒 + V (+ 呢) = belum. Setelah 還沒 TIDAK boleh ada 了, karena belum ada perubahan. Jawaban singkat: 還沒(呢)。 / 已經…了。","已經…了 = already (happened or reached). The opposite is 還沒 + V (+ 呢) = not yet. No 了 after 還沒, because nothing has changed yet. Short answers: 還沒(呢)。 / 已經…了。","Ang 已經…了 = na. Ang kabaligtaran ay 還沒 + V (+ 呢) = hindi pa. Walang 了 pagkatapos ng 還沒."],"tip":["已經 dan 了 berpasangan seperti 'sudah'. 還沒 dan 呢 berpasangan seperti 'belum nih'.","已經 pairs with 了 like 'already'. 還沒 pairs with 呢 like 'not yet, still waiting'.","已經 + 了; 還沒 + 呢."],"warn":["✗ 我還沒吃飯了。→ ✓ 我還沒吃飯（呢）。","✗ 我還沒吃飯了。→ ✓ 我還沒吃飯（呢）。","✗ 我還沒吃飯了。→ ✓ 我還沒吃飯（呢）。"],"logic":{"id":"Pasangan 'sudah/belum' dalam bahasa Indonesia sangat mirip, jadi logikanya mudah. Satu-satunya jebakan adalah 了: karena 'sudah' terasa ada 了, orang Indonesia sering menempelkannya juga pada 'belum'. Bagi penutur Taiwan, 了 menandai perubahan yang sudah terjadi, padahal 還沒 justru berarti perubahan itu belum terjadi — maka keduanya bertentangan. 呢 menambah nuansa 'masih ditunggu'.","en":"Indonesian 'sudah / belum' maps very closely, so the logic is easy. The one trap is 了: since 'sudah' feels like 了, Indonesians often attach it to 'belum' too. For Taiwanese speakers, 了 marks a change that has happened, while 還沒 says exactly that the change hasn't happened — so they clash. 呢 adds a 'still waiting' feel."},"ex":[["我已經吃飽了。","wǒ yǐ jīng chī bǎo le","Aku sudah kenyang.","I'm already full.","Busog na ako.","daily"],["他還沒起床呢。","tā hái méi qǐ chuáng ne","Dia belum bangun nih.","He's not up yet.","Hindi pa siya gising.","daily"],["報告你交了嗎？還沒呢，明天交。","bào gào nǐ jiāo le ma hái méi ne míng tiān jiāo","Laporannya sudah dikumpul? Belum, besok.","Have you handed in the report? Not yet, tomorrow.","Naipasa mo na ba ang report? Hindi pa, bukas.","campus"],["實驗室已經關門了。","shí yàn shì yǐ jīng guān mén le","Labnya sudah tutup.","The lab has already closed.","Sarado na ang lab.","campus"],["工程師還沒到，機台還不能開。","gōng chéng shī hái méi dào jī tái hái bù néng kāi","Insinyurnya belum datang, mesinnya belum boleh dinyalakan.","The engineer isn't here yet, so the tool can't be started.","Wala pa ang engineer, hindi pa puwedeng buksan ang makina.","fab"],["這批晶圓已經跑完了。","zhè pī jīng yuán yǐ jīng pǎo wán le","Lot wafer ini sudah selesai diproses.","This lot of wafers has finished running.","Tapos nang patakbuhin ang batch ng wafer na ito.","fab"]],"drill":[{"q":"現在＿十二點了，快去睡覺！","opts":["已經","還沒","剛才"],"a":0,"why":"Sudah mencapai jam 12 → 已經…了."},{"q":"我還沒吃晚餐＿。","opts":["了","呢","過"],"a":1,"why":"還沒 + V + 呢, tanpa 了."},{"q":"A：機台修好了嗎？B：＿，還在等零件。","opts":["已經好了","還沒","就好了"],"a":1,"why":"Belum → 還沒."},{"q":"他已經回宿舍＿。","opts":["呢","著","了"],"a":2,"why":"已經…了."}]},{"lv":4,"k":"b1_gang","form":"主語 + 剛 + V（baru saja）／ 剛才（tadi）+ 主語 + V + 了","icon":"clock","name":["剛 vs 剛才: baru saja vs tadi","剛 vs 剛才: just vs a moment ago","剛 vs 剛才: kakatapos lang vs kanina"],"gloss":["剛 adalah adverbia: diletakkan setelah subjek, tepat sebelum verba, artinya 'baru saja' (relatif terhadap waktu bicara atau waktu lain). 剛 biasanya tidak memakai 了 di akhir. 剛才 adalah kata waktu 'tadi', bisa di awal kalimat, dan boleh memakai 了 atau negasi 沒.","剛 is an adverb: after the subject, right before the verb, meaning 'just' (relative to now or another time). 剛 usually takes no final 了. 剛才 is a time word 'a moment ago', can start the sentence, and can take 了 or a 沒 negative.","Ang 剛 ay pang-abay bago ang pandiwa = kakatapos lang. Ang 剛才 ay salitang oras = kanina, puwede sa unahan."],"tip":["剛 = menempel ke verba (剛到). 剛才 = 'tadi', bebas bergerak seperti 昨天.","剛 = glued to the verb (剛到). 剛才 = 'earlier', moves freely like 昨天.","剛 = dikit sa pandiwa. 剛才 = malayang gumalaw tulad ng 昨天."],"warn":["✗ 剛我吃飯。／ 我剛才來台灣的時候很不習慣。→ ✓ 我剛吃完飯。／ 我剛來台灣的時候很不習慣。","✗ 剛我吃飯。/ 我剛才來台灣的時候很不習慣。→ ✓ 我剛吃完飯。/ 我剛來台灣的時候很不習慣。","✗ 剛我吃飯。/ 我剛才來台灣的時候很不習慣。→ ✓ 我剛吃完飯。/ 我剛來台灣的時候很不習慣。"],"logic":{"id":"Bahasa Indonesia punya 'baru saja' dan 'tadi', dan pembagiannya mirip sekali. 剛 seperti 'baru saja': ia memodifikasi verba dan menekankan betapa dekatnya kejadian itu, jadi 了 tidak perlu. 剛才 seperti 'tadi': ia hanya titik waktu, sama seperti 昨天, sehingga kalimatnya diperlakukan seperti kejadian lampau biasa. Penutur Taiwan juga memakai 剛 untuk hal yang lebih lama, misalnya 我剛來台灣的時候 (waktu aku baru datang ke Taiwan) — 剛才 tidak bisa dipakai di sini.","en":"Indonesian has 'baru saja' and 'tadi', and the split is almost the same. 剛 is like 'baru saja': it modifies the verb and stresses how recent the event is, so no 了 is needed. 剛才 is like 'tadi': just a time point, like 昨天, so the sentence behaves like an ordinary past event. Taiwanese speakers also use 剛 for longer spans, e.g. 我剛來台灣的時候 (when I'd just come to Taiwan) — 剛才 can't be used there."},"ex":[["我剛到高雄，還不太認識路。","wǒ gāng dào gāo xióng hái bú tài rèn shì lù","Aku baru sampai di Kaohsiung, belum terlalu hafal jalan.","I've just arrived in Kaohsiung and don't know my way yet.","Kararating ko lang sa Kaohsiung, hindi ko pa kabisado ang daan.","daily"],["你剛才去哪裡了？","nǐ gāng cái qù nǎ lǐ le","Tadi kamu ke mana?","Where did you go just now?","Saan ka pumunta kanina?","daily"],["老師剛才說的，你聽懂了嗎？","lǎo shī gāng cái shuō de nǐ tīng dǒng le ma","Yang dosen bilang tadi, kamu paham?","Did you understand what the teacher said just now?","Naintindihan mo ba ang sinabi ng guro kanina?","campus"],["我剛開始學電子電路。","wǒ gāng kāi shǐ xué diàn zǐ diàn lù","Aku baru mulai belajar rangkaian elektronika.","I've just started learning electronic circuits.","Kakasimula ko lang mag-aral ng electronic circuits.","campus"],["機台剛保養完，先跑一片試試看。","jī tái gāng bǎo yǎng wán xiān pǎo yí piàn shì shì kàn","Mesinnya baru selesai PM, coba jalankan satu wafer dulu.","The tool just finished PM; run one wafer first to test.","Kakatapos lang ng PM ng makina, subukan munang magpatakbo ng isa.","fab"],["剛才那台機台當機了，現在好了。","gāng cái nà tái jī tái dàng jī le xiàn zài hǎo le","Tadi mesin itu hang, sekarang sudah normal.","That tool crashed a moment ago, but it's fine now.","Nag-hang ang makinang iyon kanina, ayos na ngayon.","fab"]],"drill":[{"q":"我＿下課，等一下就過去。","opts":["剛","快要","已經"],"a":0,"why":"Setelah subjek, sebelum verba, 'baru saja' → 剛."},{"q":"＿你說什麼？我沒聽清楚。","opts":["剛","剛才","已經"],"a":1,"why":"Kata waktu di awal kalimat → 剛才."},{"q":"我＿來台灣的時候，一句中文都不會說。","opts":["剛","剛才","已經"],"a":0,"why":"'Waktu baru datang' (periode yang lebih panjang) → 剛來…的時候; 剛才 hanya 'tadi'."},{"q":"我＿看到學長在實驗室。","opts":["剛才","快要","就要"],"a":0,"why":"Kejadian tadi → 剛才."}]},{"lv":4,"k":"b1_yijiu","form":"主語 + 一 + V1，(主語) + 就 + V2","icon":"bolt","name":["一…就…: begitu … langsung …","一…就…: as soon as …","一…就…: pagka… agad…"],"gloss":["一 + V1，就 + V2 berarti 'begitu V1, langsung V2'. Bisa untuk satu kejadian (一到家就洗澡) atau kebiasaan/aturan (一喝酒就臉紅, 一有異常就要通知主管). 一 diletakkan setelah subjek, 就 sebelum verba kedua.","一 + V1，就 + V2 means 'as soon as V1, then V2'. It works for one event (一到家就洗澡) or a habit/rule (一喝酒就臉紅, 一有異常就要通知主管). 一 goes after the subject, 就 before the second verb.","Ang 一 + V1，就 + V2 = pagka-V1, agad V2. Para sa isang pangyayari o nakagawian. Ang 一 ay pagkatapos ng paksa."],"tip":["一 = pelatuk, 就 = langsung meledak. Dua-duanya menempel ke verba, bukan ke awal kalimat.","一 = trigger, 就 = instant reaction. Both attach to verbs, not the start of the sentence.","一 = gatilyo, 就 = agad na reaksyon."],"warn":["✗ 一我到家，就洗澡。→ ✓ 我一到家就洗澡。","✗ 一我到家，就洗澡。→ ✓ 我一到家就洗澡。","✗ 一我到家，就洗澡。→ ✓ 我一到家就洗澡。"],"logic":{"id":"Orang Indonesia bilang 'begitu sampai rumah, aku mandi' dan menaruh 'begitu' di depan seperti kata sambung. Dalam Mandarin, 一 dan 就 adalah adverbia, jadi harus berada setelah subjek dan langsung sebelum verba masing-masing. Bayangkan dua verba dihubungkan per kabel: 一 di verba pertama, 就 di verba kedua. Kalau subjeknya berbeda, masing-masing subjek tetap di depan: 老師一講，我就懂了. Di pabrik, pola ini sering untuk aturan reaksi cepat.","en":"Indonesians say 'begitu sampai rumah, aku mandi' and put 'begitu' first like a conjunction. In Mandarin 一 and 就 are adverbs, so each sits after its subject, right before its verb. Picture two verbs wired together: 一 on the first, 就 on the second. If the subjects differ, each subject stays in front: 老師一講，我就懂了. In the fab this pattern is common for quick-response rules."},"ex":[["我一到家就洗澡。","wǒ yí dào jiā jiù xǐ zǎo","Begitu sampai rumah aku langsung mandi.","As soon as I get home, I shower.","Pagdating ko sa bahay, naliligo agad ako.","daily"],["他一喝酒就臉紅。","tā yì hē jiǔ jiù liǎn hóng","Dia begitu minum alkohol langsung mukanya merah.","His face turns red as soon as he drinks.","Pagkainom niya, namumula agad ang mukha niya.","daily"],["老師一講，我就懂了。","lǎo shī yì jiǎng wǒ jiù dǒng le","Begitu dosen menjelaskan, aku langsung paham.","As soon as the teacher explained, I got it.","Pagkapaliwanag ng guro, naintindihan ko agad.","campus"],["一下課，大家就跑去吃飯。","yí xià kè dà jiā jiù pǎo qù chī fàn","Begitu kelas selesai, semua langsung lari cari makan.","As soon as class ends, everyone rushes off to eat.","Pagkatapos ng klase, nagtakbuhan agad lahat para kumain.","campus"],["機台一開機就出現警報。","jī tái yì kāi jī jiù chū xiàn jǐng bào","Begitu mesin dinyalakan langsung muncul alarm.","The alarm goes off as soon as the tool is powered on.","Pagbukas ng makina, may alarma agad.","fab"],["一有異常，就要馬上通知主管。","yì yǒu yì cháng jiù yào mǎ shàng tōng zhī zhǔ guǎn","Begitu ada abnormal, harus segera lapor atasan.","As soon as there's an abnormality, notify the supervisor immediately.","Kapag may problema, ipaalam agad sa supervisor.","fab"]],"drill":[{"q":"他＿看到蟑螂就大叫。","opts":["一","就","才"],"a":0,"why":"一 + V1 … 就 + V2."},{"q":"我一起床＿喝咖啡。","opts":["才","就","再"],"a":1,"why":"Langsung → 就."},{"q":"這台機台＿過熱就會自動停下來。","opts":["就","再","一"],"a":2,"why":"Pemicu → 一."},{"q":"下班時間＿到，他就走了。","opts":["一","才","又"],"a":0,"why":"一 + 到, 就 + 走."}]},{"lv":3,"k":"b1_xian","form":"先 + V1，然後 + V2，最後 + V3","icon":"path","name":["先…然後…最後: urutan langkah","先…然後…最後: sequencing steps","先…然後…最後: pagkakasunod ng hakbang"],"gloss":["先 = pertama/dulu, diletakkan SEBELUM verba. 然後 = lalu/kemudian, di awal klausa berikutnya. 最後 = terakhir. Pola ini sangat berguna untuk menjelaskan prosedur, arah jalan, atau langkah praktikum dan SOP.","先 = first, placed BEFORE the verb. 然後 = then, at the start of the next clause. 最後 = finally. Very useful for explaining procedures, directions, or lab and SOP steps.","Ang 先 = una, BAGO ang pandiwa. 然後 = pagkatapos. 最後 = sa huli. Magagamit sa paliwanag ng proseso."],"tip":["'Makan dulu' ≠ 吃飯先. Dalam Mandarin 'dulu' maju ke depan: 先吃飯.","Indonesian 'makan dulu' puts 'dulu' last; Mandarin moves it forward: 先吃飯.","Sa Mandarin, ang 'muna' ay nasa unahan: 先吃飯."],"warn":["✗ 我吃飯先，然後看電影。→ ✓ 我先吃飯，然後看電影。","✗ 我吃飯先，然後看電影。→ ✓ 我先吃飯，然後看電影。","✗ 我吃飯先，然後看電影。→ ✓ 我先吃飯，然後看電影。"],"logic":{"id":"Dalam bahasa Indonesia, 'dulu' diletakkan di akhir: 'makan dulu, baru nonton'. Logika Mandarin adalah 'keterangan sebelum verba', jadi 先 harus datang sebelum aksinya, sama seperti 已經 atau 一起. Penutur Taiwan menjelaskan prosedur dengan rantai yang rapi: 先…，然後…，最後…; untuk langkah terakhir yang menjadi syarat, sering ditambah 才: 最後才能進去. Di lab dan fab, urutan ini bukan sekadar gaya bicara — urutan yang salah bisa berbahaya.","en":"In Indonesian, 'dulu' (first) goes at the end: 'makan dulu, baru nonton'. Mandarin logic is 'adverbs before the verb', so 先 must come before the action, just like 已經 or 一起. Taiwanese speakers explain procedures as a neat chain: 先…，然後…，最後…; for a final step that depends on the others they often add 才: 最後才能進去. In the lab and fab, the order isn't just style — the wrong order can be dangerous."},"ex":[["我們先吃飯，然後去看電影。","wǒ men xiān chī fàn rán hòu qù kàn diàn yǐng","Kita makan dulu, lalu nonton.","Let's eat first and then see a movie.","Kumain muna tayo, tapos manood ng sine.","daily"],["先坐捷運，然後轉公車，最後走五分鐘就到了。","xiān zuò jié yùn rán hòu zhuǎn gōng chē zuì hòu zǒu wǔ fēn zhōng jiù dào le","Naik MRT dulu, lalu ganti bus, terakhir jalan lima menit, sampai deh.","Take the MRT first, then change to a bus, and finally walk five minutes.","Sumakay muna ng MRT, lumipat sa bus, tapos maglakad nang limang minuto.","daily"],["先把電源關掉，然後再拆零件。","xiān bǎ diàn yuán guān diào rán hòu zài chāi líng jiàn","Matikan dulu sumber listriknya, baru bongkar komponennya.","Turn off the power first, then remove the parts.","Patayin muna ang power, saka tanggalin ang pyesa.","campus"],["做實驗的時候，先看說明書，然後接電路，最後量電壓。","zuò shí yàn de shí hòu xiān kàn shuō míng shū rán hòu jiē diàn lù zuì hòu liáng diàn yā","Saat praktikum, baca manual dulu, lalu rangkai sirkuit, terakhir ukur tegangan.","In the lab, read the manual first, then wire the circuit, and finally measure the voltage.","Sa eksperimento, basahin muna ang manual, ikabit ang circuit, tapos sukatin ang boltahe.","campus"],["進無塵室要先穿無塵衣，然後戴手套，最後過風淋室。","jìn wú chén shì yào xiān chuān wú chén yī rán hòu dài shǒu tào zuì hòu guò fēng lín shì","Masuk cleanroom: pakai baju cleanroom dulu, lalu sarung tangan, terakhir lewat air shower.","To enter the cleanroom: suit up first, then gloves, and finally go through the air shower.","Bago pumasok sa cleanroom: magsuot ng suit, tapos gloves, at dumaan sa air shower.","fab"],["機台異常的時候，先停機，然後通知工程師。","jī tái yì cháng de shí hòu xiān tíng jī rán hòu tōng zhī gōng chéng shī","Kalau mesin abnormal, hentikan mesin dulu, lalu hubungi insinyur.","When a tool goes abnormal, stop it first, then notify the engineer.","Kapag may problema ang makina, ihinto muna, tapos tawagan ang engineer.","fab"]],"drill":[{"q":"我們＿去買票，然後去吃飯。","opts":["先","最後","然後"],"a":0,"why":"Langkah pertama → 先 sebelum verba."},{"q":"先洗手，＿吃飯。","opts":["最先","然後","以前"],"a":1,"why":"Langkah berikutnya → 然後."},{"q":"先開電源，然後暖機，＿開始跑貨。","opts":["先","然後先","最後"],"a":2,"why":"Langkah terakhir → 最後."},{"q":"你＿休息一下，等一下再做。","opts":["先","最後","後來"],"a":0,"why":"'Istirahat dulu' → 先休息."}]},{"lv":4,"k":"b1_shide","form":"主語 + (是) + 時間/地點/方式/人 + V + 的 (+ O)","icon":"target","name":["是…的: menekankan kapan/di mana/bagaimana","是…的: focusing on when/where/how","是…的: pagdiin sa kailan/saan/paano"],"gloss":["Kalau kejadian di masa lalu sudah diketahui, dan yang ingin ditanyakan/ditekankan adalah KAPAN, DI MANA, BAGAIMANA, atau DENGAN SIAPA, pakai 是…的. Informasi fokus diletakkan setelah 是, lalu verba dan 的 di akhir. Dalam percakapan, 是 sering dihilangkan, tapi 的 tetap ada. Negasinya 不是…的.","When a past event is already known and you want to ask about or stress WHEN, WHERE, HOW, or WITH WHOM, use 是…的. The focus goes right after 是, then the verb, then 的 at the end. In speech 是 is often dropped, but 的 stays. Negative: 不是…的.","Kapag alam na ang nangyari at gusto mong idiin kung KAILAN, SAAN, PAANO o KANINO, gamitin ang 是…的."],"tip":["是 = lampu sorot, arahkan ke detail yang penting. 的 = 'ini kejadian lampau yang sudah jelas'.","是 = spotlight on the key detail. 的 = 'this is a known past event'.","是 = spotlight sa detalye. 的 = nakaraang pangyayari."],"warn":["✗ 我是去年來台灣了。→ ✓ 我是去年來台灣的。","✗ 我是去年來台灣了。→ ✓ 我是去年來台灣的。","✗ 我是去年來台灣了。→ ✓ 我是去年來台灣的。"],"logic":{"id":"Bahasa Indonesia menekankan dengan intonasi atau partikel '-nya': 'Datangnya kapan?' 'Datangnya naik apa?'. Itu persis logika 是…的: kejadiannya sudah diketahui (kamu sudah datang), yang baru hanyalah detailnya. Jadi orang Taiwan tidak memakai 了, karena 了 melaporkan kejadian baru, sedangkan di sini kejadian itu bukan berita. Kalau kamu mendengar pertanyaan dengan 是…的, jawab juga dengan 是…的. Di pabrik, ini dipakai untuk menelusuri: 是什麼時候發現的？是在哪一站發生的？","en":"Indonesian stresses with intonation or '-nya': 'Datangnya kapan?' (When was it you came?). That's exactly the 是…的 logic: the event is known (you've come), only the detail is new. So Taiwanese speakers don't use 了, because 了 reports new events and here the event isn't news. If you're asked with 是…的, answer with 是…的. In the fab it's used for tracing: 是什麼時候發現的？是在哪一站發生的？"},"ex":[["你是什麼時候來台灣的？","nǐ shì shén me shí hòu lái tái wān de","Kamu datang ke Taiwan kapan?","When did you come to Taiwan?","Kailan ka dumating sa Taiwan?","daily"],["我是去年九月來的。","wǒ shì qù nián jiǔ yuè lái de","Aku datangnya September tahun lalu.","I came last September.","Noong Setyembre noong isang taon ako dumating.","daily"],["我不是坐公車來的，是走路來的。","wǒ bú shì zuò gōng chē lái de shì zǒu lù lái de","Aku datangnya bukan naik bus, tapi jalan kaki.","I didn't come by bus — I walked.","Hindi ako nag-bus, naglakad ako papunta.","daily"],["你是怎麼來學校的？我是騎機車來的。","nǐ shì zěn me lái xué xiào de wǒ shì qí jī chē lái de","Kamu ke kampus naik apa? Aku naik motor.","How did you get to school? I came by scooter.","Paano ka pumunta sa school? Nag-motor ako.","campus"],["這個電路是誰焊的？焊得很好！","zhè ge diàn lù shì shéi hàn de hàn de hěn hǎo","Rangkaian ini siapa yang menyolder? Bagus banget!","Who soldered this circuit? It's really good!","Sino ang nag-solder ng circuit na ito? Ang ganda!","campus"],["異常是昨天晚上發現的。","yì cháng shì zuó tiān wǎn shàng fā xiàn de","Abnormalnya ditemukan tadi malam.","The abnormality was found last night.","Kagabi natuklasan ang problema.","fab"],["這個問題是在哪一站發生的？","zhè ge wèn tí shì zài nǎ yí zhàn fā shēng de","Masalah ini terjadinya di step proses mana?","At which process step did this problem occur?","Sa aling station nangyari ang problemang ito?","fab"]],"drill":[{"q":"你是在哪裡學中文＿？","opts":["的","了","過"],"a":0,"why":"是…的 menanyakan tempat kejadian lampau."},{"q":"我＿坐高鐵來的。","opts":["在","是","有"],"a":1,"why":"是 + cara + V + 的."},{"q":"這台機台是上個月裝＿。","opts":["了","過","的"],"a":2,"why":"Fokus waktu → 是…的, bukan 了."},{"q":"A：你是跟誰去的？B：我是跟同學去＿。","opts":["的","了","著"],"a":0,"why":"Jawab dengan pola yang sama: 是…的."}]},{"lv":3,"k":"b1_dongliang","form":"V + (了/過) + 數字 + 次／下／趟／遍 (+ O)；V + 代名詞 + 一下","icon":"layers","name":["Kata ukur aksi: 一次, 一下, 一趟, 一遍","Verbal measure words: 一次, 一下, 一趟, 一遍","Bilang ng kilos: 一次, 一下, 一趟, 一遍"],"gloss":["Untuk menghitung berapa kali aksi terjadi, kata ukur aksi diletakkan SETELAH verba. 次 = kali (umum). 一下 = sebentar/coba (melunakkan permintaan). 趟 = sekali bolak-balik pergi ke suatu tempat. 遍 = sekali dari awal sampai akhir (membaca, menonton, mengecek). Kata ganti diletakkan sebelum: 等我一下.","To count how many times an action happens, the verbal measure word goes AFTER the verb. 次 = times (general). 一下 = briefly/have a go (softens requests). 趟 = one round trip to a place. 遍 = once from start to finish (reading, watching, checking). Pronouns go before it: 等我一下.","Para bilangin ang kilos, ilagay ang measure word PAGKATAPOS ng pandiwa. 次 = beses, 一下 = sandali, 趟 = isang biyahe, 遍 = mula simula hanggang dulo."],"tip":["次 = hitung kejadian. 趟 = hitung perjalanan. 遍 = hitung putaran penuh. 一下 = bikin sopan.","次 = count events. 趟 = count trips. 遍 = count full passes. 一下 = makes it polite.","次 = pangyayari, 趟 = biyahe, 遍 = buong ikot, 一下 = magalang."],"warn":["✗ 我一次去過日本。→ ✓ 我去過日本一次。","✗ 我一次去過日本。→ ✓ 我去過日本一次。","✗ 我一次去過日本。→ ✓ 我去過日本一次。"],"logic":{"id":"Bahasa Indonesia meletakkan 'sekali' cukup bebas dan tidak membedakan jenisnya. Penutur Taiwan memperlakukan jumlah aksi seperti durasi: sebuah ukuran yang menempel di belakang verba. Mereka juga memilih kata ukur sesuai bentuk aksinya: perjalanan (趟), putaran lengkap (遍), atau kejadian biasa (次). 一下 sangat penting secara sosial: 你可以幫我看一下嗎？ terdengar jauh lebih ramah daripada 你可以幫我看嗎？","en":"Indonesian places 'sekali' fairly freely and doesn't distinguish types. Taiwanese speakers treat the number of actions like duration: a measurement attached after the verb. They also pick the measure word by the shape of the action: a trip (趟), a full pass (遍), or a plain occurrence (次). 一下 matters socially: 你可以幫我看一下嗎？ sounds much friendlier than 你可以幫我看嗎？"},"ex":[["等我一下，我馬上來。","děng wǒ yí xià wǒ mǎ shàng lái","Tunggu aku sebentar, aku segera datang.","Wait for me a sec, I'll be right there.","Hintayin mo ako sandali, papunta na ako.","daily"],["我去過日本兩次。","wǒ qù guò rì běn liǎng cì","Aku pernah ke Jepang dua kali.","I've been to Japan twice.","Dalawang beses na akong nakapunta sa Japan.","daily"],["我下個月要回印尼一趟。","wǒ xià ge yuè yào huí yìn ní yí tàng","Bulan depan aku mau pulang ke Indonesia sebentar.","I'm making a trip back to Indonesia next month.","Uuwi ako sa Indonesia sa susunod na buwan.","daily"],["請把這段再念一遍。","qǐng bǎ zhè duàn zài niàn yí biàn","Tolong baca bagian ini sekali lagi dari awal.","Please read this passage through once more.","Pakibasa ulit ang bahaging ito.","campus"],["你可以幫我看一下這個電路嗎？","nǐ kě yǐ bāng wǒ kàn yí xià zhè ge diàn lù ma","Bisa tolong lihat sebentar rangkaian ini?","Could you take a quick look at this circuit for me?","Puwede mo bang tingnan sandali ang circuit na ito?","campus"],["這個步驟要再確認一遍。","zhè ge bù zòu yào zài què rèn yí biàn","Langkah ini harus dicek ulang sekali lagi.","This step needs to be checked through again.","Kailangang i-check ulit ang hakbang na ito.","fab"],["我得去倉庫一趟拿零件。","wǒ děi qù cāng kù yí tàng ná líng jiàn","Aku harus ke gudang sebentar ambil komponen.","I have to make a run to the warehouse for parts.","Kailangan kong pumunta sa bodega para kumuha ng pyesa.","fab"],["這台機台一天要巡兩次。","zhè tái jī tái yì tiān yào xún liǎng cì","Mesin ini harus dipatroli dua kali sehari.","This tool must be checked on twice a day.","Dalawang beses sa isang araw dapat inspeksyunin ang makinang ito.","fab"]],"drill":[{"q":"這部電影很好看，我看了三＿。","opts":["次","趟","條"],"a":0,"why":"Menghitung kejadian → 次."},{"q":"你等我＿，我拿個東西。","opts":["一遍","一下","一趟"],"a":1,"why":"Sebentar → 一下, setelah kata ganti."},{"q":"這週末我要回台北＿。","opts":["一遍","一趟","一點"],"a":1,"why":"Perjalanan pergi-pulang → 一趟."},{"q":"老師說的話，請你再說＿。","opts":["一遍","一趟","一條"],"a":0,"why":"Sekali dari awal sampai akhir → 一遍."}]},{"lv":4,"k":"b1x_budan","form":"S + 不但 + A，而且 + (還／也) + B","icon":"layers","name":["Bukan hanya…, tapi juga… (不但…而且)","Not only… but also… (不但…而且)","Hindi lang…, kundi pati… (不但…而且)"],"gloss":["Dipakai untuk menambah informasi: bagian kedua (B) memberi poin tambahan yang biasanya lebih kuat. Kalau subjek A dan B sama, subjek ditaruh sekali di depan, SEBELUM 不但. Dalam lisan, setelah 而且 sering ditambah 還 atau 也.","Adds information: the second part (B) gives an extra, usually stronger point. If both parts share the subject, the subject comes once, BEFORE 不但. In speech 而且 is often followed by 還 or 也.","Ginagamit para magdagdag ng impormasyon; mas matindi kadalasan ang ikalawang bahagi (B). Kung iisa ang paksa, ilagay ito bago ang 不但. Sa pananalita, madalas may 還 o 也 pagkatapos ng 而且."],"tip":["Bayangkan tangga: 不但 = anak tangga pertama, 而且還 = naik satu lagi. Rumus aman: [subjek] 不但…，而且還…","Think of stairs: 不但 = first step, 而且還 = one step higher. Safe formula: [subject] 不但…，而且還…","Isipin ang hagdan: 不但 = unang baitang, 而且還 = isa pang baitang. Ligtas na pormula: [paksa] 不但…，而且還…"],"warn":["✗ 不但他會修機台，而且他會寫程式。→ ✓ 他不但會修機台，而且還會寫程式。","✗ 不但他會修機台，而且他會寫程式。→ ✓ 他不但會修機台，而且還會寫程式。","✗ 不但他會修機台，而且他會寫程式。→ ✓ 他不但會修機台，而且還會寫程式。"],"logic":{"id":"Orang Indonesia bilang 'Dia bukan hanya pintar, tapi juga rajin' — urutannya mirip. Bedanya, penutur Taiwan sangat memperhatikan posisi subjek: kalau subjeknya sama, subjek muncul sekali di depan lalu 不但 menempel pada predikat. Kalau subjeknya berbeda, barulah 不但 ditaruh sebelum subjek pertama. Mereka juga hampir selalu 'menguatkan' bagian kedua dengan 還 atau 也, jadi pikirkan: fakta 1 → fakta 2 yang lebih.","en":"English 'not only… but also' is similar. The key difference is subject position: with one shared subject, it appears once at the front and 不但 attaches to the predicate; only with different subjects does 不但 go before the first subject. Taiwanese speakers almost always reinforce the second part with 還 or 也: fact 1 → an even stronger fact 2."},"ex":[["這家便當店不但便宜，而且很好吃。","zhè jiā biàn dāng diàn bú dàn pián yí ér qiě hěn hǎo chī","Toko bento ini bukan hanya murah, tapi juga enak.","This bento shop is not only cheap but also delicious.","Hindi lang mura ang bento shop na ito, masarap pa.","daily"],["我室友不但會煮飯，而且還會修機車。","wǒ shì yǒu bú dàn huì zhǔ fàn ér qiě hái huì xiū jī chē","Teman sekamarku bukan cuma bisa masak, tapi juga bisa benerin motor.","My roommate can not only cook but also fix scooters.","Ang kasama ko sa kuwarto ay marunong magluto at mag-ayos pa ng motor.","daily"],["陳老師的課不但有理論，而且還有很多實驗。","chén lǎo shī de kè bú dàn yǒu lǐ lùn ér qiě hái yǒu hěn duō shí yàn","Kelas Pak Chen bukan hanya teori, tapi juga banyak praktikum.","Professor Chen's class has not only theory but also lots of lab work.","Ang klase ni Prof. Chen ay may teorya at marami pang eksperimento.","campus"],["這個感測器不但便宜，而且很容易裝。","zhè ge gǎn cè qì bú dàn pián yí ér qiě hěn róng yì zhuāng","Sensor ini bukan hanya murah, tapi juga gampang dipasang.","This sensor is not only cheap but also easy to install.","Hindi lang mura ang sensor na ito, madali pang ikabit.","campus"],["這台機台不但當機，而且良率也變差了。","zhè tái jī tái bú dàn dāng jī ér qiě liáng lǜ yě biàn chà le","Mesin ini bukan cuma hang, yield-nya juga jadi jelek.","This tool not only crashed, its yield also got worse.","Hindi lang nag-hang ang makinang ito, bumaba pa ang yield.","fab"],["他不但準時交接班，而且每次都寫得很清楚。","tā bú dàn zhǔn shí jiāo jiē bān ér qiě měi cì dōu xiě de hěn qīng chǔ","Dia bukan cuma tepat waktu serah terima shift, tapi catatannya selalu jelas.","He not only does shift handover on time, he always writes it up clearly.","Hindi lang siya nasa oras sa handover, malinaw pa lagi ang sulat niya.","fab"]],"drill":[{"q":"小林＿準時，而且很少請假。","opts":["不但","不是","只要"],"a":0,"why":"Pola 不但…而且 untuk menambah informasi positif."},{"q":"這個製程不但慢，＿成本也很高。","opts":["而且","但是","所以"],"a":0,"why":"Pasangan 不但 adalah 而且, bukan 但是."},{"q":"這家店不但東西好吃，＿很便宜。","opts":["而且還","可是","就"],"a":0,"why":"而且還 menambah poin kedua."},{"q":"他＿會說中文，而且還會說台語。","opts":["不但","雖然","因為"],"a":0,"why":"Subjek sama → 他 di depan, lalu 不但."}]},{"lv":4,"k":"b1x_bushi_ershi","form":"不是 + A，而是 + B","icon":"arrows","name":["Bukan A, melainkan B (不是…而是)","Not A, but B (不是…而是)","Hindi A, kundi B (不是…而是)"],"gloss":["Dipakai untuk mengoreksi anggapan yang salah: A dibantah, B adalah fakta yang benar. A dan B harus jenis yang sejajar (orang–orang, sebab–sebab). Dalam lisan santai, 而是 kadang disingkat jadi 是.","Corrects a wrong assumption: A is denied and B is the real fact. A and B should be parallel (person–person, reason–reason). In casual speech 而是 is sometimes shortened to 是.","Ginagamit para itama ang maling akala: tinatanggihan ang A at B ang totoo. Dapat magkatulad ang uri ng A at B. Sa kaswal na usapan, minsan 是 na lang ang gamit sa halip na 而是."],"tip":["不是 = coret A ✗, 而是 = lingkari B ✓. Jangan tertukar dengan 不但…而且 (menambah, bukan mengoreksi).","不是 = cross out A ✗, 而是 = circle B ✓. Don't mix it up with 不但…而且 (adding, not correcting).","不是 = ekisan ang A ✗, 而是 = bilugan ang B ✓. Huwag ipagkamali sa 不但…而且 (pagdagdag, hindi pagtatama)."],"warn":["✗ 不是我的錯，可是機台的問題。→ ✓ 不是我的錯，而是機台的問題。","✗ 不是我的錯，可是機台的問題。→ ✓ 不是我的錯，而是機台的問題。","✗ 不是我的錯，可是機台的問題。→ ✓ 不是我的錯，而是機台的問題。"],"logic":{"id":"Dalam bahasa Indonesia kita bilang 'bukan…, tapi…', sehingga banyak orang memakai 可是/但是. Penutur Taiwan membedakan dua hal: 但是 = kontras biasa ('memang A, tapi B'), sedangkan 而是 = pengganti ('A salah, yang benar B'). Jadi kalau tujuanmu membetulkan anggapan orang lain, otakmu harus memilih 而是. Pola ini sangat sering dipakai saat menjelaskan penyebab masalah.","en":"Like 'not…, but…', learners often reach for 可是/但是. Taiwanese speakers distinguish plain contrast (但是: 'A, however B') from replacement (而是: 'A is wrong, it's actually B'). When your aim is to correct someone's assumption, choose 而是. It is very common when explaining the real cause of a problem."},"ex":[["我不是不想去，而是今天真的太累了。","wǒ bú shì bù xiǎng qù ér shì jīn tiān zhēn de tài lèi le","Bukannya aku nggak mau pergi, tapi hari ini aku capek banget.","It's not that I don't want to go; I'm just really too tired today.","Hindi sa ayaw kong pumunta, kundi pagod na pagod ako ngayon.","daily"],["他不是台灣人，而是馬來西亞人。","tā bú shì tái wān rén ér shì mǎ lái xī yà rén","Dia bukan orang Taiwan, melainkan orang Malaysia.","He isn't Taiwanese; he's Malaysian.","Hindi siya Taiwanese, kundi Malaysian.","daily"],["這不是電阻的問題，而是電容裝反了。","zhè bú shì diàn zǔ de wèn tí ér shì diàn róng zhuāng fǎn le","Ini bukan masalah resistor, tapi kapasitornya terpasang terbalik.","It's not the resistor; the capacitor was installed backwards.","Hindi problema ng resistor ito, kundi baligtad ang kabit ng capacitor.","campus"],["我們今天不是上課，而是去實驗室做實驗。","wǒ men jīn tiān bú shì shàng kè ér shì qù shí yàn shì zuò shí yàn","Hari ini kita bukan kuliah biasa, tapi praktikum di lab.","Today we're not having a lecture; we're doing experiments in the lab.","Ngayon ay hindi tayo magkaklase, kundi mag-eeksperimento sa lab.","campus"],["良率下降不是因為材料，而是溫度不穩。","liáng lǜ xià jiàng bú shì yīn wèi cái liào ér shì wēn dù bù wěn","Yield turun bukan karena material, tapi karena suhunya tidak stabil.","The yield drop isn't because of the material, but because the temperature is unstable.","Bumaba ang yield hindi dahil sa materyal, kundi dahil hindi stable ang temperatura.","fab"],["主管要的不是理由，而是解決方法。","zhǔ guǎn yào de bú shì lǐ yóu ér shì jiě jué fāng fǎ","Yang atasan mau bukan alasan, tapi solusi.","What the supervisor wants isn't excuses but a solution.","Ang gusto ng supervisor ay hindi dahilan, kundi solusyon.","fab"]],"drill":[{"q":"他不是工程師，＿技術員。","opts":["而是","而且","但是"],"a":0,"why":"Koreksi: bukan A, melainkan B → 而是."},{"q":"我＿不喜歡，而是沒時間。","opts":["不是","不但","沒有"],"a":0,"why":"Pasangan 而是 adalah 不是."},{"q":"機台當機不是因為停電，＿因為零件壞了。","opts":["而是","所以","而且"],"a":0,"why":"Sebab yang benar diperkenalkan dengan 而是."},{"q":"這＿我的手機，而是我室友的。","opts":["不是","沒有","不要"],"a":0,"why":"Menyangkal identitas → 不是."}]},{"lv":4,"k":"b1x_chule","form":"除了 + A + (以外)，S + 還／也 + B（tambahan）／除了 + A + (以外)，S + 都 + …（pengecualian）","icon":"grid","name":["Selain… / kecuali… (除了…以外)","Besides… / except… (除了…以外)","Bukod sa… / maliban sa… (除了…以外)"],"gloss":["Punya dua arti, ditentukan kata setelah koma. Dengan 還/也 = 'selain A, juga B' (A termasuk, ada tambahan). Dengan 都 = 'kecuali A, semuanya…' (A dikeluarkan). 以外 boleh dihilangkan dalam lisan.","Two meanings, decided by the word after the comma. With 還/也 = 'besides A, also B' (A is included, plus more). With 都 = 'except A, all…' (A is excluded). 以外 can be dropped in speech.","May dalawang kahulugan depende sa salita pagkatapos ng kuwit. Kapag 還/也 = 'bukod sa A, pati B'. Kapag 都 = 'maliban sa A, lahat…'. Puwedeng alisin ang 以外 sa pananalita."],"tip":["還/也 = ditambah (+). 都 = dikurangi (−). Lihat kata setelah koma!","還/也 = plus (+). 都 = minus (−). Look at the word after the comma!","還/也 = dagdag (+). 都 = bawas (−). Tingnan ang salita pagkatapos ng kuwit!"],"warn":["✗ 除了小王以外，我們也去了。(maksud: kecuali Xiao Wang) → ✓ 除了小王以外，我們都去了。","✗ 除了小王以外，我們也去了。(meaning 'except Xiao Wang') → ✓ 除了小王以外，我們都去了。","✗ 除了小王以外，我們也去了。(ibig sabihin 'maliban kay Xiao Wang') → ✓ 除了小王以外，我們都去了。"],"logic":{"id":"Kata 'selain' dalam bahasa Indonesia bisa berarti 'di samping' atau 'kecuali', dan kita menebak dari konteks. Penutur Taiwan tidak menebak: mereka menandainya dengan jelas di klausa kedua. Kalau ada 還/也, A ikut dihitung dan ada tambahan; kalau ada 都, A dikeluarkan dan sisanya semua sama. Jadi sebelum bicara, putuskan dulu: tambah atau kecualikan?","en":"English separates 'besides' and 'except'; Mandarin uses one frame 除了…以外 and lets the second clause decide. 還/也 means A counts and something is added; 都 means A is left out and everything else is the same. Decide first: are you adding or excluding?"},"ex":[["除了珍奶以外，我也很喜歡喝豆漿。","chú le zhēn nǎi yǐ wài wǒ yě hěn xǐ huān hē dòu jiāng","Selain bubble tea, aku juga suka minum susu kedelai.","Besides bubble tea, I also like soy milk.","Bukod sa milk tea, gusto ko rin ng soy milk.","daily"],["除了星期天，這家店每天都有開。","chú le xīng qí tiān zhè jiā diàn měi tiān dōu yǒu kāi","Kecuali hari Minggu, toko ini buka setiap hari.","Except Sundays, this shop is open every day.","Maliban sa Linggo, bukas ang tindahang ito araw-araw.","daily"],["除了電子電路，我們這學期還要修微處理機。","chú le diàn zǐ diàn lù wǒ men zhè xué qí hái yào xiū wéi chǔ lǐ jī","Selain elektronika, semester ini kita juga harus ambil mikroprosesor.","Besides electronic circuits, we also have to take microprocessors this semester.","Bukod sa electronic circuits, kukuha rin kami ng microprocessors ngayong semestre.","campus"],["除了阿明以外，全班都做完實驗了。","chú le ā míng yǐ wài quán bān dōu zuò wán shí yàn le","Kecuali A-Ming, seluruh kelas sudah selesai praktikum.","Except A-Ming, the whole class has finished the experiment.","Maliban kay A-Ming, tapos na ang buong klase sa eksperimento.","campus"],["除了換零件，我們還要重新校正機台。","chú le huàn líng jiàn wǒ men hái yào chóng xīn jiào zhèng jī tái","Selain ganti part, kita juga harus kalibrasi ulang mesinnya.","Besides replacing the part, we also need to recalibrate the tool.","Bukod sa pagpapalit ng piyesa, kailangan pa naming i-calibrate ulit ang makina.","fab"],["除了這台以外，其他機台都正常。","chú le zhè tái yǐ wài qí tā jī tái dōu zhèng cháng","Kecuali yang ini, mesin lainnya normal semua.","Except this one, all the other tools are normal.","Maliban sa isang ito, normal ang lahat ng ibang makina.","fab"]],"drill":[{"q":"除了英文以外，他＿會說日文。","opts":["還","都","就"],"a":0,"why":"Tambahan (dia juga bisa) → 還."},{"q":"除了小陳以外，大家＿到了。","opts":["都","還","也"],"a":0,"why":"Pengecualian: semua sudah datang kecuali Xiao Chen → 都."},{"q":"＿上課以外，我週末還要打工。","opts":["除了","不但","只要"],"a":0,"why":"除了…以外 + 還 = selain."},{"q":"除了無塵室以外，工廠裡其他地方我＿去過了。","opts":["都","還","才"],"a":0,"why":"Pengecualian → 都."}]},{"lv":4,"k":"b1x_zhiyao","form":"只要 + syarat，(S) + 就 + hasil","icon":"check","name":["Asal…, pasti… (只要…就)","As long as…, then… (只要…就)","Basta…, tiyak… (只要…就)"],"gloss":["Menyatakan syarat yang CUKUP: asal syarat ini terpenuhi, hasilnya pasti terjadi. 就 diletakkan setelah subjek di klausa kedua, sebelum verba.","Expresses a SUFFICIENT condition: as long as this is met, the result follows. 就 goes after the subject of the second clause, before the verb.","Nagsasaad ng sapat na kondisyon: basta matupad ito, mangyayari ang resulta. Ang 就 ay pagkatapos ng paksa sa ikalawang sugnay, bago ang pandiwa."],"tip":["只要 = 'cukup ini saja'. Pasangan tetapnya 就. Bandingkan nanti dengan 只有…才 (satu-satunya syarat).","只要 = 'this alone is enough'. Its fixed partner is 就. Compare with 只有…才 (the only condition).","只要 = 'sapat na ito'. Laging kapares ang 就. Ihambing sa 只有…才 (tanging kondisyon)."],"warn":["✗ 只要多練習，就你會進步。→ ✓ 只要多練習，你就會進步。","✗ 只要多練習，就你會進步。→ ✓ 只要多練習，你就會進步。","✗ 只要多練習，就你會進步。→ ✓ 只要多練習，你就會進步。"],"logic":{"id":"Orang Indonesia bilang 'Asal kamu latihan, kamu pasti bisa', dan kata 'pasti' bisa di mana saja. Dalam Mandarin, 就 adalah adverbia, jadi ia harus menempel tepat sebelum verba dan SETELAH subjek. Penutur Taiwan memakai 只要 untuk menenangkan atau memberi instruksi sederhana: 'cukup lakukan X, beres'. Pikirkan 只要 sebagai pintu yang mudah dibuka.","en":"In English, 'then' can be dropped and 'surely' floats anywhere. In Mandarin 就 is an adverb: it must sit right before the verb, AFTER the subject. Taiwanese use 只要 to reassure or give simple instructions: 'just do X and it's fine'. Think of 只要 as an easy door to open."},"ex":[["只要不下雨，我們就騎機車去。","zhǐ yào bú xià yǔ wǒ men jiù qí jī chē qù","Asal nggak hujan, kita naik motor ke sana.","As long as it doesn't rain, we'll ride the scooter there.","Basta hindi umulan, magmomotor tayo papunta.","daily"],["只要刷一卡通，就可以搭捷運。","zhǐ yào shuā yì kǎ tōng jiù kě yǐ dā jié yùn","Cukup tap kartu iPASS, kamu sudah bisa naik MRT.","Just tap your iPASS card and you can ride the MRT.","Basta i-tap ang iPASS card, puwede ka nang sumakay ng MRT.","daily"],["只要照著步驟做，實驗就不會失敗。","zhǐ yào zhào zhe bù zòu zuò shí yàn jiù bú huì shī bài","Asal ikuti langkah-langkahnya, praktikumnya nggak akan gagal.","As long as you follow the steps, the experiment won't fail.","Basta sundin ang mga hakbang, hindi papalpak ang eksperimento.","campus"],["只要電壓超過五伏特，燈就會亮。","zhǐ yào diàn yā chāo guò wǔ fú tè dēng jiù huì liàng","Asal tegangannya lebih dari 5 volt, lampunya akan menyala.","As long as the voltage exceeds 5 volts, the light turns on.","Basta lumampas sa 5 volts ang boltahe, sisindi ang ilaw.","campus"],["只要有異常，你就馬上通知值班工程師。","zhǐ yào yǒu yì cháng nǐ jiù mǎ shàng tōng zhī zhí bān gōng chéng shī","Begitu ada abnormal, langsung kabari engineer yang jaga.","Whenever there's an abnormality, notify the on-duty engineer right away.","Basta may abnormal, agad mong sabihan ang engineer na naka-duty.","fab"],["只要做好保養，機台就比較不會當機。","zhǐ yào zuò hǎo bǎo yǎng jī tái jiù bǐ jiào bú huì dāng jī","Asal maintenance-nya bagus, mesin jarang hang.","As long as maintenance is done well, the tool is less likely to crash.","Basta maayos ang maintenance, bihirang mag-hang ang makina.","fab"]],"drill":[{"q":"＿你有空，我就請你吃飯。","opts":["只要","只有","不但"],"a":0,"why":"Syarat cukup + 就 → 只要."},{"q":"只要按這個按鈕，機台＿會停下來。","opts":["就","才","都"],"a":0,"why":"只要 berpasangan dengan 就."},{"q":"只要多練習，你＿會越說越好。","opts":["就","還","而"],"a":0,"why":"就 setelah subjek 你."},{"q":"只要穿好無塵衣，你＿可以進去了。","opts":["就","才","再"],"a":0,"why":"Syarat cukup → 就."}]},{"lv":4,"k":"b1x_zhiyou","form":"只有 + satu-satunya syarat，(S) + 才 + hasil","icon":"target","name":["Hanya jika…, baru… (只有…才)","Only if…, then… (只有…才)","Kung… lang, saka… (只有…才)"],"gloss":["Menyatakan syarat WAJIB satu-satunya: tanpa syarat ini, hasilnya tidak akan terjadi. Pasangannya 才 (bukan 就). 才 ditaruh setelah subjek klausa kedua.","Expresses the ONLY, necessary condition: without it, the result won't happen. Its partner is 才 (not 就), placed after the subject of the second clause.","Nagsasaad ng tanging kailangang kondisyon: kung wala ito, hindi mangyayari ang resulta. Kapares nito ang 才 (hindi 就)."],"tip":["只要…就 = syarat ringan (cukup). 只有…才 = syarat ketat (harus). 才 terasa 'baru boleh / baru bisa'.","只要…就 = easy condition (enough). 只有…才 = strict condition (must). 才 feels like 'only then'.","只要…就 = magaan na kondisyon. 只有…才 = mahigpit na kondisyon. Ang 才 ay parang 'saka lang'."],"warn":["✗ 只有考過證照，就能操作。→ ✓ 只有考過證照，才能操作。","✗ 只有考過證照，就能操作。→ ✓ 只有考過證照，才能操作。","✗ 只有考過證照，就能操作。→ ✓ 只有考過證照，才能操作。"],"logic":{"id":"Dalam bahasa Indonesia 'hanya kalau…, baru…' dan 'asal…, pasti…' terasa berbeda, dan Mandarin juga membedakannya dengan tegas lewat 就 dan 才. Penutur Taiwan memakai 只有…才 untuk aturan dan batasan: SOP, keselamatan, izin. Kalau kamu salah memakai 就, kalimatnya terdengar seperti syaratnya ringan, padahal sebenarnya ketat. Ingat: 只有 selalu menuntut 才.","en":"English 'only if… (then)' vs 'as long as…' maps to 只有…才 vs 只要…就. Taiwanese use 只有…才 for rules and restrictions: SOPs, safety, permissions. Using 就 here makes the condition sound easy when it's actually strict. 只有 always calls for 才."},"ex":[["只有週末，我才有時間跟女朋友見面。","zhǐ yǒu zhōu mò wǒ cái yǒu shí jiān gēn nǚ péng yǒu jiàn miàn","Cuma pas akhir pekan aku baru ada waktu ketemu pacar.","Only on weekends do I have time to see my girlfriend.","Tuwing weekend lang ako may oras makipagkita sa girlfriend ko.","daily"],["只有多說，你的中文才會進步。","zhǐ yǒu duō shuō nǐ de zhōng wén cái huì jìn bù","Hanya kalau sering ngomong, bahasa Mandarinmu baru akan maju.","Only by speaking a lot will your Chinese improve.","Kung madalas ka lang magsalita, saka gagaling ang Chinese mo.","daily"],["只有做完實驗報告，老師才讓我們下課。","zhǐ yǒu zuò wán shí yàn bào gào lǎo shī cái ràng wǒ men xià kè","Hanya setelah laporan praktikum selesai, dosen baru izinkan kita pulang.","Only after finishing the lab report does the teacher let us leave.","Kapag tapos lang ang lab report, saka kami pinapauwi ng guro.","campus"],["只有接好地線，這個電路才安全。","zhǐ yǒu jiē hǎo dì xiàn zhè ge diàn lù cái ān quán","Hanya kalau kabel ground terpasang, rangkaian ini baru aman.","Only with the ground wire connected is this circuit safe.","Kung nakakabit lang ang ground wire, saka ligtas ang circuit na ito.","campus"],["只有通過訓練的人，才可以操作這台機台。","zhǐ yǒu tōng guò xùn liàn de rén cái kě yǐ cāo zuò zhè tái jī tái","Hanya orang yang lulus training yang boleh mengoperasikan mesin ini.","Only people who passed the training may operate this tool.","Ang mga pumasa lang sa training ang puwedeng gumamit ng makinang ito.","fab"],["只有穿好無塵衣，才能進無塵室。","zhǐ yǒu chuān hǎo wú chén yī cái néng jìn wú chén shì","Hanya kalau sudah pakai baju cleanroom, baru boleh masuk cleanroom.","Only once you're fully gowned can you enter the cleanroom.","Kapag suot mo lang ang cleanroom suit, saka ka makakapasok sa cleanroom.","fab"]],"drill":[{"q":"只有主管同意，你＿可以換班。","opts":["才","就","都"],"a":0,"why":"只有 berpasangan dengan 才."},{"q":"＿考過證照，才能操作這台機台。","opts":["只有","只要","除了"],"a":0,"why":"Ada 才 → syarat wajib 只有."},{"q":"只要有網路，我＿能在家上課。","opts":["就","才","還"],"a":0,"why":"只要 → 就 (syarat cukup)."},{"q":"只有溫度穩定，良率＿會好。","opts":["才","就","也"],"a":0,"why":"只有 → 才."}]},{"lv":4,"k":"b1x_ruguo","form":"如果／要是 + syarat + (的話)，(S) + 就 + hasil","icon":"path","name":["Kalau…, (maka)… (如果／要是…的話，就)","If…, then… (如果／要是…的話，就)","Kung…, (ay)… (如果／要是…的話，就)"],"gloss":["Kalimat pengandaian. 如果 netral, 要是 lebih lisan. 的話 di akhir klausa syarat sangat umum di Taiwan, bahkan bisa berdiri sendiri tanpa 如果 ('有空的話'). Klausa kedua biasanya memakai 就 setelah subjek.","Conditional sentences. 如果 is neutral, 要是 more colloquial. 的話 at the end of the condition is very common in Taiwan and can even be used alone without 如果 ('有空的話'). The result clause usually uses 就 after the subject.","Pangungusap na kondisyonal. Neutral ang 如果, mas kolokyal ang 要是. Karaniwan sa Taiwan ang 的話 sa dulo ng kondisyon, puwede ring wala ang 如果. Karaniwang may 就 sa ikalawang sugnay pagkatapos ng paksa."],"tip":["Rumus aman: 如果…的話，(S) 就…. Saat ngobrol cepat cukup: '…的話，就…'.","Safe formula: 如果…的話，(S) 就…. In quick talk just: '…的話，就…'.","Ligtas na pormula: 如果…的話，(S) 就…. Sa mabilis na usapan: '…的話，就…'."],"warn":["✗ 如果你忙，就我自己去。→ ✓ 如果你忙，我就自己去。","✗ 如果你忙，就我自己去。→ ✓ 如果你忙，我就自己去。","✗ 如果你忙，就我自己去。→ ✓ 如果你忙，我就自己去。"],"logic":{"id":"Orang Indonesia sering langsung bilang 'kalau…, (maka)…' dan menaruh 'maka' sebelum subjek. Dalam Mandarin 就 bukan konjungsi seperti 'maka', melainkan adverbia, jadi ia selalu setelah subjek. Penutur Taiwan juga suka menutup syarat dengan 的話 agar terdengar lebih lembut dan jelas batasnya. Kalau ragu, pakai bingkai lengkap 如果…的話，S 就….","en":"English 'then' comes before the subject; Mandarin 就 is an adverb and goes after it. Taiwanese speakers like to close the condition with 的話, which sounds softer and marks the boundary clearly. When unsure, use the full frame 如果…的話，S 就…."},"ex":[["如果明天下雨的話，我們就不去墾丁了。","rú guǒ míng tiān xià yǔ de huà wǒ men jiù bú qù kěn dīng le","Kalau besok hujan, kita nggak jadi ke Kenting.","If it rains tomorrow, we won't go to Kenting.","Kung umulan bukas, hindi na tayo pupunta sa Kenting.","daily"],["你要是累了，就先回去休息吧。","nǐ yào shì lèi le jiù xiān huí qù xiū xí ba","Kalau kamu capek, pulang dulu istirahat aja.","If you're tired, go back and rest first.","Kung pagod ka na, umuwi ka muna at magpahinga.","daily"],["如果你看不懂電路圖，就問助教。","rú guǒ nǐ kàn bù dǒng diàn lù tú jiù wèn zhù jiào","Kalau kamu nggak ngerti diagram rangkaiannya, tanya asisten dosen.","If you can't read the circuit diagram, ask the TA.","Kung hindi mo maintindihan ang circuit diagram, tanungin mo ang TA.","campus"],["有問題的話，下課後來實驗室找我。","yǒu wèn tí de huà xià kè hòu lái shí yàn shì zhǎo wǒ","Kalau ada pertanyaan, temui aku di lab setelah kelas.","If you have questions, come find me in the lab after class.","Kung may tanong ka, puntahan mo ako sa lab pagkatapos ng klase.","campus"],["要是機台再當機，你就先停機，再打電話給我。","yào shì jī tái zài dāng jī nǐ jiù xiān tíng jī zài dǎ diàn huà gěi wǒ","Kalau mesinnya hang lagi, stop dulu mesinnya, lalu telepon aku.","If the tool crashes again, stop it first, then call me.","Kung mag-hang ulit ang makina, i-stop mo muna, saka mo ako tawagan.","fab"],["如果良率一直不好的話，就要檢查製程參數。","rú guǒ liáng lǜ yì zhí bù hǎo de huà jiù yào jiǎn chá zhì chéng cān shù","Kalau yield terus jelek, parameter prosesnya harus dicek.","If the yield stays poor, we need to check the process parameters.","Kung laging mababa ang yield, kailangang suriin ang process parameters.","fab"]],"drill":[{"q":"＿你有空的話，就一起去吃飯吧。","opts":["如果","雖然","不管"],"a":0,"why":"Pengandaian + 的話 → 如果."},{"q":"你要是不舒服，＿先回家吧。","opts":["就","才","都"],"a":0,"why":"Klausa hasil memakai 就."},{"q":"有問題＿，隨時問我。","opts":["的話","以外","而且"],"a":0,"why":"…的話 = kalau…."},{"q":"如果你忙，我＿自己去。","opts":["就","才","還"],"a":0,"why":"就 setelah subjek 我."}]},{"lv":5,"k":"b1x_jishi","form":"即使／就算 + pengandaian，S + 也 + hasil (tetap)","icon":"bolt","name":["Sekalipun…, tetap… (即使／就算…也)","Even if…, still… (即使／就算…也)","Kahit pa…, … pa rin (即使／就算…也)"],"gloss":["Untuk situasi pengandaian, sering yang ekstrem: walaupun itu terjadi, hasilnya tidak berubah. 就算 lebih lisan, 即使 lebih formal. Pasangannya 也. Beda dengan 雖然: 雖然 = fakta yang sudah nyata; 即使/就算 = andaikan saja.","For hypothetical, often extreme, situations: even if it happens, the result won't change. 就算 is more colloquial, 即使 more formal; both pair with 也. Unlike 雖然 (a real fact), 即使/就算 is a 'suppose'.","Para sa ipinagpapalagay na sitwasyon: kahit mangyari iyon, hindi magbabago ang resulta. Mas kolokyal ang 就算, mas pormal ang 即使; kapares ang 也. Iba sa 雖然 na totoong pangyayari."],"tip":["雖然 = sudah terjadi (fakta). 就算 = 'anggap saja terjadi' — hasilnya tetap, jadi pasangannya 也.","雖然 = it's real. 就算 = 'suppose it happens' — result unchanged, so partner with 也.","雖然 = totoo na. 就算 = 'ipagpalagay nating mangyari' — pareho pa rin, kaya 也."],"warn":["✗ 就算很累，我就要去上班。→ ✓ 就算很累，我也要去上班。","✗ 就算很累，我就要去上班。→ ✓ 就算很累，我也要去上班。","✗ 就算很累，我就要去上班。→ ✓ 就算很累，我也要去上班。"],"logic":{"id":"Dalam bahasa Indonesia, 'walaupun' dipakai untuk fakta maupun pengandaian. Penutur Taiwan membaginya: kalau sungguh terjadi, pakai 雖然…但是/還是; kalau masih 'seandainya', pakai 就算/即使…也. Kata 也 di sini berarti 'tetap saja', menunjukkan hasil yang tidak bergeser. Pola ini sering dipakai untuk menekankan aturan keselamatan atau tekad pribadi.","en":"English 'even though' (fact) vs 'even if' (hypothesis) matches 雖然 vs 就算/即使. 也 here means 'still', showing the result doesn't budge. It's common for stressing safety rules or personal determination."},"ex":[["就算再忙，我也會打電話給我媽。","jiù suàn zài máng wǒ yě huì dǎ diàn huà gěi wǒ mā","Sesibuk apa pun, aku tetap akan telepon ibuku.","Even if I'm busy, I'll still call my mom.","Kahit gaano ako kaabala, tatawagan ko pa rin si Nanay.","daily"],["就算你不說，我也知道。","jiù suàn nǐ bù shuō wǒ yě zhī dào","Biarpun kamu nggak bilang, aku juga tahu.","Even if you don't say it, I know.","Kahit hindi mo sabihin, alam ko.","daily"],["即使考試很難，我們也不能作弊。","jí shǐ kǎo shì hěn nán wǒ men yě bù néng zuò bì","Sekalipun ujiannya susah, kita tetap nggak boleh nyontek.","Even if the exam is hard, we can't cheat.","Kahit mahirap ang exam, hindi tayo puwedeng mangopya.","campus"],["就算只差一點，這個電阻值也不能用。","jiù suàn zhǐ chà yì diǎn zhè ge diàn zǔ zhí yě bù néng yòng","Biarpun selisihnya sedikit, nilai resistor ini tetap nggak bisa dipakai.","Even if it's only slightly off, this resistance value can't be used.","Kahit kaunti lang ang diperensya, hindi pa rin puwede ang resistance value na ito.","campus"],["即使是小異常，也要寫在交接本上。","jí shǐ shì xiǎo yì cháng yě yào xiě zài jiāo jiē běn shàng","Sekalipun cuma abnormal kecil, tetap harus ditulis di buku serah terima.","Even a small abnormality must be written in the handover log.","Kahit maliit na abnormal, dapat isulat sa handover log.","fab"],["就算趕貨，也不能跳過安全檢查。","jiù suàn gǎn huò yě bù néng tiào guò ān quán jiǎn chá","Biarpun lagi kejar target produksi, pengecekan keselamatan nggak boleh dilewati.","Even when rushing orders, you can't skip safety checks.","Kahit nagmamadali sa order, hindi puwedeng laktawan ang safety check.","fab"]],"drill":[{"q":"就算明天有颱風，我＿要去上班。","opts":["也","就","才"],"a":0,"why":"就算 berpasangan dengan 也."},{"q":"＿你不喜歡，也要吃一點。","opts":["就算","因為","只要"],"a":0,"why":"Pengandaian + 也 → 就算."},{"q":"即使機台很新，＿要定期保養。","opts":["也","才","就"],"a":0,"why":"即使…也."},{"q":"他昨天＿很累，還是去上課了。","opts":["雖然","就算","只要"],"a":0,"why":"Fakta nyata (kemarin memang capek) → 雖然."}]},{"lv":4,"k":"b1x_wulun","form":"無論／不管 + kata tanya／A不A／A還是B，S + 都 + hasil","icon":"star","name":["Apa pun / bagaimanapun…, tetap… (不管／無論…都)","No matter…, always… (不管／無論…都)","Anuman / kahit ano…, … pa rin (不管／無論…都)"],"gloss":["Hasil tetap sama dalam semua kemungkinan. Setelah 不管/無論 HARUS ada bentuk pertanyaan: kata tanya (什麼, 誰, 怎麼, 多…), A不A, atau A還是B. 不管 lebih lisan, 無論 lebih formal. Pasangannya 都 (kadang 也).","The result is the same in all cases. After 不管/無論 there MUST be a question form: a question word (什麼, 誰, 怎麼, 多…), A-not-A, or A還是B. 不管 is colloquial, 無論 formal; partner is 都 (sometimes 也).","Pareho ang resulta sa lahat ng posibilidad. Pagkatapos ng 不管/無論 dapat may anyong tanong: salitang pananong, A不A, o A還是B. Kolokyal ang 不管, pormal ang 無論; kapares ang 都."],"tip":["Bayangkan 不管 membuka semua pilihan (?), lalu 都 menutupnya dengan satu hasil. Tanpa '?', kalimat rusak.","Imagine 不管 opens all options (?), then 都 closes them with one result. No '?' form = broken sentence.","Isipin na binubuksan ng 不管 ang lahat ng opsyon (?), at isinasara ng 都 sa iisang resulta."],"warn":["✗ 不管下雨，我都去。→ ✓ 不管下不下雨，我都去。","✗ 不管下雨，我都去。→ ✓ 不管下不下雨，我都去。","✗ 不管下雨，我都去。→ ✓ 不管下不下雨，我都去。"],"logic":{"id":"Orang Indonesia bilang 'Walaupun hujan, aku tetap pergi' atau 'Hujan atau tidak, aku pergi'. Penutur Taiwan berpikir dengan 'daftar kemungkinan': setelah 不管 mereka menyebut pilihan dalam bentuk pertanyaan (下不下雨, 誰, 多晚), lalu 都 menyatakan bahwa semuanya berakhir sama. Kalau hanya ada satu keadaan (下雨), itu bukan 不管, melainkan 就算 atau 雖然.","en":"English 'no matter whether/what/how' already contains a question word; Mandarin works the same: 不管 must be followed by a question form, then 都 says every option ends the same. With only one situation (下雨) you need 就算 or 雖然 instead."},"ex":[["不管多晚，我媽都會等我回家。","bù guǎn duō wǎn wǒ mā dōu huì děng wǒ huí jiā","Semalam apa pun, ibuku selalu menunggu aku pulang.","No matter how late, my mom waits for me to come home.","Gaano man kagabi, hinihintay ako ni Nanay na umuwi.","daily"],["不管你吃什麼，我都請客。","bù guǎn nǐ chī shén me wǒ dōu qǐng kè","Mau makan apa pun, aku yang traktir.","Whatever you eat, it's my treat.","Anuman ang kainin mo, libre ko.","daily"],["無論是誰，進實驗室都要穿實驗衣。","wú lùn shì shéi jìn shí yàn shì dōu yào chuān shí yàn yī","Siapa pun dia, masuk lab harus pakai jas lab.","No matter who you are, you must wear a lab coat in the lab.","Sino ka man, dapat magsuot ng lab coat sa lab.","campus"],["不管今天去不去上課，報告都要交。","bù guǎn jīn tiān qù bú qù shàng kè bào gào dōu yào jiāo","Hari ini masuk kelas atau nggak, laporan tetap harus dikumpulkan.","Whether or not you go to class today, the report must be submitted.","Pumasok ka man o hindi ngayon, kailangan pa ring ipasa ang report.","campus"],["不管白班還是夜班，交接都要寫清楚。","bù guǎn bái bān hái shì yè bān jiāo jiē dōu yào xiě qīng chǔ","Shift pagi atau malam, serah terima harus ditulis dengan jelas.","Day shift or night shift, the handover must be written clearly.","Day shift man o night shift, dapat malinaw ang handover.","fab"],["無論多趕，都要按照標準流程做。","wú lùn duō gǎn dōu yào àn zhào biāo zhǔn liú chéng zuò","Seburu-buru apa pun, harus tetap ikut prosedur standar.","No matter how rushed, you must follow the standard procedure.","Gaano man kamadali, dapat sundin ang standard procedure.","fab"]],"drill":[{"q":"不管＿，我都要去。","opts":["下不下雨","下雨","很下雨"],"a":0,"why":"Setelah 不管 harus bentuk pertanyaan: A不A."},{"q":"＿是誰，都不能在無塵室吃東西。","opts":["不管","雖然","只有"],"a":0,"why":"Kata tanya 誰 + 都 → 不管."},{"q":"不管多累，他＿會去健身房。","opts":["都","才","就"],"a":0,"why":"不管 berpasangan dengan 都."},{"q":"無論白班＿夜班，薪水都一樣。","opts":["還是","而且","但是"],"a":0,"why":"Pilihan A還是B setelah 無論."}]},{"lv":4,"k":"b1x_weile","form":"為了 + tujuan，S + V…／S + V… + 是為了 + tujuan","icon":"target","name":["Untuk / demi… (為了)","In order to / for the sake of… (為了)","Para sa / upang… (為了)"],"gloss":["Menyatakan TUJUAN. Biasanya di awal kalimat atau setelah subjek, sebelum verba utama. Kalau tujuan disebut di akhir, pakai 是為了. Jangan tertukar dengan 因為 (sebab).","Expresses PURPOSE. It usually comes at the start or after the subject, before the main verb. To put the purpose at the end, use 是為了. Don't confuse it with 因為 (cause).","Nagsasaad ng LAYUNIN. Karaniwang nasa simula o pagkatapos ng paksa, bago ang pangunahing pandiwa. Kung nasa dulo ang layunin, gamitin ang 是為了. Iba ito sa 因為 (dahilan)."],"tip":["為了 menjawab 'untuk apa?' (ke depan). 因為 menjawab 'kenapa?' (ke belakang).","為了 answers 'what for?' (looks forward). 因為 answers 'why?' (looks back).","Sinasagot ng 為了 ang 'para saan?'. Sinasagot ng 因為 ang 'bakit?'."],"warn":["✗ 我來台灣為了讀書。→ ✓ 我來台灣是為了讀書。／✓ 為了讀書，我來台灣。","✗ 我來台灣為了讀書。→ ✓ 我來台灣是為了讀書。／✓ 為了讀書，我來台灣。","✗ 我來台灣為了讀書。→ ✓ 我來台灣是為了讀書。／✓ 為了讀書，我來台灣。"],"logic":{"id":"Bahasa Indonesia bebas menaruh 'untuk…' di akhir: 'Aku datang ke Taiwan untuk kuliah.' Mandarin lebih suka tujuan disebut dulu, baru tindakannya: 為了讀書，我來台灣. Kalau mau menaruhnya di akhir, penutur Taiwan menambahkan 是 sebagai penjelas: 我來台灣是為了讀書. Selain itu, 為了 selalu soal tujuan ke depan, sedangkan 因為 soal penyebab yang sudah ada.","en":"English puts 'to…' at the end freely. Mandarin prefers purpose first, then the action: 為了讀書，我來台灣. To put it last, Taiwanese add 是: 我來台灣是為了讀書. 為了 is always a forward-looking goal; 因為 is an existing cause."},"ex":[["為了省錢，我每天自己帶便當。","wèi le shěng qián wǒ měi tiān zì jǐ dài biàn dāng","Biar hemat, aku tiap hari bawa bekal sendiri.","To save money, I bring my own lunch box every day.","Para makatipid, nagbabaon ako araw-araw.","daily"],["他為了女朋友，每個週末都去台北。","tā wèi le nǚ péng yǒu měi ge zhōu mò dōu qù tái běi","Demi pacarnya, dia ke Taipei setiap akhir pekan.","For his girlfriend's sake, he goes to Taipei every weekend.","Para sa girlfriend niya, pumupunta siya sa Taipei tuwing weekend.","daily"],["為了準備期末考，我們昨天熬夜了。","wèi le zhǔn bèi qí mò kǎo wǒ men zuó tiān áo yè le","Buat persiapan UAS, kemarin kami begadang.","We stayed up late yesterday to prepare for finals.","Para maghanda sa finals, nagpuyat kami kahapon.","campus"],["我學中文是為了以後在台灣的半導體公司工作。","wǒ xué zhōng wén shì wèi le yǐ hòu zài tái wān de bàn dǎo tǐ gōng sī gōng zuò","Aku belajar Mandarin supaya nanti bisa kerja di perusahaan semikonduktor di Taiwan.","I'm learning Chinese so I can work at a semiconductor company in Taiwan later.","Nag-aaral ako ng Chinese para makapagtrabaho sa semiconductor company sa Taiwan.","campus"],["為了提高良率，工程師一直在調參數。","wèi le tí gāo liáng lǜ gōng chéng shī yì zhí zài tiáo cān shù","Untuk menaikkan yield, engineer terus menyetel parameter.","To raise the yield, the engineers keep tuning parameters.","Para tumaas ang yield, patuloy na nag-aadjust ng parameters ang mga engineer.","fab"],["為了避免汙染，無塵室裡不能用一般的紙。","wèi le bì miǎn wū rǎn wú chén shì lǐ bù néng yòng yì bān de zhǐ","Untuk mencegah kontaminasi, di cleanroom nggak boleh pakai kertas biasa.","To avoid contamination, ordinary paper can't be used in the cleanroom.","Para maiwasan ang kontaminasyon, bawal ang ordinaryong papel sa cleanroom.","fab"]],"drill":[{"q":"＿趕上第一班捷運，他五點就起床了。","opts":["為了","因為","所以"],"a":0,"why":"Tujuan (agar sempat naik MRT pertama) → 為了."},{"q":"我來台灣是＿學技術。","opts":["為了","因為","對於"],"a":0,"why":"Tujuan di akhir → 是為了."},{"q":"他＿生病，所以沒來上班。","opts":["因為","為了","除了"],"a":0,"why":"Sebab, bukan tujuan → 因為."},{"q":"＿保護晶圓，要戴手套。","opts":["為了","因為","雖然"],"a":0,"why":"Tujuan → 為了."}]},{"lv":5,"k":"b1x_youyu","form":"（lisan）因為 A，所以 B ／（formal）由於 A，因此 B","icon":"scale","name":["Karena…, jadi… — lisan vs formal (因為…所以／由於…因此)","Because…, so… — spoken vs formal (因為…所以／由於…因此)","Dahil…, kaya… — pasalita vs pormal (因為…所以／由於…因此)"],"gloss":["Keduanya sebab-akibat, bedanya gaya bahasa. 因為…所以 dipakai saat ngobrol; sering hanya salah satu yang muncul. 由於…因此 dipakai di laporan, email kerja, pengumuman, dan presentasi. Dalam lisan santai, 由於…因此 terdengar kaku.","Both express cause and effect; the difference is register. 因為…所以 is for conversation, often with only one of the two. 由於…因此 is for reports, work email, announcements and presentations; in casual talk it sounds stiff.","Parehong sanhi at bunga; magkaiba sa estilo. Ang 因為…所以 ay sa usapan, madalas isa lang ang ginagamit. Ang 由於…因此 ay para sa report, email sa trabaho, anunsyo at presentasyon."],"tip":["Ngobrol sama teman → 因為／所以. Laporan ke atasan, presentasi, pengumuman → 由於／因此.","Chatting with friends → 因為／所以. Reports to the boss, presentations, notices → 由於／因此.","Kausap ang kaibigan → 因為／所以. Report sa boss, presentasyon, anunsyo → 由於／因此."],"warn":["✗ (ke teman) 由於我很餓，因此我要吃飯。→ ✓ 因為我很餓，所以想先吃飯。","✗ (to a friend) 由於我很餓，因此我要吃飯。→ ✓ 因為我很餓，所以想先吃飯。","✗ (sa kaibigan) 由於我很餓，因此我要吃飯。→ ✓ 因為我很餓，所以想先吃飯。"],"logic":{"id":"Bahasa Indonesia juga punya 'karena…, jadi…' (lisan) dan 'dikarenakan…, maka…' (formal). Penutur Taiwan sangat peka terhadap gaya ini: di pabrik, laporan abnormal dan email ke atasan memakai 由於…因此, tapi saat ngobrol di ruang istirahat mereka bilang 因為… atau cukup 所以…. Kalau kamu memakai 由於 ke teman, terdengar seperti membaca berita. Jadi pilih kata berdasarkan siapa pendengarnya.","en":"It's like 'because…, so…' vs 'due to…, therefore…'. Taiwanese are sensitive to register: abnormality reports and emails to managers use 由於…因此, while break-room chat uses 因為… or just 所以…. Using 由於 with friends sounds like reading the news. Choose by audience."},"ex":[["因為我睡過頭，所以沒趕上公車。","yīn wèi wǒ shuì guò tóu suǒ yǐ méi gǎn shàng gōng chē","Karena aku kesiangan, jadi ketinggalan bus.","Because I overslept, I missed the bus.","Dahil sobra ang tulog ko, naiwan ako ng bus.","daily"],["我今天不去了，因為下大雨。","wǒ jīn tiān bú qù le yīn wèi xià dà yǔ","Hari ini aku nggak jadi pergi, soalnya hujan deras.","I'm not going today because it's pouring.","Hindi na ako pupunta ngayon, kasi malakas ang ulan.","daily"],["由於颱風來襲，明天全校停課。","yóu yú tái fēng lái xí míng tiān quán xiào tíng kè","Dikarenakan topan datang, besok seluruh kampus libur kuliah.","Due to the typhoon, all classes are cancelled tomorrow.","Dahil sa bagyo, walang pasok ang buong paaralan bukas.","campus"],["因為示波器壞了，所以我們改天再量。","yīn wèi shì bō qì huài le suǒ yǐ wǒ men gǎi tiān zài liáng","Karena osiloskopnya rusak, kita ukur lain hari aja.","Because the oscilloscope is broken, we'll measure another day.","Dahil sira ang oscilloscope, sa ibang araw na lang tayo susukat.","campus"],["由於真空幫浦異常，因此機台暫停生產。","yóu yú zhēn kōng bāng pǔ yì cháng yīn cǐ jī tái zhàn tíng shēng chǎn","Dikarenakan pompa vakum abnormal, maka mesin dihentikan sementara.","Due to a vacuum pump abnormality, the tool has stopped production temporarily.","Dahil abnormal ang vacuum pump, pansamantalang itinigil ang produksyon ng makina.","fab"],["由於溫度控制不穩，因此這批晶圓的良率偏低。","yóu yú wēn dù kòng zhì bù wěn yīn cǐ zhè pī jīng yuán de liáng lǜ piān dī","Karena kontrol suhu tidak stabil, yield wafer lot ini cenderung rendah.","Due to unstable temperature control, this lot of wafers has low yield.","Dahil hindi stable ang temperature control, mababa ang yield ng batch na ito.","fab"]],"drill":[{"q":"（跟朋友聊天）＿我太累了，所以不想出門。","opts":["因為","由於","因此"],"a":0,"why":"Ngobrol santai → 因為."},{"q":"（報告）由於材料短缺，＿交期延後一週。","opts":["因此","但是","而且"],"a":0,"why":"Gaya laporan: 由於…因此."},{"q":"因為下雨，＿我們改在室內上課。","opts":["所以","而是","就算"],"a":0,"why":"因為…所以."},{"q":"（公告）＿系統維修，網站今晚暫停服務。","opts":["由於","為了","雖然"],"a":0,"why":"Pengumuman formal → 由於."}]},{"lv":4,"k":"b1x_lian","form":"連 + hal ekstrem + 都／也 + (不／沒) + V","icon":"sparkle","name":["Bahkan… pun (連…都／也)","Even… (連…都／也)","Kahit… (連…都／也)"],"gloss":["Menekankan sesuatu yang ekstrem atau tidak terduga ('bahkan X pun…'). Hal yang ditekankan ditaruh setelah 連, lalu 都/也 sebelum verba. Objek boleh dipindah ke depan. Sering dipakai dengan 一 + M: 連一句都不懂.","Emphasises something extreme or unexpected ('even X…'). The emphasised item follows 連, then 都/也 comes before the verb. The object may move to the front. Often with 一 + measure word: 連一句都不懂.","Binibigyang-diin ang isang bagay na sukdulan o hindi inaasahan. Ilagay ito pagkatapos ng 連, at 都/也 bago ang pandiwa. Madalas may 一 + M: 連一句都不懂."],"tip":["連 = 'bahkan'. Ambil hal paling ekstrem, taruh setelah 連, lalu kunci dengan 都/也.","連 = 'even'. Take the most extreme item, put it after 連, then lock it with 都/也.","連 = 'kahit'. Kunin ang pinakasukdulan, ilagay pagkatapos ng 連, saka i-lock ng 都/也."],"warn":["✗ 他連吃飯沒有時間。→ ✓ 他連吃飯的時間都沒有。","✗ 他連吃飯沒有時間。→ ✓ 他連吃飯的時間都沒有。","✗ 他連吃飯沒有時間。→ ✓ 他連吃飯的時間都沒有。"],"logic":{"id":"Orang Indonesia bilang 'Dia bahkan nggak punya waktu makan', dengan objek tetap di belakang. Penutur Taiwan menarik hal yang mengejutkan ke depan setelah 連, lalu memakai 都/也 sebagai 'pengunci' sebelum verba. Tanpa 都/也, kalimatnya terasa belum selesai. Pikirkan urutannya: 連 [hal ekstrem] 都 [verba].","en":"English 'even' can sit near the verb with the object after it. Taiwanese pull the surprising item forward after 連 and use 都/也 as a lock before the verb; without it the sentence feels unfinished. Order: 連 [extreme item] 都 [verb]."},"ex":[["我忙到連午餐都忘了吃。","wǒ máng dào lián wǔ cān dōu wàng le chī","Aku sibuk sampai makan siang pun lupa.","I was so busy I even forgot to eat lunch.","Sa sobrang abala, nakalimutan ko pang kumain ng tanghalian.","daily"],["剛來台灣的時候，我連一句中文都聽不懂。","gāng lái tái wān de shí hòu wǒ lián yí jù zhōng wén dōu tīng bù dǒng","Waktu baru datang ke Taiwan, satu kalimat Mandarin pun aku nggak ngerti.","When I first came to Taiwan, I couldn't understand even one sentence of Chinese.","Noong bagong dating ako sa Taiwan, kahit isang pangungusap sa Chinese ay hindi ko maintindihan.","daily"],["這個問題連教授都不確定。","zhè ge wèn tí lián jiào shòu dōu bú què dìng","Soal ini bahkan profesor pun nggak yakin.","Even the professor isn't sure about this question.","Kahit ang propesor ay hindi sigurado sa tanong na ito.","campus"],["他連三用電表都不會用，怎麼做實驗？","tā lián sān yòng diàn biǎo dōu bú huì yòng zěn me zuò shí yàn","Multimeter aja dia nggak bisa pakai, gimana mau praktikum?","He can't even use a multimeter, how can he do experiments?","Kahit multimeter hindi niya magamit, paano siya mag-eeksperimento?","campus"],["這個異常連資深工程師也沒看過。","zhè ge yì cháng lián zī shēn gōng chéng shī yě méi kàn guò","Abnormal ini bahkan engineer senior pun belum pernah lihat.","Even senior engineers have never seen this abnormality.","Kahit ang senior engineer ay hindi pa nakakita ng ganitong abnormal.","fab"],["最近趕貨，我們連週末都要上班。","zuì jìn gǎn huò wǒ men lián zhōu mò dōu yào shàng bān","Lagi kejar order, akhir pekan pun kami harus kerja.","We're rushing orders lately, so we even work weekends.","Nagmamadali sa order ngayon, kaya kahit weekend ay may pasok kami.","fab"]],"drill":[{"q":"他太緊張了，＿自己的名字都寫錯了。","opts":["連","把","被"],"a":0,"why":"Menekankan hal ekstrem → 連…都."},{"q":"這台機台很舊，連說明書＿找不到了。","opts":["都","就","才"],"a":0,"why":"連 berpasangan dengan 都/也."},{"q":"我連一塊錢＿沒有。","opts":["也","才","就"],"a":0,"why":"連一…也沒有 = satu pun tidak ada."},{"q":"＿老師都不知道答案。","opts":["連","除了","對"],"a":0,"why":"Bahkan guru pun → 連."}]},{"lv":4,"k":"b1x_yueyue","form":"S + 越 + A + 越 + B","icon":"wave","name":["Makin A, makin B (越…越)","The more A, the more B (越…越)","Habang A, lalong B (越…越)"],"gloss":["B berubah mengikuti A. A biasanya verba atau kondisi, B biasanya kata sifat atau verba perasaan. Bisa satu subjek (我越聽越喜歡) atau dua subjek (電阻越大，電流就越小). Jangan menambah 很 sebelum B. Ini berbeda dari 越來越 (makin lama makin).","B changes along with A. A is usually a verb or condition; B an adjective or feeling verb. One subject (我越聽越喜歡) or two (電阻越大，電流就越小). Never add 很 before B. Different from 越來越 ('more and more over time').","Nagbabago ang B kasabay ng A. Karaniwang pandiwa o kondisyon ang A, pang-uri ang B. Puwedeng isa o dalawang paksa. Huwag maglagay ng 很 bago ang B. Iba ito sa 越來越."],"tip":["越來越 = waktu yang mendorong perubahan. 越A越B = A yang mendorong B. Cocok untuk rumus fisika!","越來越 = time drives the change. 越A越B = A drives B. Perfect for physics relations!","越來越 = panahon ang nagtutulak. 越A越B = A ang nagtutulak sa B. Bagay sa mga pormula sa physics!"],"warn":["✗ 他越說越很快。→ ✓ 他越說越快。","✗ 他越說越很快。→ ✓ 他越說越快。","✗ 他越說越很快。→ ✓ 他越說越快。"],"logic":{"id":"Bahasa Indonesia memakai 'makin… makin…' dengan struktur yang hampir sama, jadi pola ini mudah. Yang perlu diingat: 越 sudah berfungsi sebagai penanda derajat, jadi 很/非常 tidak boleh ditambahkan. Penutur Taiwan memakai pola ini untuk perasaan (越看越喜歡) dan juga hubungan teknis (溫度越高，反應越快). Kalau dua subjek berbeda, 就 sering ditambahkan sebelum 越 kedua.","en":"English 'the more…, the more…' is close. 越 already marks degree, so never add 很/非常. Taiwanese use it for feelings (越看越喜歡) and technical relations (溫度越高，反應越快). With two different subjects, 就 is often added before the second 越."},"ex":[["這首歌我越聽越喜歡。","zhè shǒu gē wǒ yuè tīng yuè xǐ huān","Lagu ini makin aku dengar makin suka.","The more I listen to this song, the more I like it.","Habang pinakikinggan ko ang kantang ito, lalo ko itong nagugustuhan.","daily"],["雨越下越大，我們先找地方躲一下。","yǔ yuè xià yuè dà wǒ men xiān zhǎo dì fāng duǒ yí xià","Hujannya makin deras, kita cari tempat berteduh dulu.","The rain is getting heavier; let's find somewhere to shelter.","Lumalakas ang ulan, maghanap muna tayo ng masisilungan.","daily"],["這本電子學我越看越不懂。","zhè běn diàn zǐ xué wǒ yuè kàn yuè bù dǒng","Buku elektronika ini makin aku baca makin nggak ngerti.","The more I read this electronics book, the less I understand.","Habang binabasa ko ang electronics book na ito, lalo akong hindi nakakaintindi.","campus"],["電阻越大，電流就越小。","diàn zǔ yuè dà diàn liú jiù yuè xiǎo","Makin besar resistansinya, makin kecil arusnya.","The greater the resistance, the smaller the current.","Habang lumalaki ang resistance, lumiliit ang current.","campus"],["這台機台越用越不穩，該做保養了。","zhè tái jī tái yuè yòng yuè bù wěn gāi zuò bǎo yǎng le","Mesin ini makin dipakai makin nggak stabil, sudah waktunya maintenance.","The more this tool is used, the less stable it gets; it's time for maintenance.","Habang ginagamit ang makina, lalong hindi stable; oras na ng maintenance.","fab"],["製程越先進，對無塵室的要求越高。","zhì chéng yuè xiān jìn duì wú chén shì de yāo qiú yuè gāo","Makin canggih prosesnya, makin tinggi standar cleanroom-nya.","The more advanced the process, the stricter the cleanroom requirements.","Habang mas advanced ang process, mas mahigpit ang requirements sa cleanroom.","fab"]],"drill":[{"q":"他＿跑越快。","opts":["越","更","很"],"a":0,"why":"Pola tetap 越A越B."},{"q":"這個遊戲越玩越＿。","opts":["好玩","很好玩","非常好玩"],"a":0,"why":"Tidak boleh 很/非常 setelah 越."},{"q":"溫度＿高，反應速度越快。","opts":["越","更","最"],"a":0,"why":"Dua subjek: 溫度越高，速度越快."},{"q":"雨越下越＿，我們回去吧。","opts":["大","很大","太大"],"a":0,"why":"越 + adjektiva polos."}]},{"lv":4,"k":"b1x_yiyang","form":"A + 跟 + B + 一樣／不一樣／差不多 (+ Vs)","icon":"scale","name":["Sama / beda / mirip (跟…一樣／不一樣／差不多)","Same / different / about the same (跟…一樣／不一樣／差不多)","Pareho / iba / halos pareho (跟…一樣／不一樣／差不多)"],"gloss":["Membandingkan kesamaan. A 跟 B 一樣 (+ sifat) = A sama (…nya) dengan B. 不一樣 = berbeda. 差不多 = kurang lebih sama / mirip. 跟 bisa diganti 和. Sifat yang dibandingkan ditaruh setelah 一樣/差不多: 一樣高, 差不多熱.","Compares similarity. A 跟 B 一樣 (+ adjective) = A is as … as B. 不一樣 = different. 差不多 = about the same. 跟 can be replaced by 和. The compared quality goes after 一樣/差不多: 一樣高, 差不多熱.","Naghahambing ng pagkakatulad. A 跟 B 一樣 (+ pang-uri) = pareho ang A at B. 不一樣 = magkaiba. 差不多 = halos pareho. Ang katangian ay pagkatapos ng 一樣/差不多."],"tip":["Urutan: [A] 跟 [B] 一樣 [sifat]. Sifat selalu paling belakang.","Order: [A] 跟 [B] 一樣 [quality]. The quality always comes last.","Ayos: [A] 跟 [B] 一樣 [katangian]. Laging nasa dulo ang katangian."],"warn":["✗ 我的手機一樣你的。→ ✓ 我的手機跟你的一樣。","✗ 我的手機一樣你的。→ ✓ 我的手機跟你的一樣。","✗ 我的手機一樣你的。→ ✓ 我的手機跟你的一樣。"],"logic":{"id":"Bahasa Indonesia bilang 'HP-ku sama dengan HP-mu' atau 'setinggi kamu', dengan 'sama' di tengah. Penutur Taiwan mengumpulkan kedua hal yang dibandingkan dulu (A 跟 B), baru memberi kesimpulan di akhir (一樣/不一樣/差不多). Kalau ada sifat yang dibandingkan, sifat itu ditaruh setelah 一樣. Jadi pikirkan: 'A dan B → hasilnya sama/beda'.","en":"English says 'A is the same as B' or 'as tall as B' with the comparison word in the middle. Taiwanese first gather both items (A 跟 B), then give the verdict at the end (一樣/不一樣/差不多), followed by any quality. Think: 'A and B → same/different'."},"ex":[["高雄的夏天跟雅加達差不多熱。","gāo xióng de xià tiān gēn yǎ jiā dá chà bù duō rè","Musim panas di Kaohsiung kurang lebih sepanas Jakarta.","Summer in Kaohsiung is about as hot as Jakarta.","Halos kasing-init ng Jakarta ang tag-init sa Kaohsiung.","daily"],["台灣的插座跟印尼的不一樣。","tái wān de chā zuò gēn yìn ní de bù yí yàng","Stopkontak di Taiwan beda dengan di Indonesia.","Taiwan's power sockets are different from Indonesia's.","Iba ang saksakan sa Taiwan kaysa sa Indonesia.","daily"],["這個實驗的步驟跟上次差不多。","zhè ge shí yàn de bù zòu gēn shàng cì chà bù duō","Langkah praktikum ini mirip dengan yang kemarin.","The steps of this experiment are about the same as last time.","Halos pareho sa nakaraan ang mga hakbang ng eksperimentong ito.","campus"],["串聯跟並聯的接法不一樣。","chuàn lián gēn bìng lián de jiē fǎ bù yí yàng","Cara menyambung seri dan paralel itu berbeda.","Series and parallel connections are wired differently.","Magkaiba ang pagkakabit ng series at parallel.","campus"],["新機台的產能跟舊的一樣，可是比較省電。","xīn jī tái de chǎn néng gēn jiù de yí yàng kě shì bǐ jiào shěng diàn","Kapasitas mesin baru sama dengan yang lama, tapi lebih hemat listrik.","The new tool has the same capacity as the old one but uses less power.","Pareho ang capacity ng bagong makina sa luma, pero mas tipid sa kuryente.","fab"],["夜班的工作內容跟白班差不多。","yè bān de gōng zuò nèi róng gēn bái bān chà bù duō","Isi pekerjaan shift malam kurang lebih sama dengan shift pagi.","Night-shift duties are about the same as day-shift ones.","Halos pareho ang trabaho sa night shift at day shift.","fab"]],"drill":[{"q":"我的想法＿你一樣。","opts":["跟","比","把"],"a":0,"why":"A 跟 B 一樣."},{"q":"他跟他哥哥＿高。","opts":["一樣","一點","比較"],"a":0,"why":"跟…一樣 + sifat."},{"q":"這兩台機台的型號＿一樣。","opts":["不","沒","別"],"a":0,"why":"Negasinya 不一樣."},{"q":"這次的結果跟上次＿，沒什麼變化。","opts":["差不多","一點","多了"],"a":0,"why":"Mirip/hampir sama → 差不多."}]},{"lv":4,"k":"b1x_meiyou_name","form":"A + 沒有 + B + (那麼／這麼) + Vs","icon":"no","name":["A tidak se-… B (沒有…那麼)","A is not as … as B (沒有…那麼)","Hindi kasing-… ng B ang A (沒有…那麼)"],"gloss":["Cara paling alami untuk perbandingan negatif dalam lisan. 那麼 untuk hal yang jauh atau sedang dibicarakan, 這麼 untuk yang dekat atau sekarang; keduanya boleh dihilangkan. Jangan memakai 比…不… untuk arti 'kurang dari'.","The most natural negative comparison in speech. 那麼 for something distant or being discussed, 這麼 for something near or current; both are optional. Don't use 比…不… to mean 'less than'.","Pinakanatural na negatibong paghahambing sa usapan. 那麼 para sa malayo o pinag-uusapan, 這麼 para sa malapit; puwedeng alisin. Huwag gamitin ang 比…不…."],"tip":["Mau bilang 'A tidak lebih … dari B'? Jangan 比…不…, pakai 沒有…那麼.","Want 'A isn't as … as B'? Not 比…不… — use 沒有…那麼.","Gusto mong sabihing 'hindi kasing-… ang A'? Hindi 比…不…, gamitin ang 沒有…那麼."],"warn":["✗ 台北比高雄不熱。→ ✓ 台北沒有高雄那麼熱。","✗ 台北比高雄不熱。→ ✓ 台北沒有高雄那麼熱。","✗ 台北比高雄不熱。→ ✓ 台北沒有高雄那麼熱。"],"logic":{"id":"Orang Indonesia cenderung menerjemahkan 'Taipei lebih tidak panas daripada Kaohsiung' atau 'Taipei tidak lebih panas'. Penutur Taiwan berpikir dengan patokan: B adalah standar, lalu A 'tidak mencapai' standar itu — 沒有 B 那麼…. Bentuk 不比 memang ada, tapi artinya membantah ('belum tentu lebih…'), bukan 'kurang dari'. Untuk percakapan sehari-hari, 沒有…那麼 adalah pilihan paling aman.","en":"Learners try 'A 比 B 不 hot'. Taiwanese think with a benchmark: B is the standard and A doesn't reach it — A 沒有 B 那麼…. 不比 exists but means 'not necessarily more', a rebuttal. In daily talk 沒有…那麼 is the safe choice."},"ex":[["台北沒有高雄那麼熱。","tái běi méi yǒu gāo xióng nà me rè","Taipei nggak sepanas Kaohsiung.","Taipei isn't as hot as Kaohsiung.","Hindi kasing-init ng Kaohsiung ang Taipei.","daily"],["這家的牛肉麵沒有我們學校附近那家好吃。","zhè jiā de niú ròu miàn méi yǒu wǒ men xué xiào fù jìn nà jiā hǎo chī","Mi daging sapi di sini nggak seenak yang dekat kampus kita.","This place's beef noodles aren't as good as the one near our school.","Hindi kasing-sarap ng beef noodles malapit sa school namin ang dito.","daily"],["今天的考試沒有上次那麼難。","jīn tiān de kǎo shì méi yǒu shàng cì nà me nán","Ujian hari ini nggak sesusah yang kemarin.","Today's exam wasn't as hard as last time.","Hindi kasing-hirap ng nakaraan ang exam ngayon.","campus"],["焊接沒有我想的這麼簡單。","hàn jiē méi yǒu wǒ xiǎng de zhè me jiǎn dān","Menyolder ternyata nggak segampang yang aku kira.","Soldering isn't as easy as I thought.","Hindi kasing-dali ng inakala ko ang pag-solder.","campus"],["這批貨的良率沒有上個月那麼高。","zhè pī huò de liáng lǜ méi yǒu shàng ge yuè nà me gāo","Yield lot ini nggak setinggi bulan lalu.","This lot's yield isn't as high as last month's.","Hindi kasing-taas ng nakaraang buwan ang yield ng batch na ito.","fab"],["夜班沒有你想的那麼累，習慣就好。","yè bān méi yǒu nǐ xiǎng de nà me lèi xí guàn jiù hǎo","Shift malam nggak secapek yang kamu kira, nanti juga terbiasa.","Night shift isn't as tiring as you think; you'll get used to it.","Hindi kasing-pagod ng iniisip mo ang night shift, masasanay ka rin.","fab"]],"drill":[{"q":"我的中文＿他那麼好。","opts":["沒有","不","比"],"a":0,"why":"Perbandingan negatif → 沒有…那麼."},{"q":"這台機台沒有那台＿快。","opts":["那麼","一點","多了"],"a":0,"why":"沒有 B 那麼 + sifat."},{"q":"高雄的冬天＿台北冷。","opts":["沒有","不","不是"],"a":0,"why":"A 沒有 B (那麼) 冷."},{"q":"這次報告沒有上次＿難，大家都很快就寫完了。","opts":["那麼","多了","得多"],"a":0,"why":"得多/多了 hanya dipakai dengan 比."}]},{"lv":4,"k":"b1x_bi_degree","form":"A + 比 + B + Vs + 一點／得多／多了／(jumlah)","icon":"arrows","name":["Lebih … sedikit / jauh lebih … (比…一點／得多)","A bit / much more … than (比…一點／得多)","Mas … nang kaunti / mas … nang malaki (比…一點／得多)"],"gloss":["Menambahkan ukuran pada perbandingan 比. 一點 = sedikit lebih. 得多 / 多了 = jauh lebih (多了 lebih lisan). Bisa juga angka: 貴一百塊, 少兩個步驟. Tidak boleh memakai 很/非常/太 bersama 比. Untuk verba: A V得比B Vs一點.","Adds degree to a 比 comparison. 一點 = a bit more. 得多 / 多了 = much more (多了 is more colloquial). Numbers also work: 貴一百塊, 少兩個步驟. Never use 很/非常/太 with 比. With verbs: A V得比B Vs一點.","Nagdadagdag ng antas sa paghahambing na 比. 一點 = kaunti pa. 得多 / 多了 = mas malaki. Puwede rin ang numero. Bawal ang 很/非常/太 kasama ng 比."],"tip":["Ukuran selalu SETELAH sifat: 高一點, 快多了, 貴一百塊. 很 dilarang masuk!","The amount always comes AFTER the adjective: 高一點, 快多了, 貴一百塊. 很 is banned!","Laging pagkatapos ng pang-uri ang dami: 高一點, 快多了. Bawal ang 很!"],"warn":["✗ 他比我很高。→ ✓ 他比我高得多。／✓ 他比我高一點。","✗ 他比我很高。→ ✓ 他比我高得多。／✓ 他比我高一點。","✗ 他比我很高。→ ✓ 他比我高得多。／✓ 他比我高一點。"],"logic":{"id":"Orang Indonesia bilang 'jauh lebih tinggi' atau 'sedikit lebih mahal', dengan penguat di depan. Penutur Taiwan menaruh sifat dulu, lalu 'seberapa besar' selisihnya di belakang: 高一點, 快多了, 貴一百塊. Karena 比 sudah berarti 'lebih', kata 很 akan terasa bertabrakan. Ini sangat berguna di pabrik untuk menyebut selisih data dengan tepat.","en":"English puts 'much/a bit' before the adjective. Taiwanese say the adjective first, then how big the gap is: 高一點, 快多了, 貴一百塊. Since 比 already means 'more', 很 clashes. Very useful in fabs for stating data differences precisely."},"ex":[["騎機車比走路快多了。","qí jī chē bǐ zǒu lù kuài duō le","Naik motor jauh lebih cepat daripada jalan kaki.","Riding a scooter is way faster than walking.","Mas mabilis nang malaki ang pagmomotor kaysa maglakad.","daily"],["這件比那件貴一點，可是品質比較好。","zhè jiàn bǐ nà jiàn guì yì diǎn kě shì pǐn zhí bǐ jiào hǎo","Yang ini sedikit lebih mahal dari yang itu, tapi kualitasnya lebih bagus.","This one is a bit pricier than that one, but the quality is better.","Medyo mas mahal ito kaysa roon, pero mas maganda ang kalidad.","daily"],["這學期的課比上學期難得多。","zhè xué qí de kè bǐ shàng xué qí nán de duō","Kuliah semester ini jauh lebih susah daripada semester lalu.","This semester's courses are much harder than last semester's.","Mas mahirap nang malaki ang mga klase ngayong semestre kaysa noong nakaraan.","campus"],["他焊得比我快一點。","tā hàn de bǐ wǒ kuài yì diǎn","Dia menyolder sedikit lebih cepat dari aku.","He solders a bit faster than me.","Medyo mas mabilis siyang mag-solder kaysa sa akin.","campus"],["換了新零件以後，良率比以前高多了。","huàn le xīn líng jiàn yǐ hòu liáng lǜ bǐ yǐ qián gāo duō le","Setelah ganti part baru, yield jauh lebih tinggi dari sebelumnya.","After replacing the part, the yield is much higher than before.","Pagkapalit ng bagong piyesa, mas mataas nang malaki ang yield kaysa dati.","fab"],["這個製程比舊的少兩個步驟。","zhè ge zhì chéng bǐ jiù de shǎo liǎng ge bù zòu","Proses ini dua langkah lebih sedikit daripada yang lama.","This process has two fewer steps than the old one.","Dalawang hakbang na mas kaunti ang process na ito kaysa sa luma.","fab"]],"drill":[{"q":"今天比昨天冷＿。","opts":["多了","很","非常"],"a":0,"why":"Penguat diletakkan setelah sifat: 冷多了."},{"q":"他比我高＿，只差兩公分。","opts":["一點","得多","多了"],"a":0,"why":"Selisih kecil → 一點."},{"q":"新機台比舊機台快＿多。","opts":["得","的","地"],"a":0,"why":"Bentuknya 快得多."},{"q":"這家店比那家＿。","opts":["便宜得多","很便宜","非常便宜"],"a":0,"why":"Tidak boleh 很/非常 dengan 比."}]},{"lv":4,"k":"b1x_suggest","form":"(你) + 最好 + (不要) + V…／(我們) + 還是 + V… + 吧","icon":"chat","name":["Memberi saran: sebaiknya / mending… aja (最好／還是…吧)","Giving advice: you'd better / let's just… (最好／還是…吧)","Pagpapayo: mas mabuti / … na lang (最好／還是…吧)"],"gloss":["Dua cara memberi saran yang sangat lisan. 最好 = 'sebaiknya', saran kuat atau peringatan halus; negatifnya 最好不要/最好別. 還是…吧 = 'mending… aja', dipakai setelah menimbang beberapa pilihan. 吧 di akhir membuat nada lebih lembut.","Two very spoken ways to advise. 最好 = 'you'd better', a strong suggestion or soft warning; negative 最好不要/最好別. 還是…吧 = 'let's just…', after weighing options. Final 吧 softens the tone.","Dalawang paraan ng pagpapayo. 最好 = 'mas mabuti', malakas na payo o mahinang babala; negatibo 最好不要. 還是…吧 = '… na lang', pagkatapos timbangin ang mga opsyon. Pinalalambot ng 吧 ang tono."],"tip":["還是…吧 = 'setelah dipikir-pikir, pilih ini aja'. 最好 = 'saran terbaik dariku'. Jangan lupa 吧!","還是…吧 = 'after thinking it over, let's go with this'. 最好 = 'my best advice'. Don't forget 吧!","還是…吧 = 'pagkatapos pag-isipan, ito na lang'. 最好 = 'pinakamainam kong payo'."],"warn":["✗ 我們還是搭計程車。(terdengar memerintah) → ✓ 我們還是搭計程車吧。","✗ 我們還是搭計程車。(sounds bossy) → ✓ 我們還是搭計程車吧。","✗ 我們還是搭計程車。(parang utos) → ✓ 我們還是搭計程車吧。"],"logic":{"id":"Orang Indonesia sering memberi saran dengan 'kamu harus…', yang dalam Mandarin (你要/你應該) bisa terdengar terlalu keras. Penutur Taiwan lebih suka melunakkan: 最好 memberi alasan tersirat ('lebih aman begitu'), dan 還是…吧 menunjukkan bahwa kamu sudah menimbang pilihan lain. Di pabrik, ini cara sopan untuk mengusulkan sesuatu ke senior tanpa terdengar menggurui.","en":"Learners often advise with 你要/你應該, which can sound harsh. Taiwanese soften it: 最好 implies 'it's safer that way', and 還是…吧 shows you've weighed other options. In a fab, it's a polite way to suggest something to a senior without lecturing."},"ex":[["外面在下雨，我們還是叫計程車吧。","wài miàn zài xià yǔ wǒ men hái shì jiào jì chéng chē ba","Di luar hujan, mending kita panggil taksi aja.","It's raining outside; let's just call a taxi.","Umuulan sa labas, tumawag na lang tayo ng taxi.","daily"],["你發燒了，最好去看醫生。","nǐ fā shāo le zuì hǎo qù kàn yī shēng","Kamu demam, sebaiknya ke dokter.","You have a fever; you'd better see a doctor.","May lagnat ka, mas mabuting magpatingin ka sa doktor.","daily"],["報告明天就要交，你最好今天寫完。","bào gào míng tiān jiù yào jiāo nǐ zuì hǎo jīn tiān xiě wán","Laporannya dikumpul besok, sebaiknya kamu selesaikan hari ini.","The report is due tomorrow; you'd better finish it today.","Ipapasa bukas ang report, mas mabuting tapusin mo ngayon.","campus"],["電路還沒檢查好，還是先別通電吧。","diàn lù hái méi jiǎn chá hǎo hái shì xiān bié tōng diàn ba","Rangkaiannya belum dicek, mending jangan dialiri listrik dulu.","The circuit hasn't been checked yet; let's not power it on yet.","Hindi pa nasusuri ang circuit, huwag muna nating kuryentehan.","campus"],["這個異常不太對，還是先問一下主管吧。","zhè ge yì cháng bú tài duì hái shì xiān wèn yí xià zhǔ guǎn ba","Abnormal ini agak aneh, mending tanya atasan dulu.","This abnormality doesn't look right; let's ask the supervisor first.","Parang mali ang abnormal na ito, tanungin muna natin ang supervisor.","fab"],["進無塵室以前，你最好先去洗手間。","jìn wú chén shì yǐ qián nǐ zuì hǎo xiān qù xǐ shǒu jiān","Sebelum masuk cleanroom, sebaiknya kamu ke toilet dulu.","Before entering the cleanroom, you'd better use the restroom first.","Bago pumasok sa cleanroom, mas mabuting mag-CR ka muna.","fab"]],"drill":[{"q":"太晚了，我們＿回家吧。","opts":["還是","或是","而是"],"a":0,"why":"Saran setelah menimbang → 還是…吧."},{"q":"你＿不要遲到，主管很在意。","opts":["最好","最近","最後"],"a":0,"why":"Saran/peringatan → 最好不要."},{"q":"這台機台怪怪的，還是先停機＿。","opts":["吧","嗎","呢"],"a":0,"why":"還是…吧 melunakkan saran."},{"q":"天氣很熱，你＿多喝水。","opts":["最好","最多","最少"],"a":0,"why":"最好 = sebaiknya."}]},{"lv":4,"k":"b1x_causative","form":"A + 讓／叫／使 + B + V／Vs","icon":"bolt","name":["Menyuruh / membuat / membiarkan (讓／叫／使)","Make / let / tell someone to (讓／叫／使)","Pagpapagawa / pagpapahintulot (讓／叫／使)"],"gloss":["Kalimat kausatif: A membuat B melakukan atau merasakan sesuatu. 叫 = menyuruh (perintah, sangat lisan). 讓 = membiarkan/mengizinkan atau membuat merasa (paling umum). 使 = menyebabkan (gaya tulisan/laporan, biasanya perubahan keadaan).","Causatives: A makes B do or feel something. 叫 = tell/order (very spoken). 讓 = let/allow, or make someone feel (most common). 使 = cause (written/report style, usually a change of state).","Kausatibo: pinapagawa o pinaparamdam ng A ang B. 叫 = utusan. 讓 = payagan o paramdamin (pinakakaraniwan). 使 = maging sanhi (pormal, pagbabago ng kalagayan)."],"tip":["叫 = suruh. 讓 = biar / bikin (perasaan). 使 = 'menyebabkan' (gaya laporan).","叫 = tell to. 讓 = let / make feel. 使 = cause (report style).","叫 = utusan. 讓 = payagan / paramdamin. 使 = sanhi (pang-report)."],"warn":["✗ 這部電影做我很難過。→ ✓ 這部電影讓我很難過。","✗ 這部電影做我很難過。→ ✓ 這部電影讓我很難過。","✗ 這部電影做我很難過。→ ✓ 這部電影讓我很難過。"],"logic":{"id":"Dalam bahasa Indonesia, 'membuat' bisa berarti 'membikin barang' maupun 'menyebabkan perasaan', sehingga orang tergoda memakai 做. Penutur Taiwan tidak pernah memakai 做 untuk ini: perasaan dan izin memakai 讓, perintah memakai 叫, dan perubahan hasil dalam laporan memakai 使. Strukturnya selalu A + kata kausatif + B + verba/sifat, tanpa 'untuk' di tengah.","en":"English 'make' covers both producing things and causing feelings, so learners reach for 做. Taiwanese never use 做 here: feelings and permission take 讓, orders take 叫, and result changes in reports take 使. Structure: A + causative + B + verb/adjective, nothing in between."},"ex":[["我媽叫我早點回家。","wǒ mā jiào wǒ zǎo diǎn huí jiā","Ibuku nyuruh aku pulang lebih awal.","My mom told me to come home early.","Pinauwi ako nang maaga ni Nanay.","daily"],["這部電影讓我很想家。","zhè bù diàn yǐng ràng wǒ hěn xiǎng jiā","Film ini bikin aku kangen rumah.","This movie makes me homesick.","Pinapa-miss ako ng pelikulang ito sa bahay.","daily"],["老師讓我們用手機查資料。","lǎo shī ràng wǒ men yòng shǒu jī chá zī liào","Dosen membolehkan kami pakai HP buat cari data.","The teacher lets us use our phones to look things up.","Pinapayagan kami ng guro na gumamit ng phone para maghanap ng impormasyon.","campus"],["助教叫我們先把電源關掉。","zhù jiào jiào wǒ men xiān bǎ diàn yuán guān diào","Asisten dosen menyuruh kami matikan power dulu.","The TA told us to switch off the power first.","Inutusan kami ng TA na patayin muna ang power.","campus"],["主管叫我明天上夜班。","zhǔ guǎn jiào wǒ míng tiān shàng yè bān","Atasan menyuruh aku masuk shift malam besok.","My supervisor told me to work the night shift tomorrow.","Pinag-night shift ako ng supervisor bukas.","fab"],["新的參數使良率提高了百分之五。","xīn de cān shù shǐ liáng lǜ tí gāo le bǎi fēn zhī wǔ","Parameter baru menyebabkan yield naik lima persen.","The new parameters raised the yield by five percent.","Dahil sa bagong parameters, tumaas nang limang porsiyento ang yield.","fab"]],"drill":[{"q":"他的話＿我很感動。","opts":["讓","把","被"],"a":0,"why":"Menyebabkan perasaan → 讓."},{"q":"主管＿我去倉庫拿零件。","opts":["叫","被","對"],"a":0,"why":"Menyuruh → 叫."},{"q":"新製程＿成本降低了不少。","opts":["使","叫","被"],"a":0,"why":"Gaya laporan, perubahan keadaan → 使."},{"q":"爸媽不＿我晚上一個人騎機車。","opts":["讓","使","被"],"a":0,"why":"Mengizinkan → 讓."}]},{"lv":5,"k":"b1x_ba_result","form":"S + 把 + O + V + 成／到／在／給 + (hasil／tempat／orang)","icon":"blocks","name":["把 lanjutan: V成／V到／V在／V給","Advanced 把: V成／V到／V在／V給","Advanced 把: V成／V到／V在／V給"],"gloss":["Objek dipindahkan atau diubah menuju hasil akhir. V成 = menjadi (翻譯成, 換成). V到 = sampai ke tempat/tingkat (送到, 調到). V在 = diletakkan/berada di (放在, 寫在). V給 = diserahkan ke orang (交給, 傳給). Dengan komplemen ini, 把 hampir wajib.","The object is moved or changed toward an end point. V成 = into (翻譯成, 換成). V到 = to a place/level (送到, 調到). V在 = placed at (放在, 寫在). V給 = handed to someone (交給, 傳給). With these complements 把 is practically required.","Inililipat o binabago ang layon tungo sa huling resulta. V成 = maging. V到 = hanggang sa lugar/antas. V在 = ilagay sa. V給 = ibigay sa tao. Halos kailangan ang 把 sa mga ito."],"tip":["Tanya: objeknya pergi ke mana? 成 (jadi apa), 到 (sampai mana), 在 (diam di mana), 給 (ke siapa).","Ask: where does the object end up? 成 (into what), 到 (to where), 在 (rests where), 給 (to whom).","Itanong: saan napupunta ang layon? 成 (magiging ano), 到 (hanggang saan), 在 (nasaan), 給 (kanino)."],"warn":["✗ 我放手機在桌上。→ ✓ 我把手機放在桌上。","✗ 我放手機在桌上。→ ✓ 我把手機放在桌上。","✗ 我放手機在桌上。→ ✓ 我把手機放在桌上。"],"logic":{"id":"Bahasa Indonesia berpola 'taruh HP di meja': verba – objek – tempat. Dalam Mandarin, setelah verba hanya boleh ada SATU hal, dan tempat/hasil harus menempel langsung pada verba (放在桌上). Karena itu penutur Taiwan menarik objek ke depan dengan 把, lalu verba + 在/到/成/給 + tujuan. Pikirkan 把 sebagai 'pegang objeknya dulu', lalu katakan ke mana objek itu berakhir.","en":"English 'put the phone on the table' is verb–object–place. In Mandarin only ONE thing can follow the verb, and the place/result must attach directly to it (放在桌上). So Taiwanese pull the object forward with 把, then verb + 在/到/成/給 + destination. Think of 把 as 'grab the object first', then say where it ends up."},"ex":[["你把鑰匙放在哪裡了？","nǐ bǎ yào shi fàng zài nǎ lǐ le","Kuncinya kamu taruh di mana?","Where did you put the keys?","Saan mo inilagay ang susi?","daily"],["請幫我把這段話翻譯成印尼文。","qǐng bāng wǒ bǎ zhè duàn huà fān yì chéng yìn ní wén","Tolong terjemahkan kalimat ini ke bahasa Indonesia.","Please help me translate this passage into Indonesian.","Pakisalin mo ito sa Indonesian.","daily"],["做完實驗，把三用電表放在桌上就好。","zuò wán shí yàn bǎ sān yòng diàn biǎo fàng zài zhuō shàng jiù hǎo","Habis praktikum, taruh multimeternya di meja aja.","After the experiment, just leave the multimeter on the table.","Pagkatapos ng eksperimento, ilagay mo na lang ang multimeter sa mesa.","campus"],["請把實驗報告傳給助教。","qǐng bǎ shí yàn bào gào chuán gěi zhù jiào","Tolong kirim laporan praktikum ke asisten dosen.","Please send the lab report to the TA.","Pakipadala ang lab report sa TA.","campus"],["把溫度調到兩百度，再觀察十分鐘。","bǎ wēn dù tiáo dào liǎng bǎi dù zài guān chá shí fēn zhōng","Setel suhunya sampai 200 derajat, lalu amati sepuluh menit.","Set the temperature to 200 degrees, then observe for ten minutes.","I-set ang temperatura sa 200 degrees, saka obserbahan nang sampung minuto.","fab"],["你把這批晶圓送到黃光區。","nǐ bǎ zhè pī jīng yuán sòng dào huáng guāng qū","Antar lot wafer ini ke area litografi.","Take this lot of wafers to the photo (lithography) area.","Dalhin mo ang batch ng wafers na ito sa photo area.","fab"],["記得把異常寫在交接本上。","jì de bǎ yì cháng xiě zài jiāo jiē běn shàng","Jangan lupa tulis abnormalnya di buku serah terima.","Remember to write the abnormality in the handover log.","Tandaan mong isulat ang abnormal sa handover log.","fab"]],"drill":[{"q":"請把這句話翻譯＿中文。","opts":["成","在","給"],"a":0,"why":"Berubah menjadi → V成."},{"q":"我把手機放＿桌上了。","opts":["在","成","給"],"a":0,"why":"Diletakkan di tempat → V在."},{"q":"你把這份文件交＿主管。","opts":["給","成","在"],"a":0,"why":"Diserahkan ke orang → V給."},{"q":"請把機台的壓力調＿正常範圍。","opts":["到","成","給"],"a":0,"why":"Sampai ke tingkat tertentu → V到."},{"q":"我＿書放在包包裡了。","opts":["把","被","讓"],"a":0,"why":"Objek ditarik ke depan → 把."}]},{"lv":5,"k":"b1x_passive_speech","form":"S (penerima) + 被／讓／給 + (pelaku) + V + 了／komplemen","icon":"arrows","name":["Pasif dalam lisan: 被／讓／給","Passive in speech: 被／讓／給","Passive sa pananalita: 被／讓／給"],"gloss":["Dalam percakapan Taiwan, selain 被 orang juga sering memakai 讓 atau 給, biasanya untuk kejadian yang tidak menyenangkan. Dengan 被 dan 給, pelaku boleh tidak disebut; dengan 讓, pelaku HARUS disebut (讓人, 讓他). Verba hampir selalu diikuti 了 atau komplemen hasil.","In Taiwanese conversation, besides 被 people often use 讓 or 給, usually for unpleasant events. With 被 and 給 the agent can be omitted; with 讓 the agent MUST appear (讓人, 讓他). The verb almost always takes 了 or a result complement.","Sa usapan sa Taiwan, bukod sa 被 ginagamit din ang 讓 o 給, kadalasan para sa di-kanais-nais na pangyayari. Sa 被 at 給 puwedeng walang gumagawa; sa 讓 dapat may gumagawa. Laging may 了 o complement ang pandiwa."],"tip":["被 = netral, bisa tanpa pelaku. 讓 = wajib ada pelaku. 給 = santai sekali, sering di rumah/teman.","被 = neutral, agent optional. 讓 = agent required. 給 = very casual, among family/friends.","被 = neutral, puwedeng walang gumagawa. 讓 = dapat may gumagawa. 給 = kaswal na kaswal."],"warn":["✗ 我的機車讓偷了。→ ✓ 我的機車被偷了。／✓ 我的機車讓人偷了。","✗ 我的機車讓偷了。→ ✓ 我的機車被偷了。／✓ 我的機車讓人偷了。","✗ 我的機車讓偷了。→ ✓ 我的機車被偷了。／✓ 我的機車讓人偷了。"],"logic":{"id":"Bahasa Indonesia memakai pasif di- untuk hampir semua hal ('laporannya sudah dikirim'). Penutur Taiwan jauh lebih jarang memakai pasif; mereka memakainya terutama saat sesuatu yang buruk terjadi pada subjek (dicuri, dimarahi, rusak). Untuk hal netral, mereka cukup bilang 報告寄了 tanpa 被. Dalam lisan, 讓 dan 給 terdengar lebih alami daripada 被, tapi ingat aturan pelaku untuk 讓.","en":"English uses passives fairly freely. Taiwanese use them much less, mainly when something bad happens to the subject (stolen, scolded, damaged); for neutral things they just say 報告寄了 without 被. In speech 讓 and 給 sound more natural than 被, but 讓 needs an explicit agent."},"ex":[["我的機車被偷了！","wǒ de jī chē bèi tōu le","Motorku dicuri!","My scooter got stolen!","Ninakaw ang motor ko!","daily"],["我的蛋糕給我弟吃掉了。","wǒ de dàn gāo gěi wǒ dì chī diào le","Kueku dihabisin adikku.","My cake got eaten by my little brother.","Kinain ng kapatid ko ang cake ko.","daily"],["我昨天上課滑手機，被老師抓到了。","wǒ zuó tiān shàng kè huá shǒu jī bèi lǎo shī zhuā dào le","Kemarin aku main HP di kelas, ketahuan dosen.","I was scrolling my phone in class yesterday and got caught by the teacher.","Nag-cellphone ako sa klase kahapon at nahuli ako ng guro.","campus"],["保險絲又讓他燒斷了。","bǎo xiǎn sī yòu ràng tā shāo duàn le","Sekeringnya diputusin dia lagi.","He blew the fuse again.","Napaputok na naman niya ang fuse.","campus"],["那片晶圓被刮傷了，不能用了。","nà piàn jīng yuán bèi guā shāng le bù néng yòng le","Wafer itu tergores, sudah nggak bisa dipakai.","That wafer got scratched and can't be used.","Nagasgas ang wafer na iyon, hindi na magagamit.","fab"],["這個問題讓主管發現了，大家都被罵了。","zhè ge wèn tí ràng zhǔ guǎn fā xiàn le dà jiā dōu bèi mà le","Masalah ini ketahuan atasan, semua orang kena marah.","The supervisor found out about this problem, and everyone got scolded.","Nalaman ng supervisor ang problema, at napagalitan kaming lahat.","fab"]],"drill":[{"q":"我的傘＿人拿走了。","opts":["被","把","對"],"a":0,"why":"Pasif → 被 (+ pelaku 人)."},{"q":"錢包讓＿偷了。","opts":["小偷","了","被"],"a":0,"why":"Setelah 讓 pelaku wajib disebut."},{"q":"我的飲料＿我室友喝完了。","opts":["給","把","對"],"a":0,"why":"Pasif santai → 給."},{"q":"他遲到，被主管罵＿。","opts":["了","過","著"],"a":0,"why":"Verba pasif biasanya diikuti 了."}]},{"lv":4,"k":"b1x_dui","form":"對 + orang + 來說／對 + N + (很)有興趣／對 + N + 有影響","icon":"pin","name":["Bagi… / tertarik pada… / berpengaruh pada… (對…來說／有興趣／有影響)","For… / interested in… / affects… (對…來說／有興趣／有影響)","Para sa… / interesado sa… / may epekto sa… (對…)"],"gloss":["Tiga pola penting dengan 對. 對 + orang + 來說 = 'bagi / menurut sudut pandang…'. 對 + N + 有興趣 = 'tertarik pada'. 對 + N + 有影響 / 影響很大 = 'berpengaruh pada'. Frasa 對… selalu ditaruh SEBELUM verba atau kata sifat.","Three key patterns with 對. 對 + person + 來說 = 'for / from the viewpoint of'. 對 + N + 有興趣 = 'interested in'. 對 + N + 有影響 / 影響很大 = 'has an effect on'. The 對… phrase always comes BEFORE the verb or adjective.","Tatlong mahalagang pattern ng 對. 對 + tao + 來說 = 'para sa'. 對 + N + 有興趣 = 'interesado sa'. 對 + N + 有影響 = 'may epekto sa'. Laging bago ang pandiwa ang 對…."],"tip":["Target dulu, perasaan/efek belakangan: 我 [對半導體] 有興趣.","Target first, feeling/effect last: 我 [對半導體] 有興趣.","Target muna, damdamin/epekto pagkatapos: 我 [對半導體] 有興趣."],"warn":["✗ 我有興趣對半導體。→ ✓ 我對半導體有興趣。","✗ 我有興趣對半導體。→ ✓ 我對半導體有興趣。","✗ 我有興趣對半導體。→ ✓ 我對半導體有興趣。"],"logic":{"id":"Bahasa Indonesia bilang 'Aku tertarik pada semikonduktor' — perasaan dulu, sasaran belakangan. Penutur Taiwan menyebut sasaran lebih dulu dengan 對, baru perasaan atau efeknya: 我對半導體有興趣. Hal yang sama berlaku untuk 'berpengaruh pada' (對良率有影響) dan 'bagi saya' (對我來說). Jadi biasakan: siapa/apa sasarannya → baru kata kerjanya.","en":"English says 'interested IN X' with the target after. Taiwanese name the target first with 對, then the feeling or effect: 我對半導體有興趣. Same for 'affects' (對良率有影響) and 'for me' (對我來說). Habit: target → then the verb."},"ex":[["對我來說，中文最難的是聲調。","duì wǒ lái shuō zhōng wén zuì nán de shì shēng diào","Buat aku, yang paling susah dari bahasa Mandarin itu nadanya.","For me, the hardest part of Chinese is the tones.","Para sa akin, ang pinakamahirap sa Chinese ay ang tono.","daily"],["熬夜對身體有不好的影響。","áo yè duì shēn tǐ yǒu bù hǎo de yǐng xiǎng","Begadang berpengaruh buruk bagi tubuh.","Staying up late has a bad effect on your body.","May masamang epekto sa katawan ang pagpupuyat.","daily"],["我對自動控制很有興趣。","wǒ duì zì dòng kòng zhì hěn yǒu xìng qù","Aku sangat tertarik dengan kontrol otomatis.","I'm very interested in automatic control.","Interesado ako sa automatic control.","campus"],["對新生來說，這門課有點難。","duì xīn shēng lái shuō zhè mén kè yǒu diǎn nán","Bagi mahasiswa baru, mata kuliah ini agak susah.","For freshmen, this course is a bit hard.","Para sa mga bagong estudyante, medyo mahirap ang klaseng ito.","campus"],["濕度對光阻的品質影響很大。","shī dù duì guāng zǔ de pǐn zhí yǐng xiǎng hěn dà","Kelembapan sangat berpengaruh pada kualitas photoresist.","Humidity greatly affects photoresist quality.","Malaki ang epekto ng humidity sa kalidad ng photoresist.","fab"],["對工程師來說，交接清楚非常重要。","duì gōng chéng shī lái shuō jiāo jiē qīng chǔ fēi cháng zhòng yào","Bagi engineer, serah terima yang jelas itu sangat penting.","For engineers, a clear handover is extremely important.","Para sa mga engineer, napakahalaga ng malinaw na handover.","fab"]],"drill":[{"q":"＿我來說，騎機車比搭公車方便。","opts":["對","跟","給"],"a":0,"why":"對…來說 = bagi…."},{"q":"他對日本文化很有＿。","opts":["興趣","喜歡","好奇"],"a":0,"why":"對…有興趣 = tertarik pada."},{"q":"溫度＿良率有很大的影響。","opts":["對","跟","被"],"a":0,"why":"對…有影響."},{"q":"對外國人＿，台語很難。","opts":["來說","以外","的話"],"a":0,"why":"對…來說."}]},{"lv":5,"k":"b1x_guanyu_duiyu","form":"關於 + topik，…／關於 + topik + 的 + N／對於 + sasaran，S + …","icon":"book","name":["Tentang / terhadap (關於／對於)","About / regarding (關於／對於)","Tungkol sa / hinggil sa (關於／對於)"],"gloss":["關於 = 'tentang / soal' (topik pembicaraan). Biasanya di awal kalimat, atau sebagai atribut: 關於X的書. 對於 = 'terhadap' (sasaran sikap atau tindakan), versi formal dari 對. Keduanya sering dipakai di rapat, email, dan presentasi.","關於 = 'about / regarding' (topic). It usually opens the sentence or forms an attribute: 關於X的書. 對於 = 'toward / with regard to' (target of an attitude or action), a formal 對. Both are common in meetings, email and presentations.","關於 = 'tungkol sa' (paksa ng usapan), karaniwang nasa simula o bilang 關於X的書. 對於 = 'hinggil sa' (target ng saloobin o kilos), pormal na 對. Karaniwan sa meeting, email at presentasyon."],"tip":["關於 = topik ('soal…, nih'). 對於 = sasaran sikap ('terhadap…'). 關於 jangan ditaruh setelah subjek.","關於 = topic ('as for…'). 對於 = target of attitude ('toward…'). Don't put 關於 after the subject.","關於 = paksa. 對於 = target ng saloobin. Huwag ilagay ang 關於 pagkatapos ng paksa."],"warn":["✗ 我關於這個問題有一個想法。→ ✓ 關於這個問題，我有一個想法。","✗ 我關於這個問題有一個想法。→ ✓ 關於這個問題，我有一個想法。","✗ 我關於這個問題有一個想法。→ ✓ 關於這個問題，我有一個想法。"],"logic":{"id":"Dalam bahasa Indonesia, 'tentang' dan 'terhadap' bisa muncul di tengah kalimat dengan bebas. Penutur Taiwan memakai 關於 sebagai 'judul' di depan kalimat: mereka umumkan topiknya dulu, lalu bicara. 對於 lebih seperti 對: menandai sasaran yang akan diberi sikap atau perlakuan, dan bisa muncul setelah subjek. Di rapat pabrik, 關於這次的異常… adalah pembuka yang sangat umum.","en":"English 'about' and 'regarding' float freely. Taiwanese use 關於 as a headline at the front: announce the topic, then talk. 對於 works like 對, marking the target of an attitude or treatment, and can follow the subject. In fab meetings, 關於這次的異常… is a very common opener."},"ex":[["關於租房子的事，我們晚上再聊。","guān yú zū fáng zi de shì wǒ men wǎn shàng zài liáo","Soal sewa rumah, kita ngobrol lagi nanti malam.","About renting the apartment, let's talk tonight.","Tungkol sa pag-upa ng bahay, mag-usap tayo mamayang gabi.","daily"],["我想看一些關於台灣歷史的影片。","wǒ xiǎng kàn yì xiē guān yú tái wān lì shǐ de yǐng piàn","Aku mau nonton video tentang sejarah Taiwan.","I want to watch some videos about Taiwanese history.","Gusto kong manood ng mga video tungkol sa kasaysayan ng Taiwan.","daily"],["關於期末專題，教授有幾點要求。","guān yú qí mò zhuān tí jiào shòu yǒu jǐ diǎn yāo qiú","Tentang proyek akhir semester, profesor punya beberapa syarat.","Regarding the final project, the professor has a few requirements.","Tungkol sa final project, may ilang requirements ang propesor.","campus"],["對於遲到的同學，老師會扣分。","duì yú chí dào de tóng xué lǎo shī huì kòu fēn","Terhadap mahasiswa yang terlambat, dosen akan potong nilai.","For students who are late, the teacher deducts points.","Sa mga estudyanteng nahuhuli, magbabawas ng puntos ang guro.","campus"],["關於這次的異常，請大家看一下報告。","guān yú zhè cì de yì cháng qǐng dà jiā kàn yí xià bào gào","Mengenai abnormal kali ini, silakan semua lihat laporannya.","Regarding this abnormality, please everyone take a look at the report.","Tungkol sa abnormal na ito, pakitingnan ng lahat ang report.","fab"],["對於新人的問題，學長都很有耐心。","duì yú xīn rén de wèn tí xué zhǎng dōu hěn yǒu nài xīn","Terhadap pertanyaan orang baru, senior selalu sabar.","The seniors are always patient with newcomers' questions.","Laging matiyaga ang mga senior sa tanong ng mga bago.","fab"]],"drill":[{"q":"＿這個問題，我們明天開會討論。","opts":["關於","被","比"],"a":0,"why":"Topik di awal kalimat → 關於."},{"q":"這是一本＿半導體製程的書。","opts":["關於","對於","對"],"a":0,"why":"Buku tentang… → 關於…的書."},{"q":"＿客戶的抱怨，公司很重視。","opts":["對於","為了","因為"],"a":0,"why":"Sasaran sikap (menanggapi keluhan) → 對於."},{"q":"他＿這件事的看法跟我不一樣。","opts":["對","比","被"],"a":0,"why":"對…的看法 = pandangan terhadap."}]},{"lv":4,"k":"b1x_tongshi","form":"S + 同時 + V／(在) + V1 + 的同時，(也) + V2／A，同時(也) + 是 B","icon":"clock","name":["Pada saat yang sama / sekaligus (同時)","At the same time (同時／…的同時)","Sabay / kasabay nito (同時)"],"gloss":["同時 = dua hal terjadi pada waktu yang sama, atau satu hal punya dua peran sekaligus. Posisinya seperti adverbia: setelah subjek, sebelum verba (同時處理). Bisa untuk subjek berbeda, mesin, atau hal abstrak — beda dengan 一邊…一邊 yang hanya untuk dua aktivitas sengaja oleh satu orang. Pola yang lebih formal: 在 + V1 + 的同時，也 + V2.","同時 = two things happen at the same time, or one thing has two roles at once. It behaves like an adverb: after the subject, before the verb (同時處理). It works with different subjects, machines or abstract things — unlike 一邊…一邊, which is only for two deliberate activities by one person. More formal pattern: 在 + V1 + 的同時，也 + V2.","同時 = dalawang bagay na nangyayari nang sabay, o isang bagay na may dalawang papel. Parang pang-abay ito: pagkatapos ng paksa, bago ang pandiwa (同時處理). Puwede sa magkaibang paksa, makina o abstraktong bagay — iba sa 一邊…一邊 na para lang sa dalawang gawain ng iisang tao. Mas pormal: 在 + V1 + 的同時，也 + V2."],"tip":["同時 = 'sekaligus'. Tempelkan SEBELUM verba: 同時 + V. Untuk satu orang yang santai melakukan dua aktivitas ('sambil'), pakai 一邊…一邊.","同時 = 'at once'. Stick it BEFORE the verb: 同時 + V. For one person casually doing two activities ('while'), use 一邊…一邊.","同時 = 'sabay'. Ilagay BAGO ang pandiwa: 同時 + V. Para sa isang taong gumagawa ng dalawang gawain ('habang'), gamitin ang 一邊…一邊."],"warn":["✗ 這台機台處理兩片晶圓同時。→ ✓ 這台機台可以同時處理兩片晶圓。","✗ 這台機台處理兩片晶圓同時。→ ✓ 這台機台可以同時處理兩片晶圓。","✗ 這台機台處理兩片晶圓同時。→ ✓ 這台機台可以同時處理兩片晶圓。"],"logic":{"id":"Orang Indonesia bilang 'mesin ini memproses dua wafer sekaligus / secara bersamaan' — keterangan waktunya di akhir kalimat. Penutur Taiwan menaruh 同時 di depan verba, seperti adverbia lain (也, 都, 常常): 同時處理. Untuk menyambung dua klausa, mereka memakai 在…的同時，也…, yang sering terdengar di rapat dan presentasi ('sambil menaikkan output, kualitas juga harus dijaga'). Pola A，同時也是 B dipakai untuk peran ganda: 'dia teman sekelasku, sekaligus teman sekamarku'. Kalau hanya satu orang melakukan dua aktivitas santai, pakai 一邊…一邊.","en":"English can put 'at the same time' at the end of the sentence; Mandarin cannot. Taiwanese speakers place 同時 before the verb like other adverbs (也, 都, 常常): 同時處理. To link two clauses they use 在…的同時，也…, common in meetings and presentations ('while raising output, we must also watch quality'). A，同時也是 B expresses a double role: 'he's my classmate and also my roommate'. For one person casually doing two activities, use 一邊…一邊."},"ex":[["他在讀書的同時，也在超商打工。","tā zài dú shū de tóng shí yě zài chāo shāng dǎ gōng","Selain kuliah, pada saat yang sama dia juga kerja paruh waktu di minimarket.","While studying, he also works part-time at a convenience store.","Habang nag-aaral, nagtatrabaho rin siya nang part-time sa convenience store.","daily"],["我跟室友同時到家。","wǒ gēn shì yǒu tóng shí dào jiā","Aku dan teman sekamarku sampai rumah bersamaan.","My roommate and I got home at the same time.","Sabay kaming dumating sa bahay ng kasama ko sa kuwarto.","daily"],["他是我的同學，同時也是我的室友。","tā shì wǒ de tóng xué tóng shí yě shì wǒ de shì yǒu","Dia teman sekelasku, sekaligus teman sekamarku.","He is my classmate and also my roommate.","Kaklase ko siya, at kasama ko rin sa kuwarto.","campus"],["這個程式可以同時控制三個馬達。","zhè ge chéng shì kě yǐ tóng shí kòng zhì sān ge mǎ dá","Program ini bisa mengontrol tiga motor sekaligus.","This program can control three motors at the same time.","Kayang kontrolin ng program na ito ang tatlong motor nang sabay.","campus"],["按下開關，兩個燈會同時亮。","àn xià kāi guān liǎng ge dēng huì tóng shí liàng","Begitu saklar ditekan, dua lampu menyala bersamaan.","When you press the switch, both lights turn on at the same time.","Pag pinindot ang switch, sabay na sisindi ang dalawang ilaw.","campus"],["這台機台可以同時處理二十五片晶圓。","zhè tái jī tái kě yǐ tóng shí chǔ lǐ èr shí wǔ piàn jīng yuán","Mesin ini bisa memproses 25 wafer sekaligus.","This tool can process 25 wafers at the same time.","Kayang iproseso ng makinang ito ang 25 wafer nang sabay.","fab"],["提高產量的同時，也要注意品質。","tí gāo chǎn liàng de tóng shí yě yào zhù yì pǐn zhí","Sambil menaikkan output, kualitas juga harus diperhatikan.","While increasing output, we also have to watch quality.","Habang tinataasan ang output, kailangang bantayan din ang kalidad.","fab"]],"drill":[{"q":"他是工程師，＿也是老師。","opts":["同時","一邊","以後"],"a":0,"why":"Peran ganda (sekaligus) → 同時也是."},{"q":"這台機台可以＿處理兩片晶圓。","opts":["同時","一邊","越"],"a":0,"why":"Mesin, bukan aktivitas sengaja orang → 同時, sebelum verba."},{"q":"在追求速度的＿，也要顧到安全。","opts":["同時","一邊","時間"],"a":0,"why":"Pola 在…的同時，也…."},{"q":"兩個警報＿響了。","opts":["同時","一邊","越"],"a":0,"why":"Dua hal (bukan aktivitas orang) terjadi bersamaan → 同時."},{"q":"他喜歡一邊洗澡，＿唱歌。","opts":["一邊","同時","也"],"a":0,"why":"Satu orang, dua aktivitas santai → 一邊…一邊 (pasangannya tetap 一邊)."}]},{"lv":4,"k":"b1x_benlai_yuanlai","form":"本來 + rencana/keadaan awal (lalu berubah)／原來 + kenyataan yang baru disadari","icon":"sparkle","name":["Tadinya vs ternyata (本來／原來)","Originally vs so it turns out (本來／原來)","Dati / balak vs iyon pala (本來／原來)"],"gloss":["本來 = awalnya / tadinya: rencana atau keadaan sebelumnya yang kemudian berubah (sering diikuti 後來, 可是, 現在). 原來 = ternyata: baru menyadari kebenaran ('Oh, jadi begitu!'). Untuk arti 'ternyata', hanya 原來 yang benar.","本來 = originally / was going to: an earlier plan or state that later changed (often followed by 後來, 可是, 現在). 原來 = so it turns out: suddenly realising the truth. For 'it turns out', only 原來 works.","本來 = dati / balak: naunang plano o kalagayan na nagbago (madalas may 後來, 可是). 原來 = iyon pala: biglang pagkaunawa sa totoo. Para sa 'iyon pala', 原來 lang."],"tip":["本來… → 後來/可是… (cerita berubah). 原來… = 'Oh, ternyata!' (baru paham).","本來… → 後來/可是… (story changes). 原來… = 'Oh, so that's it!' (realisation).","本來… → 後來/可是… (nagbago). 原來… = 'Ah, iyon pala!'"],"warn":["✗ 本來是你！我還以為是誰。→ ✓ 原來是你！我還以為是誰。","✗ 本來是你！我還以為是誰。→ ✓ 原來是你！我還以為是誰。","✗ 本來是你！我還以為是誰。→ ✓ 原來是你！我還以為是誰。"],"logic":{"id":"Bahasa Indonesia punya 'tadinya' dan 'ternyata' yang jelas berbeda, dan Mandarin juga begitu — masalahnya kamus sering menerjemahkan keduanya sebagai 'semula'. Penutur Taiwan memakai 本來 saat bercerita tentang rencana yang berubah, dan 原來 saat sebuah misteri terpecahkan. Di pabrik, 原來是…，難怪… adalah kombinasi favorit saat menemukan penyebab masalah.","en":"Dictionaries give 'originally' for both, but they differ like 'was going to' vs 'turns out'. Taiwanese use 本來 when telling how a plan changed, and 原來 when a mystery is solved. In fabs, 原來是…，難怪… is a favourite combo when the root cause is found."},"ex":[["我本來想去夜市，後來下雨就沒去了。","wǒ běn lái xiǎng qù yè shì hòu lái xià yǔ jiù méi qù le","Tadinya aku mau ke pasar malam, tapi akhirnya hujan jadi nggak pergi.","I was going to go to the night market, but it rained so I didn't.","Balak kong pumunta sa night market, pero umulan kaya hindi na ako tumuloy.","daily"],["原來你也是印尼人！","yuán lái nǐ yě shì yìn ní rén","Ternyata kamu juga orang Indonesia!","So you're Indonesian too!","Indonesian ka rin pala!","daily"],["這門課本來是星期三，現在改到星期五了。","zhè mén kè běn lái shì xīng qí sān xiàn zài gǎi dào xīng qí wǔ le","Kuliah ini tadinya hari Rabu, sekarang pindah ke Jumat.","This class was originally on Wednesday; now it's moved to Friday.","Dating Miyerkules ang klaseng ito, ngayon ay inilipat sa Biyernes.","campus"],["原來是二極體接反了，難怪燈不亮。","yuán lái shì èr jí tǐ jiē fǎn le nán guài dēng bú liàng","Ternyata diodanya terpasang terbalik, pantas lampunya nggak nyala.","So the diode was connected backwards; no wonder the light didn't turn on.","Baligtad pala ang kabit ng diode, kaya pala hindi sumisindi ang ilaw.","campus"],["我本來排白班，因為人手不夠，改成夜班了。","wǒ běn lái pái bái bān yīn wèi rén shǒu bú gòu gǎi chéng yè bān le","Tadinya aku dijadwalkan shift pagi, karena kurang orang jadi dipindah ke shift malam.","I was originally scheduled for day shift, but they were short-handed, so I was switched to nights.","Dati akong naka-day shift, pero kulang sa tao kaya inilipat ako sa night shift.","fab"],["原來機台當機是因為感測器髒了。","yuán lái jī tái dāng jī shì yīn wèi gǎn cè qì zāng le","Ternyata mesinnya hang karena sensornya kotor.","Turns out the tool crashed because the sensor was dirty.","Nag-hang pala ang makina dahil marumi ang sensor.","fab"]],"drill":[{"q":"我＿想搭捷運，後來決定騎機車。","opts":["本來","原來","終於"],"a":0,"why":"Rencana awal yang berubah → 本來."},{"q":"＿你在這裡！我找你好久了。","opts":["原來","本來","其實"],"a":0,"why":"Baru sadar → 原來."},{"q":"他＿不是工程師，後來才轉行的。","opts":["本來","難怪","終於"],"a":0,"why":"Keadaan awal → 本來."},{"q":"＿是保險絲燒了，換一個就好了。","opts":["原來","本來","最好"],"a":0,"why":"Menemukan penyebab → 原來."}]},{"lv":4,"k":"b1x_zhongyu_zongsuan","form":"(setelah lama/berusaha) + S + 終於／總算 + V + 了","icon":"check","name":["Akhirnya (終於／總算)","Finally / at last (終於／總算)","Sa wakas (終於／總算)"],"gloss":["終於 = akhirnya, setelah lama menunggu atau berusaha. 總算 = lebih lisan, dengan nuansa lega ('akhirnya juga…, syukurlah'). Keduanya ditaruh setelah subjek, sebelum verba, dan kalimatnya biasanya diakhiri 了.","終於 = finally, after a long wait or effort. 總算 is more colloquial, with a sense of relief ('at last, thank goodness'). Both go after the subject, before the verb, and the sentence usually ends with 了.","終於 = sa wakas, pagkatapos ng mahabang paghihintay o pagsisikap. Mas kolokyal ang 總算, may ginhawa. Pareho silang pagkatapos ng paksa, bago ang pandiwa, at karaniwang may 了."],"tip":["最後 = urutan paling akhir (langkah terakhir). 終於 = akhirnya setelah perjuangan. 總算 = akhirnya, lega!","最後 = the last in order. 終於 = finally after a struggle. 總算 = finally, phew!","最後 = huli sa pagkakasunod. 終於 = sa wakas matapos ang hirap. 總算 = sa wakas, hay salamat!"],"warn":["✗ 我終於去台北。→ ✓ 我終於去台北了。","✗ 我終於去台北。→ ✓ 我終於去台北了。","✗ 我終於去台北。→ ✓ 我終於去台北了。"],"logic":{"id":"Kata 'akhirnya' dalam bahasa Indonesia dipakai untuk urutan ('akhirnya kami pulang') maupun perasaan lega setelah menunggu. Mandarin memisahkan: 最後 untuk urutan langkah, 終於/總算 untuk hasil yang ditunggu-tunggu. Karena 終於 selalu tentang perubahan yang baru tercapai, penutur Taiwan hampir selalu menutupnya dengan 了. 總算 terdengar lebih emosional dan sering dipakai setelah kerja keras bersama tim.","en":"Indonesian 'akhirnya' covers both sequence and relief. Mandarin splits them: 最後 for the last step, 終於/總算 for a long-awaited outcome. Since 終於 marks a newly reached change, Taiwanese almost always end with 了. 總算 sounds more emotional, often after hard teamwork."},"ex":[["等了半個小時，公車終於來了。","děng le bàn ge xiǎo shí gōng chē zhōng yú lái le","Setelah nunggu setengah jam, busnya akhirnya datang.","After waiting half an hour, the bus finally came.","Pagkatapos maghintay ng kalahating oras, dumating din sa wakas ang bus.","daily"],["下了一個星期的雨，今天總算出太陽了。","xià le yí ge xīng qí de yǔ jīn tiān zǒng suàn chū tài yáng le","Setelah hujan seminggu, hari ini akhirnya cerah juga.","After a week of rain, the sun is finally out today.","Matapos ang isang linggong ulan, sumikat din sa wakas ang araw ngayon.","daily"],["我終於考過中文檢定了！","wǒ zhōng yú kǎo guò zhōng wén jiǎn dìng le","Aku akhirnya lulus ujian kemampuan Mandarin!","I finally passed the Chinese proficiency test!","Sa wakas pumasa ako sa Chinese proficiency test!","campus"],["改了三次，電路總算可以動了。","gǎi le sān cì diàn lù zǒng suàn kě yǐ dòng le","Setelah diubah tiga kali, rangkaiannya akhirnya jalan juga.","After three revisions, the circuit finally works.","Pagkatapos ng tatlong pagbabago, gumana rin sa wakas ang circuit.","campus"],["修了一整晚，機台終於恢復正常了。","xiū le yì zhěng wǎn jī tái zhōng yú huī fù zhèng cháng le","Setelah diperbaiki semalaman, mesinnya akhirnya normal lagi.","After repairing it all night, the tool is finally back to normal.","Pagkatapos ayusin buong gabi, bumalik din sa normal ang makina.","fab"],["這批貨總算準時出貨了，大家辛苦了。","zhè pī huò zǒng suàn zhǔn shí chū huò le dà jiā xīn kǔ le","Lot ini akhirnya terkirim tepat waktu, terima kasih kerja kerasnya semua.","This batch finally shipped on time — thanks for the hard work, everyone.","Sa wakas na-ship nang on time ang batch na ito, salamat sa pagod ninyo.","fab"]],"drill":[{"q":"找了好久，我＿找到鑰匙了。","opts":["終於","本來","原來"],"a":0,"why":"Setelah lama mencari → 終於."},{"q":"期末考考完了，＿可以放假了！","opts":["總算","最好","其實"],"a":0,"why":"Lega → 總算."},{"q":"機台修好了，產線終於恢復生產＿。","opts":["了","過","著"],"a":0,"why":"終於…了."},{"q":"他排隊排了兩個小時，＿買到了。","opts":["終於","最好","同時"],"a":0,"why":"Setelah menunggu lama → 終於."}]},{"lv":4,"k":"b1x_qishi_fanzheng_nanguai","form":"其實 + fakta sebenarnya／反正 + kesimpulan／難怪 + akibat yang kini masuk akal","icon":"chat","name":["Sebenarnya / toh / pantesan (其實／反正／難怪)","Actually / anyway / no wonder (其實／反正／難怪)","Ang totoo / tutal / kaya pala (其實／反正／難怪)"],"gloss":["Tiga adverbia lisan yang membuat bicaramu terdengar natural. 其實 = sebenarnya (mengoreksi anggapan atau mengungkap fakta). 反正 = toh / bagaimanapun (apa pun alasannya, kesimpulannya sama). 難怪 = pantesan (setelah tahu alasannya, hasilnya jadi masuk akal). Biasanya di awal klausa.","Three spoken adverbs that make you sound natural. 其實 = actually (corrects an assumption or reveals a fact). 反正 = anyway (whatever the reason, the conclusion is the same). 難怪 = no wonder (now that you know why, the result makes sense). Usually at the start of the clause.","Tatlong pasalitang pang-abay. 其實 = ang totoo. 反正 = tutal / anyway. 難怪 = kaya pala. Karaniwang nasa simula ng sugnay."],"tip":["其實 = 'sebenernya sih…'. 反正 = 'toh…'. 難怪 = 'pantesan!' (alasan dulu, 難怪 belakangan).","其實 = 'actually…'. 反正 = 'anyway…'. 難怪 = 'no wonder!' (reason first, 難怪 after).","其實 = 'ang totoo…'. 反正 = 'tutal…'. 難怪 = 'kaya pala!' (dahilan muna)."],"warn":["✗ 他是新人，所以難怪他不知道。→ ✓ 他是新人，難怪他不知道。","✗ 他是新人，所以難怪他不知道。→ ✓ 他是新人，難怪他不知道。","✗ 他是新人，所以難怪他不知道。→ ✓ 他是新人，難怪他不知道。"],"logic":{"id":"Kata-kata seperti 'sebenernya', 'toh', dan 'pantesan' sangat sering muncul dalam obrolan Indonesia, dan penutur Taiwan memakai padanannya dengan frekuensi yang sama. 難怪 sudah mengandung makna 'jadi/karena itu', sehingga tidak perlu 所以. 反正 dipakai untuk menutup diskusi ('ya sudah, toh sama saja'), sedangkan 其實 untuk membuka fakta yang berbeda dari kesan pertama. Menguasai tiga kata ini membuat Mandarinmu terdengar jauh lebih hidup.","en":"Taiwanese use these three as often as English speakers say 'actually', 'anyway' and 'no wonder'. 難怪 already contains 'so', so don't add 所以. 反正 closes a discussion ('it's the same anyway'), while 其實 opens a fact that differs from first impressions. Mastering them makes your Mandarin sound alive."},"ex":[["這件衣服看起來很貴，其實才三百塊。","zhè jiàn yī fú kàn qǐ lái hěn guì qí shí cái sān bǎi kuài","Baju ini kelihatan mahal, padahal cuma tiga ratus.","This shirt looks expensive, but it's actually only 300.","Mukhang mahal ang damit na ito, pero 300 lang pala talaga.","daily"],["你不用急，反正電影九點才開始。","nǐ bú yòng jí fǎn zhèng diàn yǐng jiǔ diǎn cái kāi shǐ","Nggak usah buru-buru, toh filmnya baru mulai jam sembilan.","No need to rush; the movie doesn't start until nine anyway.","Huwag kang magmadali, tutal alas-nuwebe pa magsisimula ang pelikula.","daily"],["你昨天熬夜讀書？難怪上課一直打瞌睡。","nǐ zuó tiān áo yè dú shū nán guài shàng kè yì zhí dǎ kē shuì","Kamu begadang belajar kemarin? Pantesan di kelas ngantuk terus.","You stayed up studying last night? No wonder you kept nodding off in class.","Nagpuyat ka kahapon sa pag-aaral? Kaya pala antok ka sa klase.","campus"],["這個題目其實沒有很難，只是步驟比較多。","zhè ge tí mù qí shí méi yǒu hěn nán zhǐ shì bù zòu bǐ jiào duō","Soal ini sebenarnya nggak terlalu susah, cuma langkahnya banyak.","This problem actually isn't that hard; it just has more steps.","Ang totoo, hindi naman mahirap ang tanong na ito, marami lang ang hakbang.","campus"],["反正今天要做保養，就順便把濾網也換了吧。","fǎn zhèng jīn tiān yào zuò bǎo yǎng jiù shùn biàn bǎ lǜ wǎng yě huàn le ba","Toh hari ini ada maintenance, sekalian ganti filternya aja.","We're doing maintenance today anyway, so let's swap the filter too.","Tutal may maintenance ngayon, palitan na rin natin ang filter.","fab"],["原來真空度不夠，難怪蝕刻的結果不穩定。","yuán lái zhēn kōng dù bú gòu nán guài shí kè de jié guǒ bù wěn dìng","Ternyata vakumnya kurang, pantesan hasil etching nggak stabil.","So the vacuum level was insufficient — no wonder the etch results were unstable.","Kulang pala ang vacuum, kaya pala hindi stable ang resulta ng etching.","fab"]],"drill":[{"q":"他看起來很兇，＿人很好。","opts":["其實","反正","難怪"],"a":0,"why":"Fakta berbeda dari kesan → 其實."},{"q":"＿我也沒事，我陪你去吧。","opts":["反正","難怪","其實"],"a":0,"why":"'Toh aku juga nganggur' → 反正."},{"q":"他每天練習，＿中文說得那麼好。","opts":["難怪","反正","其實"],"a":0,"why":"Setelah tahu alasannya → 難怪."},{"q":"機台沒接地？＿一直有雜訊。","opts":["難怪","其實","反正"],"a":0,"why":"Alasan ditemukan → 難怪."}]},{"lv":5,"k":"b1x_renzhi","form":"kata tanya (什麼／誰／哪裡／怎麼…) + 都／也 + (不／沒) + V","icon":"question","name":["Kata tanya = 'apa pun / siapa pun' (什麼都／誰都／哪裡都)","Question words as 'any/every' (什麼都／誰都／哪裡都)","Pananong bilang 'kahit ano' (什麼都／誰都／哪裡都)"],"gloss":["Kata tanya dipakai bukan untuk bertanya, tapi berarti 'semua / apa saja / siapa pun'. Positif: 什麼都吃 = makan apa saja. Negatif: 什麼都不吃 = tidak makan apa pun. Kata tanya (atau objek) dipindah ke depan, sebelum 都/也 dan verba. Polanya mirip dengan 一 + M + 都不/沒.","Question words used not to ask but to mean 'everything / anything / anyone'. Positive: 什麼都吃 = eat anything. Negative: 什麼都不吃 = eat nothing. The question word (or object) moves before 都/也 and the verb. Similar to 一 + M + 都不/沒.","Ginagamit ang pananong hindi para magtanong, kundi bilang 'lahat / kahit ano / kahit sino'. 什麼都吃 = kumakain ng kahit ano. 什麼都不吃 = walang kinakain. Inililipat ang pananong bago ang 都/也 at pandiwa."],"tip":["Kata tanya + 都 = 'semua'. Kata tanya + 都不/也沒 = 'sama sekali tidak'. Selalu: [kata tanya] → 都 → [verba].","Question word + 都 = 'all'. Question word + 都不/也沒 = 'none at all'. Always: [question word] → 都 → [verb].","Pananong + 都 = 'lahat'. Pananong + 都不/也沒 = 'wala talaga'. Laging: [pananong] → 都 → [pandiwa]."],"warn":["✗ 我不吃什麼都。→ ✓ 我什麼都不吃。","✗ 我不吃什麼都。→ ✓ 我什麼都不吃。","✗ 我不吃什麼都。→ ✓ 我什麼都不吃。"],"logic":{"id":"Orang Indonesia bilang 'Aku nggak mau makan apa-apa' — negasi dulu, 'apa-apa' di akhir. Penutur Taiwan justru memindahkan 'apa pun' ke depan: 什麼 → 都 → 不 → 吃, artinya 'apa pun itu, semuanya tidak kumakan'. Kata 都/也 berfungsi seperti 'semuanya tercakup'. Begitu kamu terbiasa urutan ini, kamu juga bisa membuat 誰都知道, 哪裡都不想去, 怎麼試都不行.","en":"English says 'I don't eat anything' with 'anything' at the end. Taiwanese move it forward: 什麼 → 都 → 不 → 吃, i.e. 'whatever it is, I don't eat any of it'. 都/也 means 'all covered'. Once used to this order you can say 誰都知道, 哪裡都不想去, 怎麼試都不行."},"ex":[["我太累了，哪裡都不想去。","wǒ tài lèi le nǎ lǐ dōu bù xiǎng qù","Aku capek banget, nggak mau ke mana-mana.","I'm too tired; I don't want to go anywhere.","Pagod na pagod ako, ayokong pumunta kahit saan.","daily"],["我不挑食，什麼都吃。","wǒ bù tiāo shí shén me dōu chī","Aku nggak pilih-pilih makanan, apa aja dimakan.","I'm not picky; I eat everything.","Hindi ako mapili, kinakain ko ang kahit ano.","daily"],["這間實驗室誰都可以用，可是要先登記。","zhè jiān shí yàn shì shéi dōu kě yǐ yòng kě shì yào xiān dēng jì","Lab ini siapa pun boleh pakai, tapi harus daftar dulu.","Anyone can use this lab, but you have to sign up first.","Kahit sino ay puwedeng gumamit ng lab na ito, pero kailangang magparehistro muna.","campus"],["這個問題誰都不會，連助教也不會。","zhè ge wèn tí shéi dōu bú huì lián zhù jiào yě bú huì","Soal ini nggak ada yang bisa, bahkan asisten dosen juga nggak bisa.","No one can solve this problem, not even the TA.","Walang nakakasagot sa tanong na ito, kahit ang TA.","campus"],["機台怎麼重開都開不起來。","jī tái zěn me chóng kāi dōu kāi bù qǐ lái","Mesinnya mau di-restart gimana pun tetap nggak mau nyala.","No matter how we restart the tool, it won't come up.","Kahit paano i-restart ang makina, ayaw pa ring bumukas.","fab"],["進無塵室的時候，什麼東西都不能亂帶。","jìn wú chén shì de shí hòu shén me dōng xī dōu bù néng luàn dài","Waktu masuk cleanroom, barang apa pun nggak boleh dibawa sembarangan.","When entering the cleanroom, you can't just bring anything in.","Pagpasok sa cleanroom, bawal magdala ng kahit anong gamit nang basta-basta.","fab"]],"drill":[{"q":"我現在＿都不想吃。","opts":["什麼","怎麼","為什麼"],"a":0,"why":"'Apa pun' → 什麼都不…."},{"q":"這個週末我哪裡＿不去，在家休息。","opts":["都","就","才"],"a":0,"why":"Kata tanya + 都 + 不."},{"q":"＿都不知道他去哪裡了。","opts":["誰","哪","幾"],"a":0,"why":"'Tidak ada yang tahu' → 誰都不知道."},{"q":"他怎麼修＿修不好。","opts":["都","才","就"],"a":0,"why":"怎麼 + V + 都 + 不/V不…."}]},{"lv":5,"k":"b1x_fanwen","form":"不是 + … + 嗎？／難道 + … + 嗎？（pertanyaan retoris）","icon":"question","name":["Pertanyaan retoris: bukannya…? / masa sih…? (不是…嗎／難道…嗎)","Rhetorical questions: isn't it…? / surely not…? (不是…嗎／難道…嗎)","Retorikal na tanong: hindi ba…? / talaga bang…? (不是…嗎／難道…嗎)"],"gloss":["Bukan pertanyaan sungguhan, tapi cara menegaskan atau menunjukkan heran. 不是…嗎？ = 'bukannya…?' (mengingatkan atau menegaskan sesuatu yang dianggap sudah jelas). 難道…嗎？ = 'masa sih…?' (lebih kuat, kaget atau tidak percaya). Makna sebenarnya berlawanan dengan bentuknya: 難道你不知道嗎？ = kamu pasti tahu.","Not real questions but ways to emphasise or show surprise. 不是…嗎？ = 'isn't it…? / didn't you…?' (reminding or stressing something obvious). 難道…嗎？ = 'surely you don't…? / don't tell me…' (stronger, shock or disbelief). The real meaning is the opposite of the form: 難道你不知道嗎？ = you must know.","Hindi totoong tanong kundi paraan ng pagdiin o pagkagulat. 不是…嗎？ = 'hindi ba…?'. 難道…嗎？ = 'talaga bang…?' (mas malakas). Kabaligtaran ng anyo ang tunay na kahulugan."],"tip":["不是你說的嗎？ = 'Kamu sendiri yang bilang, kan!' 難道你不知道嗎？ = 'Masa kamu nggak tahu?' (pasti tahu).","不是你說的嗎？ = 'You said it yourself!' 難道你不知道嗎？ = 'Don't tell me you don't know!' (you must).","不是你說的嗎？ = 'Ikaw mismo ang nagsabi!' 難道你不知道嗎？ = 'Hindi mo ba talaga alam?'"],"warn":["✗ 你沒有說明天考試嗎？(maksud: bukannya kamu bilang…) → ✓ 你不是說明天考試嗎？","✗ 你沒有說明天考試嗎？(meaning 'didn't you say…') → ✓ 你不是說明天考試嗎？","✗ 你沒有說明天考試嗎？(ibig sabihin 'hindi ba sinabi mo…') → ✓ 你不是說明天考試嗎？"],"logic":{"id":"Orang Indonesia bilang 'Bukannya kamu bilang besok ujian?' dan kadang menerjemahkannya dengan 沒有, yang malah menjadi pertanyaan biasa ('Kamu tidak bilang?'). Penutur Taiwan memakai 不是…嗎 sebagai 'pengingat yang agak menuntut', dan 難道…嗎 saat benar-benar heran. Nada suara naik di akhir dan sering diikuti kalimat lanjutan seperti 怎麼還…？ Pakai dengan hati-hati ke atasan karena bisa terdengar menyalahkan.","en":"English 'Didn't you say…?' tempts learners to use 沒有, which becomes a plain question. Taiwanese use 不是…嗎 as a pointed reminder and 難道…嗎 for real disbelief, often followed by 怎麼還…？ Use carefully with superiors, as it can sound accusatory."},"ex":[["你不是說今天要請客嗎？","nǐ bú shì shuō jīn tiān yào qǐng kè ma","Bukannya kamu bilang hari ini mau traktir?","Didn't you say you'd treat us today?","Hindi ba sabi mo manlilibre ka ngayon?","daily"],["難道你連捷運站在哪裡都不知道嗎？","nán dào nǐ lián jié yùn zhàn zài nǎ lǐ dōu bù zhī dào ma","Masa kamu nggak tahu stasiun MRT di mana?","Don't tell me you don't even know where the MRT station is?","Talaga bang hindi mo alam kung nasaan ang MRT station?","daily"],["這個公式上禮拜不是教過了嗎？","zhè ge gōng shì shàng lǐ bài bú shì jiāo guò le ma","Rumus ini bukannya sudah diajarkan minggu lalu?","Wasn't this formula taught last week?","Hindi ba itinuro na ang formula na ito noong isang linggo?","campus"],["難道電源沒插就開始量了嗎？","nán dào diàn yuán méi chā jiù kāi shǐ liáng le ma","Masa kamu mulai ukur tanpa colok power dulu?","Surely you didn't start measuring without plugging in the power?","Talaga bang nagsimula kang sumukat nang hindi nakasaksak ang power?","campus"],["不是說好四點交接嗎？怎麼還沒來？","bú shì shuō hǎo sì diǎn jiāo jiē ma zěn me hái méi lái","Bukannya sudah janji serah terima jam empat? Kok belum datang?","Didn't we agree on a four o'clock handover? Why aren't they here yet?","Hindi ba napagkasunduan ang handover nang alas-kuwatro? Bakit wala pa?","fab"],["難道這個異常沒人發現嗎？","nán dào zhè ge yì cháng méi rén fā xiàn ma","Masa abnormal ini nggak ada yang sadar?","Are you telling me nobody noticed this abnormality?","Talaga bang walang nakapansin sa abnormal na ito?","fab"]],"drill":[{"q":"你＿已經吃過了嗎？怎麼還在吃？","opts":["不是","不要","不但"],"a":0,"why":"Mengingatkan hal yang dianggap jelas → 不是…嗎."},{"q":"＿你不知道今天要考試嗎？","opts":["難道","雖然","如果"],"a":0,"why":"Heran/tidak percaya → 難道…嗎."},{"q":"不是說好一起去＿？","opts":["嗎","吧","呢"],"a":0,"why":"不是…嗎？"},{"q":"難道你忘了要戴手套＿？","opts":["嗎","吧","了"],"a":0,"why":"難道…嗎？"}]}];